| Booked revenue | The rental charge before tax, after discounts, for bookings confirmed in the period. A cancelled booking counts only what was kept; refunds come off. |

## Sales staff: in person or remote

Each Sales person works in person (Toronto) or remote (anywhere, a contractor). Staff and roles lists them under Sales staff: in person or remote.

1. Press **Work mode** on a person (or on their Sales page), choose In person or Remote and give the reason. A new Sales person starts in person.
2. The list shows the mode, the rate now, the rate the month would end at, and for remote this month''s touches against 400, the peak hours scheduled this week (20 needed, Thursday to Sunday afternoons) and the replies on time.
3. On a remote person''s Sales page, Remote duties shows their checklist, touches, blocks and reply time. **Void** beside a touch logged by mistake takes it off, with a reason.
4. When you approve a Sales month, its mode, rates, touches and any drop are locked: a later change of mode or settings does not change it. Their My sales shows each month in one line.

|  | Rule |
| --- | --- |
| Rates | In person 10%, 15% from 50 rental days, 20% from 100. Remote 5 points lower on every tier: 5%, 10%, 15% |
| Credit | In person: walk-ins, handovers, partner visits and the rentals they source. Remote: only the rentals they source; a website request they answer with the first offer during their blocks is credited to them; a walk-in or a partner deal earns them nothing |
| Remote minimum | 400 touches a month. Under it, when the month ends, the month''s rate is one tier lower (5% becomes 2.5%). Settings > Program settings, Staff commissions, changes the minimum, the drop and the floor |

## An Admin has every staff page

An Admin account is only an Admin: it already has every page of the staff portals, so no office or field role can be added to it, and the invite form and Staff and roles refuse it. To work as staff, use a separate account. An Admin can still be given a field job and opens it on the field portal.
## Two records of one person

When two renter records are clearly the same person (the same phone verified with a code, or the same name, date of birth and phone), the site merges them by itself within 15 minutes, into the record with more bookings. Bookings, licences, cards, payments, documents and messages move. The person can then sign in with either email or with their phone number and a code, and gets one short note: "Your CarmaCars accounts are now one". A match on the name alone stays a task for you, and **Merge into this record** under the renter still works as before.

1. Open the renter. The Merged records card lists each merge, automatic or by staff, with what moved and the emails that now sign in there.
2. Two different people after all? Press **Undo** and say why. Everything moved goes back and both records are as they were.

## New staff: the academy, then the agreement, then the portal

Every staff member (never an Admin) opens their portal in this order: their staff agreement first, then the academy, then everything else (release 48: the agreement moved before the academy; anyone who already passed the academy is only asked to sign). Until the agreement is signed they open only **Welcome**, their profile, the guide and their documents to sign; after it, until the academy is passed, only the academy, the guide, their profile and Welcome.

1. The agreement is sent by itself to everyone without one, filled from their record and their hire''s pay and start date: the Field Staff Agreement for field work, the contractor agreement for customer service, Fleet, Finance and Sales (in person or remote). One reminder goes 3 days after it was sent.
2. **Team** > **Staff and roles**, **Staff agreements**: who has not signed, what the automatic send waits for (for example a field hire''s licence number), and **Waive** with the reason.
3. Welcome also asks for the name they go by (the preferred name, shown across the portals and on the staff list), and, once the agreement and the academy are done, shows the team''s WhatsApp group (Program settings, **WhatsApp team group link** and **WhatsApp Sales group link**; empty until you set them: while either is empty, Hiring warns and To do keeps an urgent task. Reset the invite link in WhatsApp, keep Add other members for admins only and Approve new participants on, then paste it). Each group shows the person''s member tag ("Name - Position") with Copy and the steps; I joined needs **I set my member tag**. The same link goes by email, once.

## Accounts locked for inactivity

A staff account with no sign-in or use for 10 days (Program settings, **Staff inactive lock days**) is locked; the person is warned by email on day 7 and sees "Account locked for inactivity" when they sign in. You get an alert. On **Team** > **Staff and roles** the row says **Locked for inactivity**: press **Unlock**. The staff list shows each person''s last sign-in. Admin accounts are never locked.

## Hours and the townhall

**Team** > **Timesheet**: the hours customer service, Fleet and Finance clocked (Clock in and out on their home page). Add hours someone forgot, or void a wrong entry, with the reason. A person not clocked in 15 minutes after their start time (customer service 9:00, Fleet 11:00, Toronto) is reminded.

**Breaks and idle time (release 35).** Customer service, Fleet and Finance press **Start break** and **End break** next to the clock; breaks have no fixed length. On **Timesheet**, each person''s days show the hours clocked and worked, their breaks (how many, the total and the longest) and their idle time, with every break and idle stretch listed. **Edit** or **Remove** a break with the reason (in the audit log). Finance sees the breaks but never the idle time. A break open past 30 minutes reminds the person and you. Whether breaks are paid is **Program settings** > va_breaks_paid (on: salaried; off: breaks come off the hours on the payroll, where each line shows the period''s breaks).

While someone is clocked in, not on a break and within their scheduled hours, the portal notes the fact of their activity (never keys, pages or screens), at most once a minute; their actions count too. With no activity for more than va_idle_alert_minutes (10), you get one alert, "Name (role) inactive since 10:42, 12 min", and one more at va_idle_followup_minutes (30). A call they are on (their Quo user, set with **Set Quo user** on Timesheet; the **Call** button; a note in the caller pop-up) and the townhall (joined or present, to its end plus 10 minutes) pause it. **KPIs** shows **Idle minutes** against kpi_idle_minutes_week.

**Team** > **Townhall**: the weekly staff call (Wednesdays at 6:30 pm Toronto). The deck builds itself every Sunday night from the week''s data: the week, platform updates, fleet, staff, sales with the leaderboard, finances and claims (the last two for Admins only). Add a note to any slide; **Build again** refreshes the numbers. With no call link in Program settings, **Join the call** opens the call in the site; staff add the call to their calendar from the page.

## The townhall day, attendance and the team slide (release 35)

1. The townhall is every Wednesday at 6:30 pm Toronto time. To change it, press **Change the day or time** on the Townhall page. Beside it, a table shows the website''s visitor sessions of the last 8 weeks for each day, as information. Field applicants'' live calls always take the hour before.
2. Every staff member is invited and reminded an hour before. **Join the call** on the townhall page, or **Check in** from 15 minutes before, counts them as there.
3. When the call ends, the people who missed it are recorded, the staff list shows "Missed N townhalls" for the last 8 weeks, and you get an alert with the names.
4. The deck''s last slide is the team: a tile per person with their role''s numbers for the week. Press **Add a shout-out** on a tile to add yours.

## Where staff live (release 35)

Welcome asks every hire for their city and country. In the Toronto area Sales keep the mode they were hired in; elsewhere Sales is remote. The staff list shows the location.

## Staff onboarding, breaks and shifts (release 35)

- New staff open their portal after four steps in order: the staff agreement, the academy, confirming the team''s WhatsApp groups, then an Admin''s or a Fleet team member''s approval (or a rejection with a reason the person sees). Everyone already working waits for the same approval once.
- Each person''s row on the Staff onboarding card in Settings and on the Fleet approvals list says exactly what is missing, for example "Waiting on: Academy (3 of 11 sections), Staff agreement signature". **Mark WhatsApp joined** records only the WhatsApp groups, at any step: it never passes the academy or signs the agreement, and it counts when the person reaches that step. Once the agreement and the academy are done, **Confirm WhatsApp and approve** marks the groups and approves in one press (Admins only, recorded in the audit log).
- Schedules: customer service, Fleet and Finance have a schedule per role, and an Admin can give one person their own. Today''s duty board shows who is working, late or absent.
- Breaks: office staff log a break from their home page, and the time on break is kept on their timesheet. While someone is on a break, on a call or in the townhall, the idle alert is paused; otherwise a person with no activity for a while on a shift gets an alert, then the Admins do.
- Quiet hours: staff alerts held by a person''s quiet hours arrive as one summary when they end, and no text goes to a renter at night (an answer asked for then arrives in the morning).
- Field staff set their availability (mornings, afternoons and evenings for each weekday) on Welcome and later on My shifts or Profile; Fleet and Admin see it on the shift board.
- Standing weekly shifts are claimed by themselves up to two weeks ahead; the minimum shifts a week is a Program setting (2 in 7 days), and anyone under it gets a reminder and a To do.
- Shifts are published by themselves every hour from the shift template in Program settings (Field jobs and handovers: one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 for one person, every second day, up to 14 days ahead, only forward from the latest shift already published and never before the start date set there). A handover or return no shift covers gets a shift of its own, 90 minutes either side.
- A published shift nobody has claimed 48 hours before it starts alerts Fleet and the Admins with the people to ask.
- Payroll runs every two weeks: Finance prepares it, an Admin approves it and records the payments. KPIs per role are on Team, KPIs, each against a target in Program settings.
- The townhall is every Wednesday at 6:30 pm Toronto time; two missed in a row lock the account until an Admin restores it. A townhall that did not happen (nobody attended, cancelled ahead, or marked by an Admin) counts nobody absent.

## Work chats only

All staff work communication happens in the group work chats (the CarmaCars Team and Sales WhatsApp groups, and the chats in the portal), never in private messages. It is in every staff guide and in the academy (Work chats). Answer a private work message in the group.

## Staff rewards (release 48)

1. **People** > **Team** > **Staff rewards** lists every staff member: whether they get rental perks and why not, their tier, their progress, their free days and what they used.
2. Rental perks are for in-person staff in Canada. Remote and international staff get none. Use **Perks** to switch one person on or off by hand, with the reason they read.
3. From day one (the academy and the agreement done): 15% off their own rentals. Sales earn 1 free day per 100 rental days booked, Field 1 per 100 handovers. Silver at 50 rental days booked in a month is 20% off; Gold at 100 is 25% off and 1 bonus free day. The month''s top seller gets a free weekend.
4. A perk rental is picked up within 48 hours of booking and never on dates a renter asked for, never on exotic or partner cars, and the staff member must be the driver. A free day ends after 6 months. A suspended account''s perks are frozen.
5. Free days go on CarmaCars'' and shareholders'' cars first. On a co-host owner''s car the owner is paid as at the full rate. Each perk used is posted as a staff benefit expense (account 5300).
6. **Add free days** gives a person free days by hand, with the reason. Every number is in **Settings** > **Program settings** > **Staff rewards**.
## Data to check on each record (release 48)

Every portal checks the person''s own record and shows them a box with the fix: Settings > Staff, Owners and Renters (renters with a booking in the last 90 days) list everyone with something open, in words. **Send reminder** sends a staff member an alert; an owner or a renter sees the box again at their next page, even a warning they put off. A blocking item (the staff agreement waiting for the licence number or the home address, an expired licence of someone who drives) cannot be put off. In-person staff with a home address outside Ontario are asked to confirm it with the reason; what they wrote is kept.

## Updated agreements to accept (release 48)

When a document changes (the terms of use, the privacy policy, the rental agreement, the owner program agreement, the staff agreements), everyone it binds sees one box at their next sign-in: what changed in a few lines, the new text, and **Accept and continue**. Accepting is recorded with the version, the time, the IP address and the device; nobody signs again. Declining keeps their portal closed and shows how to reach us. Admin settings, Terms, lists each version with how many accepted, declined or still wait, and who.

Release 48 published three: the rental agreement (the new return charges), the owner program agreement (owner use for someone else, the $150 Install Fee) and the staff agreements (confidentiality, non-solicitation for 12 months, data returned or deleted on exit, and a non-compete for contractors only: none for employees, as Ontario''s Employment Standards Act requires).

## People on the live map

The live map (Visitors, and Cars > Fleet tracking) has a **People** layer: staff on shift or on a job, and renters and owners at a pickup or return, each with a marker by role. Use the role chips to show or hide each group. Staff appear only after they accept the electronic monitoring policy, and never off duty; renters and owners only with their phone''s permission and only two hours either side of a pickup or return. Only the latest position is kept, plus a job''s points for 30 days. Admins and Fleet see everyone; customer service and Sales see renters at a pickup or return; Finance and field staff see no one.

## Resignations (release 50)

Staff resign themselves on their **Profile** (**Resign**, the last section; on **Welcome** while still in onboarding). You get an email and an alert, Finance too, and an Offboarding To do opens in the Admin queue.

**People** > **Staff and roles** shows **Resigning: last day** with the day notice was given, the reason and the **Offboarding To do** link. After the last day it shows Resigned, with the dates.

1. The To do lists what to do: final pay up to the last day (Finance), the keys, cards and equipment to collect (not tracked in the system), their open field jobs and shifts to reassign, and the leads, chats, To dos and claims to hand back.
2. Their field jobs and shifts after the last day go back to the queue at once; nobody can give them a shift or a job after it.
3. **Change last day** moves it earlier or later (from today); they are emailed the new day and the To do follows. **Withdraw resignation** cancels it for them. **End access now** ends it at once.
4. After the last day their access ends by itself (the same as **End access**), their open To dos and chats go back to the queues and their claims are released. **Restore** gives access back if they return.
5. Someone who resigned by email or in person: **Record a resignation** on their row, with the last day and the reason as they gave it. Today ends their access now.
6. The connector''s `list_staff` shows each person''s resignation.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Let people in, help them back in when they are locked out, and see exactly what they see. Every step is recorded in the audit log.</p><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-portals-and-sign-in" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Portals and sign-in</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Portals and view as</b>. Every portal has a card.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each card links to <b class="gd-ui">Its sign-in page</b>, the address to send that person.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose a person in the list on the card.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Open as this person</b> to see that portal as they see it.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The site&#39;s own test accounts (verify- addresses and Resend&#39;s test inboxes) are marked &quot;Test account&quot; in People who can sign in. They sign in like anyone, but no real work is ever given to them (see Data health).</div></aside><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/portals</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/820"><img src="/guides/img/admin-27-portals-desktop-0361bf61.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="820"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:65.9%;top:30.2%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:58.1%;top:39.4%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:51.6%;top:45.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-invite-a-person" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Invite a person</h2><p class="gd-p">Invitations work for staff, field staff, owners and investors. The person gets our invitation email and chooses a password.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Under Invite a person, choose the Role: Staff (assistant), Field staff, Owner on file or Investor on file. Admin is not offered: only rent@carmacars.ca can be an Admin.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Fill in the Name and Email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">For staff, pick the Main function, and tick Also covers for any other function they help with. For field staff, pick the Field function.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Invite</b>. The link in the email works for 24 hours.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/portals</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/360"><img src="/guides/img/admin-27-portals-desktop-c10725cb.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="360"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:18.8%;top:40.8%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:50%;top:40.8%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:18.8%;top:66.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:9.8%;top:87.8%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Someone who already signs in gets the new role at once, with no email. Owners and investors must be on file first: People &gt; Owners and People &gt; Investors also have a one-click invite for a record without a sign-in.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-add-an-investor" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add an investor</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Investors</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Add an investor</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Fill in the Legal name and the Type: Individual, or Corporation with the Person who signs for the corporation. Then the Email, the Phone and the Address (start typing and choose it).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Optional: the Amount committed, and the Yearly return offered (the investor offer&#39;s, 30% unless you change it; the investment agreement sets the one that applies).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Invite now is ticked: press <b class="gd-ui">Add and invite</b>. The record is added and the investor gets the invitation to choose a password for the investor portal. Untick it to add the record only, and invite later from the list.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-send-a-password-link" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Send a password link</h2><p class="gd-p">For anyone who forgot their password or let their invitation expire.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Under People who can sign in, search by name or email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On their row, press <b class="gd-ui">Send password link</b>. They get &quot;Reset your CarmaCars password&quot;, valid for 24 hours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">View as (...)</b> on the same row opens their portal, read only.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/portals</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/440"><img src="/guides/img/admin-27-portals-desktop-ee9b3e94.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="440"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:74.8%;top:6.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:68.2%;top:28.6%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:84.1%;top:28.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-view-as-see-what-someone-sees" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">View as: see what someone sees</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A red banner says &quot;Viewing as Name (email), read only.&quot; on every page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Click around their portal. Nothing can be changed: every save is refused.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Exit</b> to come back. A view also ends by itself after 30 minutes.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/620"><img src="/guides/img/admin-28-view-as-desktop-f858e38c.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="620"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:48.6%;top:4.5%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:94.4%;top:4.5%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Can&#39;t change anything in Admin? You may still be viewing as someone. Look for the red banner and press Exit.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-the-audit-log" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The audit log</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Logs</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Changes</b> tab, shows who changed what, and when.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Changes lists every change with the person, the action, the table and the record. Data access lists lookups of private data.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Every View as is recorded (view_as_start), with the person viewed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Search by table, record id or value.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/audit</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/560"><img src="/guides/img/admin-29-audit-desktop-b7504100.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="560"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:22.6%;top:31.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:39%;top:46.4%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:89.6%;top:20.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-staff-and-roles" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Staff and roles</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Team</b> opens Staff and roles.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Invite staff here too: Role, Name, Email, Main function and Also covers, then <b class="gd-ui">Invite</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each row has <b class="gd-ui">Send password link</b>, <b class="gd-ui">View as (...)</b> and Limits (how much they may approve or refund).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">End access</b> to close their staff portal at once. <b class="gd-ui">Restore</b> undoes it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/settings/staff</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/780"><img src="/guides/img/admin-26-staff-desktop-72287d0b.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="780"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.8%;top:59%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:94.4%;top:86.7%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:83.3%;top:92.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-admin-access" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Admin access</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then Admin access. Who may hold the Admin role.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The list holds rent@carmacars.ca, and verify-admin@carmacars.ca, the automated test account the site&#39;s nightly checks sign in with.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Below it: everyone who holds the Admin role now. Each must be on the list; the database refuses the Admin role to any other address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Change the list only if the business&#39;s Admin address changes.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-staff-scorecards" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Staff scorecards</h2><p class="gd-p">See how each assistant is doing against the targets.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a staff member&#39;s row in Staff and roles, press <b class="gd-ui">Scorecard</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">By week shows each measure (for example quote sent within 5 minutes) and the result for each week.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A task meets its target when it is done by its due time. Daily checks count when done by 9:00 and 18:00.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/scorecard</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/350"><img src="/guides/img/va-sales-05-scorecard-desktop-956a5a9e.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="350"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:21.1%;top:42.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-sales-by-staff-member" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sales by staff member</h2><p class="gd-p">See each person&#39;s commissions, quotes, offers, rentals added, bookings confirmed and booked revenue.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a staff member&#39;s row in Staff and roles, press <b class="gd-ui">Sales</b>. Press <b class="gd-ui">By week</b> or <b class="gd-ui">By month</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The tiles show the current week or month. By week (or By month) lists each period: quotes created, offers sent, rentals added, bookings confirmed, conversion and booked revenue.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Follow-ups due lists their open deals with the next step. Deals lists each booking they created, added or sent an offer on, with what it counts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A deal credited to the wrong person, or marked sourced when it was not? Press <b class="gd-ui">Reassign</b> beside it, choose who, say whether they sourced the client, and write the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Commission rate</b> gives this person their own flat rate (empty: the Program settings). <b class="gd-ui">Reverse</b> beside a commission stops it, for example for a household rental found later.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Staff enter their own home address (at their first sign-in, before they sign their agreement, or in their profile). It is needed before they add a rental or earn a commission, and spots a household rental. <b class="gd-ui">Home address</b> here changes it if it is wrong.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">The whole team: <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Overview</b>, the Sales card at the bottom. Choose another month and press <b class="gd-ui">Show</b>.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Figure</th><th scope="col">How it is counted</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Credited to</td><td>Whoever created the quote or added the rental; for a website request, whoever sent its first offer. An Admin can reassign it.</td></tr><tr><td>Conversion</td><td>Of the deals credited in the period, the share confirmed so far.</td></tr><tr><td>Booked revenue</td><td>The rental charge before tax, after discounts, for bookings confirmed in the period. A cancelled booking counts only what was kept; refunds come off.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-sales-staff-in-person-or-remote" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sales staff: in person or remote</h2><p class="gd-p">Each Sales person works in person (Toronto) or remote (anywhere, a contractor). Staff and roles lists them under Sales staff: in person or remote.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Work mode</b> on a person (or on their Sales page), choose In person or Remote and give the reason. A new Sales person starts in person.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The list shows the mode, the rate now, the rate the month would end at, and for remote this month&#39;s touches against 400, the peak hours scheduled this week (20 needed, Thursday to Sunday afternoons) and the replies on time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">On a remote person&#39;s Sales page, Remote duties shows their checklist, touches, blocks and reply time. <b class="gd-ui">Void</b> beside a touch logged by mistake takes it off, with a reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">When you approve a Sales month, its mode, rates, touches and any drop are locked: a later change of mode or settings does not change it. Their My sales shows each month in one line.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">Rule</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Rates</td><td>In person 10%, 15% from 50 rental days, 20% from 100. Remote 5 points lower on every tier: 5%, 10%, 15%</td></tr><tr><td>Credit</td><td>In person: walk-ins, handovers, partner visits and the rentals they source. Remote: only the rentals they source; a website request they answer with the first offer during their blocks is credited to them; a walk-in or a partner deal earns them nothing</td></tr><tr><td>Remote minimum</td><td>400 touches a month. Under it, when the month ends, the month&#39;s rate is one tier lower (5% becomes 2.5%). Settings &gt; Program settings, Staff commissions, changes the minimum, the drop and the floor</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-an-admin-has-every-staff-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">An Admin has every staff page</h2><p class="gd-p">An Admin account is only an Admin: it already has every page of the staff portals, so no office or field role can be added to it, and the invite form and Staff and roles refuse it. To work as staff, use a separate account. An Admin can still be given a field job and opens it on the field portal.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-two-records-of-one-person" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Two records of one person</h2><p class="gd-p">When two renter records are clearly the same person (the same phone verified with a code, or the same name, date of birth and phone), the site merges them by itself within 15 minutes, into the record with more bookings. Bookings, licences, cards, payments, documents and messages move. The person can then sign in with either email or with their phone number and a code, and gets one short note: &quot;Your CarmaCars accounts are now one&quot;. A match on the name alone stays a task for you, and <b class="gd-ui">Merge into this record</b> under the renter still works as before.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the renter. The Merged records card lists each merge, automatic or by staff, with what moved and the emails that now sign in there.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Two different people after all? Press <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> and say why. Everything moved goes back and both records are as they were.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-new-staff-the-academy-then-the-agreement-then-the-portal" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">New staff: the academy, then the agreement, then the portal</h2><p class="gd-p">Every staff member (never an Admin) opens their portal in this order: their staff agreement first, then the academy, then everything else (release 48: the agreement moved before the academy; anyone who already passed the academy is only asked to sign). Until the agreement is signed they open only <b class="gd-ui">Welcome</b>, their profile, the guide and their documents to sign; after it, until the academy is passed, only the academy, the guide, their profile and Welcome.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The agreement is sent by itself to everyone without one, filled from their record and their hire&#39;s pay and start date: the Field Staff Agreement for field work, the contractor agreement for customer service, Fleet, Finance and Sales (in person or remote). One reminder goes 3 days after it was sent.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Team</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff and roles</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Staff agreements</b>: who has not signed, what the automatic send waits for (for example a field hire&#39;s licence number), and <b class="gd-ui">Waive</b> with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Welcome also asks for the name they go by (the preferred name, shown across the portals and on the staff list), and, once the agreement and the academy are done, shows the team&#39;s WhatsApp group (Program settings, <b class="gd-ui">WhatsApp team group link</b> and <b class="gd-ui">WhatsApp Sales group link</b>; empty until you set them: while either is empty, Hiring warns and To do keeps an urgent task. Reset the invite link in WhatsApp, keep Add other members for admins only and Approve new participants on, then paste it). Each group shows the person&#39;s member tag (&quot;Name - Position&quot;) with Copy and the steps; I joined needs <b class="gd-ui">I set my member tag</b>. The same link goes by email, once.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-accounts-locked-for-inactivity" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Accounts locked for inactivity</h2><p class="gd-p">A staff account with no sign-in or use for 10 days (Program settings, <b class="gd-ui">Staff inactive lock days</b>) is locked; the person is warned by email on day 7 and sees &quot;Account locked for inactivity&quot; when they sign in. You get an alert. On <b class="gd-ui">Team</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff and roles</b> the row says <b class="gd-ui">Locked for inactivity</b>: press <b class="gd-ui">Unlock</b>. The staff list shows each person&#39;s last sign-in. Admin accounts are never locked.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-hours-and-the-townhall" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Hours and the townhall</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Team</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Timesheet</b>: the hours customer service, Fleet and Finance clocked (Clock in and out on their home page). Add hours someone forgot, or void a wrong entry, with the reason. A person not clocked in 15 minutes after their start time (customer service 9:00, Fleet 11:00, Toronto) is reminded.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Breaks and idle time (release 35).</b> Customer service, Fleet and Finance press <b class="gd-ui">Start break</b> and <b class="gd-ui">End break</b> next to the clock; breaks have no fixed length. On <b class="gd-ui">Timesheet</b>, each person&#39;s days show the hours clocked and worked, their breaks (how many, the total and the longest) and their idle time, with every break and idle stretch listed. <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> a break with the reason (in the audit log). Finance sees the breaks but never the idle time. A break open past 30 minutes reminds the person and you. Whether breaks are paid is <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; va_breaks_paid (on: salaried; off: breaks come off the hours on the payroll, where each line shows the period&#39;s breaks).</p><p class="gd-p">While someone is clocked in, not on a break and within their scheduled hours, the portal notes the fact of their activity (never keys, pages or screens), at most once a minute; their actions count too. With no activity for more than va_idle_alert_minutes (10), you get one alert, &quot;Name (role) inactive since 10:42, 12 min&quot;, and one more at va_idle_followup_minutes (30). A call they are on (their Quo user, set with <b class="gd-ui">Set Quo user</b> on Timesheet; the <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> button; a note in the caller pop-up) and the townhall (joined or present, to its end plus 10 minutes) pause it. <b class="gd-ui">KPIs</b> shows <b class="gd-ui">Idle minutes</b> against kpi_idle_minutes_week.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Team</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Townhall</b>: the weekly staff call (Wednesdays at 6:30 pm Toronto). The deck builds itself every Sunday night from the week&#39;s data: the week, platform updates, fleet, staff, sales with the leaderboard, finances and claims (the last two for Admins only). Add a note to any slide; <b class="gd-ui">Build again</b> refreshes the numbers. With no call link in Program settings, <b class="gd-ui">Join the call</b> opens the call in the site; staff add the call to their calendar from the page.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-the-townhall-day-attendance-and-the-team-slide-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The townhall day, attendance and the team slide (release 35)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The townhall is every Wednesday at 6:30 pm Toronto time. To change it, press <b class="gd-ui">Change the day or time</b> on the Townhall page. Beside it, a table shows the website&#39;s visitor sessions of the last 8 weeks for each day, as information. Field applicants&#39; live calls always take the hour before.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Every staff member is invited and reminded an hour before. <b class="gd-ui">Join the call</b> on the townhall page, or <b class="gd-ui">Check in</b> from 15 minutes before, counts them as there.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">When the call ends, the people who missed it are recorded, the staff list shows &quot;Missed N townhalls&quot; for the last 8 weeks, and you get an alert with the names.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The deck&#39;s last slide is the team: a tile per person with their role&#39;s numbers for the week. Press <b class="gd-ui">Add a shout-out</b> on a tile to add yours.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-where-staff-live-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Where staff live (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Welcome asks every hire for their city and country. In the Toronto area Sales keep the mode they were hired in; elsewhere Sales is remote. The staff list shows the location.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-staff-onboarding-breaks-and-shifts-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Staff onboarding, breaks and shifts (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>New staff open their portal after four steps in order: the staff agreement, the academy, confirming the team&#39;s WhatsApp groups, then an Admin&#39;s or a Fleet team member&#39;s approval (or a rejection with a reason the person sees). Everyone already working waits for the same approval once.</li><li>Each person&#39;s row on the Staff onboarding card in Settings and on the Fleet approvals list says exactly what is missing, for example &quot;Waiting on: Academy (3 of 11 sections), Staff agreement signature&quot;. <b class="gd-ui">Mark WhatsApp joined</b> records only the WhatsApp groups, at any step: it never passes the academy or signs the agreement, and it counts when the person reaches that step. Once the agreement and the academy are done, <b class="gd-ui">Confirm WhatsApp and approve</b> marks the groups and approves in one press (Admins only, recorded in the audit log).</li><li>Schedules: customer service, Fleet and Finance have a schedule per role, and an Admin can give one person their own. Today&#39;s duty board shows who is working, late or absent.</li><li>Breaks: office staff log a break from their home page, and the time on break is kept on their timesheet. While someone is on a break, on a call or in the townhall, the idle alert is paused; otherwise a person with no activity for a while on a shift gets an alert, then the Admins do.</li><li>Quiet hours: staff alerts held by a person&#39;s quiet hours arrive as one summary when they end, and no text goes to a renter at night (an answer asked for then arrives in the morning).</li><li>Field staff set their availability (mornings, afternoons and evenings for each weekday) on Welcome and later on My shifts or Profile; Fleet and Admin see it on the shift board.</li><li>Standing weekly shifts are claimed by themselves up to two weeks ahead; the minimum shifts a week is a Program setting (2 in 7 days), and anyone under it gets a reminder and a To do.</li><li>Shifts are published by themselves every hour from the shift template in Program settings (Field jobs and handovers: one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 for one person, every second day, up to 14 days ahead, only forward from the latest shift already published and never before the start date set there). A handover or return no shift covers gets a shift of its own, 90 minutes either side.</li><li>A published shift nobody has claimed 48 hours before it starts alerts Fleet and the Admins with the people to ask.</li><li>Payroll runs every two weeks: Finance prepares it, an Admin approves it and records the payments. KPIs per role are on Team, KPIs, each against a target in Program settings.</li><li>The townhall is every Wednesday at 6:30 pm Toronto time; two missed in a row lock the account until an Admin restores it. A townhall that did not happen (nobody attended, cancelled ahead, or marked by an Admin) counts nobody absent.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-work-chats-only" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Work chats only</h2><p class="gd-p">All staff work communication happens in the group work chats (the CarmaCars Team and Sales WhatsApp groups, and the chats in the portal), never in private messages. It is in every staff guide and in the academy (Work chats). Answer a private work message in the group.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-staff-rewards-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Staff rewards (release 48)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Team</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff rewards</b> lists every staff member: whether they get rental perks and why not, their tier, their progress, their free days and what they used.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Rental perks are for in-person staff in Canada. Remote and international staff get none. Use <b class="gd-ui">Perks</b> to switch one person on or off by hand, with the reason they read.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">From day one (the academy and the agreement done): 15% off their own rentals. Sales earn 1 free day per 100 rental days booked, Field 1 per 100 handovers. Silver at 50 rental days booked in a month is 20% off; Gold at 100 is 25% off and 1 bonus free day. The month&#39;s top seller gets a free weekend.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A perk rental is picked up within 48 hours of booking and never on dates a renter asked for, never on exotic or partner cars, and the staff member must be the driver. A free day ends after 6 months. A suspended account&#39;s perks are frozen.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Free days go on CarmaCars&#39; and shareholders&#39; cars first. On a co-host owner&#39;s car the owner is paid as at the full rate. Each perk used is posted as a staff benefit expense (account 5300).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add free days</b> gives a person free days by hand, with the reason. Every number is in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff rewards</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-data-to-check-on-each-record-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Data to check on each record (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every portal checks the person&#39;s own record and shows them a box with the fix: Settings &gt; Staff, Owners and Renters (renters with a booking in the last 90 days) list everyone with something open, in words. <b class="gd-ui">Send reminder</b> sends a staff member an alert; an owner or a renter sees the box again at their next page, even a warning they put off. A blocking item (the staff agreement waiting for the licence number or the home address, an expired licence of someone who drives) cannot be put off. In-person staff with a home address outside Ontario are asked to confirm it with the reason; what they wrote is kept.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-updated-agreements-to-accept-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Updated agreements to accept (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">When a document changes (the terms of use, the privacy policy, the rental agreement, the owner program agreement, the staff agreements), everyone it binds sees one box at their next sign-in: what changed in a few lines, the new text, and <b class="gd-ui">Accept and continue</b>. Accepting is recorded with the version, the time, the IP address and the device; nobody signs again. Declining keeps their portal closed and shows how to reach us. Admin settings, Terms, lists each version with how many accepted, declined or still wait, and who.</p><p class="gd-p">Release 48 published three: the rental agreement (the new return charges), the owner program agreement (owner use for someone else, the $150 Install Fee) and the staff agreements (confidentiality, non-solicitation for 12 months, data returned or deleted on exit, and a non-compete for contractors only: none for employees, as Ontario&#39;s Employment Standards Act requires).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-people-on-the-live-map" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">People on the live map</h2><p class="gd-p">The live map (Visitors, and Cars &gt; Fleet tracking) has a <b class="gd-ui">People</b> layer: staff on shift or on a job, and renters and owners at a pickup or return, each with a marker by role. Use the role chips to show or hide each group. Staff appear only after they accept the electronic monitoring policy, and never off duty; renters and owners only with their phone&#39;s permission and only two hours either side of a pickup or return. Only the latest position is kept, plus a job&#39;s points for 30 days. Admins and Fleet see everyone; customer service and Sales see renters at a pickup or return; Finance and field staff see no one.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-resignations-release-50" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Resignations (release 50)</h2><p class="gd-p">Staff resign themselves on their <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b> (<b class="gd-ui">Resign</b>, the last section; on <b class="gd-ui">Welcome</b> while still in onboarding). You get an email and an alert, Finance too, and an Offboarding To do opens in the Admin queue.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff and roles</b> shows <b class="gd-ui">Resigning: last day</b> with the day notice was given, the reason and the <b class="gd-ui">Offboarding To do</b> link. After the last day it shows Resigned, with the dates.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The To do lists what to do: final pay up to the last day (Finance), the keys, cards and equipment to collect (not tracked in the system), their open field jobs and shifts to reassign, and the leads, chats, To dos and claims to hand back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Their field jobs and shifts after the last day go back to the queue at once; nobody can give them a shift or a job after it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Change last day</b> moves it earlier or later (from today); they are emailed the new day and the To do follows. <b class="gd-ui">Withdraw resignation</b> cancels it for them. <b class="gd-ui">End access now</b> ends it at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">After the last day their access ends by itself (the same as <b class="gd-ui">End access</b>), their open To dos and chats go back to the queues and their claims are released. <b class="gd-ui">Restore</b> gives access back if they return.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Someone who resigned by email or in person: <b class="gd-ui">Record a resignation</b> on their row, with the last day and the reason as they gave it. Today ends their access now.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">The connector&#39;s <span class="gd-url">list_staff</span> shows each person&#39;s resignation.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'fleet-and-listings', 'chapter', 'calendar-sync-with-turo-and-other-platforms', 'Vehicles is the fleet. Listings turns a car into a page on carmacars.ca in four steps: photos, covered plates, a review, and live on the site.

## Vehicles

**Cars** > **Vehicles**

1. Filter by status; More filters has who supplies the car, retired cars and the mode. Each row shows the plate, class, owner, mode, status, listing and daily rate.
2. Search by plate, model or owner. **Cars** > **Rates for many cars** changes the rates of many cars at once.
3. Open a car for its tabs: Overview, Rates, Fees and coverage, Calendar, Listing, and Owner, documents, tracker. The Tracker card links to Fleet tracking.

![](/guides/img/admin-08-vehicles-desktop-46461f49.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 900; address: carmacars.ca/admin/vehicles; pins: 1 74.3 31.1, 2 37.5 24.3, 3 48.6 52.4")

## Set a car''s rates and kilometres

Open the car, then the **Rates** tab. Everything on it saves together, in one step.

1. Type the four rates. Only the daily rate is needed: an empty weekend rate is the daily rate, an empty weekly rate is 6 days at the daily rate, and an empty monthly rate is 22 days.
2. Kilometres: keep **Use the defaults** (the kilometres a day in Settings, Kilometre choices, and the extra kilometre rate in Fee defaults for the car''s class), or choose **Custom for this car** and type them.
3. Check the deposit (the class default is filled in), and the delivery and pickup fees: each is one way, an empty pickup fee is the delivery fee, and 0 means not offered.
4. Read What renters pay under the fields: real prices for a weekend, a few weekdays, a week and a month, worked out the way bookings are priced. Press **Save the rates**.

| Rate | What it means |
| --- | --- |
| Daily rate | A price per day, for each day that starts on a Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday or Thursday |
| Weekend rate | A price per day, not for the whole weekend: each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday. Friday 10 am to Sunday 10 am is 2 days at this rate; Sunday to Monday is a daily day |
| Weekly rate | The price for 7 days. Rentals of 7 to 29 days cost this for each 7 days, counted by the day. A 1 to 6 day rental never costs more |
| Monthly rate | The price for 30 days. A 7 to 29 day rental never costs more |

5. Lead-time pricing for this car, below the rates: **Program settings** (the tiers there), **Off for this car**, or **Its own tiers** (a table like the one in Program settings). Press **Save**.
6. **Price limits**, beside them: the lowest and highest daily rate the owner accepts. **This car** sets the car''s own; the owner''s line sets them for every car of that owner (a car''s own come first, field by field). Empty is no limit. Press **Save price limits**. Owners set the same limits in their portal.

> Good to know: Price limits hold the rental a day (after lead-time pricing, the non-refundable discount, a discount, a promo code or a price typed by hand; never fees, add-ons or tax) between the minimum and the maximum: one line, "Minimum daily rate for this car" or "Maximum daily rate for this car", brings it back. Never on an Owner Booking or a booking billed to an insurer. To price one request outside them, open its review screen, **More options**, tick **Allow a price outside the car''s price limits (Admin only)** and say why: it is kept on the booking and in the audit log. Untick it and the limits apply again.

> Tip: A problem shows on its own field, in words, as you type. When similar cars have rates, a line suggests them with Use these; it is only a hint. The same fields are on **Add a car**, so a car can be added with its rates in one pass.

## Fleet tracking

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, the **Fleet tracking** tab. Fleet staff have the same map as **Fleet map** in their menu; customer service, Sales and Finance open it from **Find a car** (**Car map**) and field staff under **Map**, read only: every staff member sees where the cars are, and only Admins and fleet staff mark alerts as seen. Every car on the same map as the Live map, with who has it. A car''s page and a booking''s page show **Where the car is** (or **No tracker yet**). Each owner sees the location and trips of their own cars in the owner portal, never the renter or the booking.

1. The four numbers: cars on rent, moving, parked, and open alerts.
2. The map shows each car as its photo in a ring: green moving (the arrow is its heading), yellow engine on, blue parked, orange not reporting. The list beside it has every car with its renter, booking, when it is due back (late in red) and its state.
3. Press a car on the map or in the list for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery, whether the tracker has the car''s power, and the trip under way.
4. **Alerts**: speeding, left Ontario, left your zone, still driving after the return time, low tracker battery, unplugged and not reporting. Each also comes to the bell and, with phone alerts on, under Urgent alerts. Press **Show** to see where, **Seen** when it is handled, or **Mark all as seen**.
5. **Trips by booking**: each booking''s trips, kilometres and top speed (red at the speeding level). Press the last trip to draw its route on the map.

## Pair a tracker with a car

1. A new tracker that reports shows under **Trackers**, "Reporting, not on a car yet". Press **Pair**, choose the car and the install date.
2. Or press **Pair a tracker** and type its device ID (the IMEI or serial number on the tracker).
3. The install date starts the Tracker Fee on the owner''s invoice when the car has none yet. A replacement tracker keeps the car''s first date; the old tracker is taken off by itself.
4. **Remove** takes a tracker off a car (tick "faulty" for a broken one). The Tracker Fee is not changed.

## Tracking settings

Below the trackers: the speeding level (140 km/h), the minutes of grace after the return time (15), the low battery level (20%), the hours before "not reporting" (6), the Ontario alert, and one optional zone (a name, its centre and a radius in km). History keeps a moving car''s position once a minute for 90 days, trips and alerts for 365 days (at most 365: the privacy policy keeps tracker data 12 months).

1. Demo mode (off): simulated cars drive the GTA''s highways here and on the Live map, for a demonstration. Nothing is saved. Turn it off before the trackers go live.
2. **Make the ingest key**: the relay or tracker service signs every batch of positions with it. It is shown once; making a new one stops the old one at once.

> Tip: The Live map shows the same cars with its Fleet layer (tick Fleet).

## Tracker events, evidence and pound flags (release 48)

Below the map on the **Fleet tracking** tab of **Cars**. It is off until the trackers are installed: an Admin turns on **Tracker events** under **Tracker event settings**.

On, each event makes one alert per car, kind and 30 minutes (never a flood), an evidence record, and a notice to the renter and to the car''s owner:

- **Speeding over 180, 220 or 300 km/h**: one record per event, at the highest limit reached, with that limit''s speeding charge of Settings > Program ($500, $1,000 and $2,500 plus HST by default). One event is one charge: 226 km/h is $1,000, not $500 plus $1,000. The renter is told what the Tracker recorded, the charge and the clause (rental agreement 10.5).
- **Over the speeding alert level** (140 km/h) and **harsh driving**: a friendly heads-up to the renter, no charge.
- **Left Ontario**, **driving after the return time**, a tracker unplugged or tampered with: a notice with the clause. No set charge.
- **Left Canada**: urgent, once per crossing. Admins and on-duty Fleet get an alert, an email and a text at once (always on), Fleet gets an urgent To do, and the renter is told that leaving Canada needs written approval (rental agreement 10.1). Leaving Ontario for another province or a state reaches the same people the same way.
- **Driving at night** (off unless you turn it on): staff and the owner only. The agreement sets no curfew.
- **At a pound**: see Pound flags below.

The **Tracker events** table shows each record: when, the car and booking, the speed and the map point, where it came from, how many readings it keeps, its seal (a SHA-256), the charge and the clause, and who was told.

1. To bill a speeding record, press **Charge** on its row (an Admin or Finance). The charge is added to the booking with the evidence record attached, and it is taken from the deposit first.
2. The record goes into the dispute pack by itself, with the notice the renter got.

**Pound flags**: a car whose tracker parks inside a pound lot''s radius for 20 minutes is flagged. Fleet gets an urgent To do and alert, Fleet and Admins an email, and the renter is told to call.

1. Call the lot (its phone and hours are on the flag), then the renter. Keep the receipts.
2. Press **Record the path**: the non-return charge ($1,000) or the theft recovery charge ($1,500) with the tow, impound and storage costs, **Recovered, nothing to charge**, or **Not a pound**. Write what happened.
3. A charge still waits for its other evidence (the final late notice, the receipt) like every fee.

**Pound lots**: the known Ontario lots, with name, address, phone and hours. It starts with the lots the Toronto and Peel police publish.

1. Press **Find the pins from the addresses** once; a lot with no pin cannot flag a car.
2. **Edit** a lot to add its hours, fix its details or type its pin, and tick **I checked these details with the lot**.
3. **Add a lot** for any other pound you know of.

> Note: The renter''s notice about a charge is always sent. The renter can mute the heads-up, and the owner can mute their alerts, in their own notification settings.

## The listing pipeline

Open **Cars** > **Listings**. A draft waiting for review shows Needs review.

1. Each row shows the car, plate, state, photos and the work done on it so far.
2. Press **Start a listing** to begin one for a car that has none.
3. Open a car to review it.

![](/guides/img/admin-09-listings-desktop-970819b6.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 560; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings; pins: 1 53.5 37.0, 2 87.2 21.1, 3 32.6 37.0")

## Review a listing

1. Steps to go live shows four numbered steps: **1 Photos** (how many of the required photos are in, 14 for most cars, 13 for a two-seater with no rear seats), **2 Cover plates**, **3 Review** and **4 Live on the site**. Each says what it needs and has one button to where it is done; the step to do now is in red. A step that stopped (a photo edit or the copy) shows under them with **Retry**.
2. Similar cars on file lists possible duplicates. Press **Not a duplicate** or **Same car**. An open flag does not keep the car off the site; only Same car does.
3. The copy is written by itself from the car''s facts and published when it passes the checks: nothing to type. To change a line, press Change; that field is then locked and kept by every new version.
4. Under Photos, each public photo shows its plate state: Plate not checked, Plate covered or No plate visible.

![](/guides/img/admin-10-listing-review-desktop-352745fd.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1100; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449; pins: 1 20.6 16.6, 2 86.1 47.5, 3 19.9 106.8, 4 74.9 106.8")

## Cover the licence plate

The plates are checked by themselves. Every photo is looked at by the vision model within the day''s free AI share: a plate it finds is blurred so no character can be read (the photo shows Covered automatically, with how sure it was), a photo with no plate is marked No plate visible (No plate seen automatically), and a photo it is not sure of stays Plate not checked for you. While photos wait, the Photos card says how many. A wrong decision: press **Undo** on the photo (the photo as it was comes back, Plate not checked), or **Not a plate: no plate visible** on a cover put where there is no plate.

To cover a plate yourself, press **Cover the plate** on the photo. The editor opens right under it.

1. Check the box over the plate, or press **Suggest the plate**.
2. Drag over a plate to draw a box. Drag a box to move it, or its corner to resize it.
3. The plate is blurred so no character can be read, only over the plate itself, with rounded corners and a soft edge. Nothing is drawn on a plate. A car with no front plate gets no box there. The studio photos Gemini makes have no plate at all: it is taken off cleanly, and a bumper without a plate is left as it is.
4. Press **Save the covered photo**. **Clear the boxes** starts over.
5. No plate in the shot? Press **No plate visible on this photo**.

![](/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-desktop-4219ad93.jpg "desktop; size: 690 703; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449; pins: 1 42.5 83.8, 2 49.6 29.9, 3 4.3 77.4, 4 15.5 83.8, 5 18.1 91.2")

> Tip: The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately. Keyboard: N adds a box, the arrows move it, Shift and the arrows resize it, Delete removes it.

## Publish

1. A real car that is not on the site is a line on To do: press **Set rates and publish**. The daily rate is filled in (the car''s own, or the suggested rate from similar cars or the class); change it if you like and press **Publish now**.
2. On the car itself, the Listing tab has **Publish now**; each open item of its checklist has a button to where it is done.
3. From a listing review: press **Approve and publish**, **Approve, publish later**, or **Send back** with what to fix.

> Watch out: The plate check never holds a car back: a real photo whose plate is not checked stays private (the other photos, or the sample photos, show instead) and goes public by itself once its plate is covered or marked not visible. Listings already live show "Plate not checked" on such photos.

## Photos filed under the wrong shot, and interior windows

1. On the Photos card, each shot lists its photos. A photo filed under the wrong shot: press **Remove** under it, then **Remove it**. The shot is free again: take or pick the right photo. The removed photo is kept privately and the removal is in the history. A live listing''s photos change in the review instead (Reject).
2. Dashboard and seat photos: what shows through the windows is replaced by the studio background when the cut is clean (a quality check: some but not most of the frame seen through, high in the frame, a few clean regions, sharp edges). Otherwise the windows are blurred, and the photo is marked windows blurred. Nothing to do.
3. A car with 2 seats or fewer needs no Rear seats photo.

## A listing without photos yet: sample photos

A car can be listed before its photos are taken. Until then the site shows a sample photo.

1. Submit the listing without photos. The listing copy is still written for you from the car''s details.
2. The car page and the car''s card show a sample photo, captioned "Sample photo", so renters know it is not this car. Staff see "Using sample photos" on the car and in Listings.
3. Publishing does not wait for a plate check: a sample photo has no plate.
4. Add the real photos when they are taken. Once real photos are approved they replace the sample at once; nothing else to do.

## Sample photos

**Settings** > **Sample photos**. The pictures a car shows until its real photos are in.

1. Every body type has a built-in picture (sedan, SUV, truck, van, coupe, hatchback, electric car).
2. Add your own: choose the Body type, and a Make and Model if the photo is of that exact model, pick the Photo, and press **Add the photo**.
3. The most specific photo wins: make and model, then make and body type, then body type. **Turn off** or **Delete** a photo you no longer want.
4. Cars using sample photos lists the cars still waiting for real photos. Each real car showing sample photos is also a line on To do, with **Add photos**.

![](/guides/img/admin-36-sample-photos-desktop-55c64070.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 812; address: carmacars.ca/admin/settings/sample-photos; pins: 4 26.8 28.9")

## Publish now, and new cars published by themselves

Nothing between a new car and the site has to be finished first: the car goes on the site, and what is still open shows on its checklist.

1. **Settings** > **Program**, **Publish new cars automatically** (on by default): a new real car goes on the site by itself as soon as it has its year, make and model and its rates, when it is added with rates, when its rates are saved, when it is added for an owner, or when an owner''s application is approved.
2. Otherwise open the car: its Listing tab says why it is not on the site and has **Publish now**. A car with no rates yet is published with the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults in Program settings); change them later on the Rates tab.
3. Every real car has its listing from the moment it is added, as a draft. It shows in Listings and in Not on the site yet until it is published.
4. An owner''s own application waits for your decision before its car is published by itself; Publish now still works.
5. A car taken off the site by staff, or scheduled for a later date, is never published by itself: press **Publish now**.

## The checklist: what is still open on a listed car

Open items never stop publishing. They show as warnings on the car''s Listing tab and after Publish now.

| Item | What it means |
| --- | --- |
| Paperwork | Ownership permit, registry forms, agreements signed, Forms C and D, upfront payment, registry visit, tracker, safety certificate |
| Insurance | Not on the fleet insurance policy yet: the car can be booked, but not handed over |
| Details | Colour, body, seats, gearbox: the car page leaves out what is missing |
| Photos | No real photos: sample photos stand in. A photo whose plate is not checked stays private until it is |
| No VIN yet | A car added by its plate alone: add the VIN when you have it |
| Possible duplicate | An open flag in Similar cars. Only Same car keeps the car off the site |
| Owner terms | The management fee (Revenue Share) and fees not set: a request uses the owner''s terms or the standard grid |

## The fleet policy rule at handover

A program owner''s car is listed and can be requested, offered and paid for while its paperwork is open. It is never handed over until the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet insurance policy.

- Staff see a warning on a request and an offer for a car not on the policy yet.
- The handover refuses the car until the insurer''s confirmation is recorded (Owners and onboarding). The field app says so on the job.
- Only real states keep a car off the site: retired, left the program, out of service, Turo only, bookings turned off, a self-managed owner in arrears, or a paused listing.

## Cars on sample photos

**Cars**, **Listings** ends with **Cars on sample photos**: each real car whose page still shows sample photos, with its newest handover photos (the check-in and check-out photos field staff take).

1. Where a handover photographed the car, press **Use the handover photos**. They go into the car''s listing as if taken on the capture screen.
2. When every required shot is there, the listing is submitted: Gemini makes each photo from the original, then the listing waits for your review like any other.
3. A car with no handover photos yet gets them at its next handover, or press **Start a listing** and take them.

> Good to know: The listing photos use no Cloudflare image processing: Gemini makes every photo and the site makes the sizes.

## A car''s registration and documents

Open the car, then **Owner & documents**. The **Registration** card:

1. Correct the **VIN** (it is checked: 17 characters, the check digit, not on another car; decoded again for the body style and trim), the **Year** and the **Body style**.
2. Type the **Ontario permit number** and the date the **Plate sticker expires**. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before; save the new date after the renewal and the task closes.
3. Under **Documents**, choose the kind (**Ownership permit**, Safety Standards Certificate, owner''s insurance, other), pick the photo or PDF and press **Upload**. The ownership permit clears that item of the owner''s checklist.
4. For the **Safety Standards Certificate**, also type its number, the date it was issued and the date it expires. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before it expires; upload the new certificate with its dates and the task closes. It is a document on the car, not a service record, and nothing is billed to the owner.
5. **Add a car** takes the ownership permit and the Safety Standards Certificate too, under **Documents (optional)**.

## A car added under the wrong owner

Open the car, Overview, **Who supplies the car**, **Move to another owner**. Choose the owner, or **CarmaCars (owner not known yet)**: the car becomes a company car, with no owner schedule or terms.

- The car''s unsigned owner application and vehicle schedule are withdrawn (kept in the history), and its draft owner invoices are deleted. Nobody is notified.
- It is refused once anything for the car is signed, issued, paid or on a statement.

### The VIN from the car, not typed

Every VIN field (Add a car, Add a car for an owner, the car''s **Registration**, **Start a listing**) has **Scan the barcode** and **Photo of the VIN**. Scan the barcode in the driver''s door frame or at the bottom of the windshield: the phone''s camera reads it by itself. Or take a photo of the VIN plate or sticker: the barcode in it is read first, else the photo is read for the printed VIN. The VIN is checked (17 characters, the check digit; I, O and Q become 1 and 0) and decoded as when you type it. Check it against the car before saving.

### Photos in any order

**Add photos** on the listing takes any number of photos at once from the camera roll. Each is sorted to its shot by itself (front three-quarter, sides, rear, dashboard, seats and the rest); a shot that already has its photo sends the new one to the extra photos, so nothing is replaced by accident. The shots are a guide, not a rule: a listing is complete with 10 photos that can go on the site and one outside photo for the cover. Outside photos get the studio background: the car is cropped to its edges and placed big in the frame with its wheels on the floor and a soft shadow under the tyres, and any corner watermark or caption beside the car is left out. Inside and detail photos are kept as taken; when one has a watermark, a logo or caption text on it, the edge with the mark is cut off by itself, and a photo whose mark cannot be cut off (one in the middle) stays off the site until you replace it. **Cover the plate** opens on every outside photo with the plate box suggested; check it and save.

Outside photos made before the newest framing (the car small in the frame, or without the model''s name behind it) are made again with **Frame the outside photos again** above the photos of the listing, then **Yes, frame again**. The cover and the main outside views get the model''s name lettered behind the car, as on the sample photos (for example CLA, C CLASS, AMG GT). The photos leave the site until their plates are checked again: the plate box is suggested on the new photos; check each and cover it. On a published listing each goes back on the site once its plate is checked.

## Showroom photos

Outside photos go in the CarmaCars showroom by themselves. When a real photographed room is stored (dealership or studio photos licensed for commercial use, fetched once from Wikimedia Commons with their author and licence kept), the car stands in it: about 70% of the width, its wheels on the room''s floor, a soft shadow and a faint reflection under it, its light matched to the room, and no sign or lettering on the real wall. Program settings > Listings has the switch (Photographed showroom rooms, on), the car''s width and the cut-out quality floor: a cut-out that is not clean enough (pieces, a blurry or ragged edge) is never placed in a room, the real photo is used instead (its plate covered as usual) and the photo says so. Without a stored room it is the drawn dark showroom: a simple dark dealership with linear lights in the ceiling, a slatted wood wall between two light strips with a big lit CarmaCars sign, and a polished dark floor with the car''s reflection and a shadow under each tyre. Every angle of a car is in the same room, and the cover has the model''s name in metal letters on the wall under the sign. The image model may relight the car or turn it slightly; a photo that shows another car, model or colour is not used. **Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings** has the switch (Showroom photos, on), the image model that makes the photos look photographed, and its daily limit. Past the limit, or when the image model is not available, the site makes the showroom itself for free, and the photo says why under it.

- A car whose photos were made on the black studio: press **Apply showroom to this car** above its photos, then **Yes, apply**.
- Every car at once: **Listings** > **Showroom photos** > **Apply showroom to every car**, then **Yes, every car**.
- Under a photo in the showroom: **Redo** makes it again, **Back to the original** puts back the version before the showroom.

A car that stays where it was keeps its plate check. When the image model made the photo, check the plate again: the photo is off the site until you do. Photos made in the first showroom are made again in the new one with **Apply showroom to this car** or **Apply showroom to every car**.

## Failed photos

The site makes the photo sizes itself: the image service is asked only to cut the car out (**Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings**: the switch to let the image service make every photo step is off). When the image service is busy or over its allowance, the photo still goes on the site from the original and is made again later. A listing marked Failed has **Retry failed photos** in its note; **Retry failed photos** at the top does every listing. They are made again a few at a time, and the listing leaves Failed when they are done.

## The primary photo is always the front exterior (release 43)

The first photo of every car on the site, in the cards, the feeds and the Marketplace kit is its exterior at the standard angle (front three-quarter, in the dark showroom). An inside photo is never ahead of an outside one, and the cover mark follows by itself whenever photos are added, made again or reordered.

- **Primary photo is not exterior** is a flag and a filter in **Cars** > **Vehicles**: it marks a car whose first photo is an inside one because its best outside photo is not on the site yet, or it has none. Add or approve an outside photo and the flag clears by itself.
- **Redo photos with Gemini** on the car page makes every photo of the car again from its original with Gemini, and generates its missing angles. A photo Gemini cannot make well stays off the site, flagged. It needs the image model switched on in Program settings, Listings.
- The same press checks the car''s **Other detail** photos again: an outside view filed there is moved to the outside photos (the front three-quarter becomes the first photo) and made in the showroom. This is what clears the flag on a car that showed nothing to redo.
- Every outside photo has the same room behind it: Gemini replaces the whole background from the original photo.
- Every plate is blurred; nothing is drawn on it and there is no text anywhere else. Inside photos stay sharp from front to back.
- **Redo every car with Gemini** (Listings, Showroom photos; Admin and Fleet) is the same as **Redo every car** on the Photo standard card.

## The photo standard: every photo made by Gemini (release 45)

Every listing photo is made by Gemini from the original photo, never from a cut-out. Outside photos get their whole background replaced by the CarmaCars showroom, with nothing of the place they were taken in left. Inside photos are cleaned up (no clutter) and sharp from front to back. Every plate is blurred so no character can be read; no plate is drawn and there is no text anywhere else on the photo.

- **The check.** A second Gemini look compares each new photo with the original and refuses it when the old background shows, the car is warped, another colour or model, has parts added or missing, a plate can be read, or there is text anywhere. The site also checks the edges are the dark showroom. A refused photo is made again, twice; then it stays off the site and is counted as flagged.
- **Missing angles.** Every car shows the standard set: front three-quarter, front, side profile, rear three-quarter, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats and trunk. An angle the car has no photo of is generated by Gemini from the car''s own photos, in the same showroom, and marked **AI generated** on the listing (staff only). A real photo of that angle replaces it by itself.
- **The order.** The front three-quarter is always first, then the other outside photos, then the inside ones. A car whose first photo would be an inside one shows no photos and cannot be published until it has an outside one; its front three-quarter is generated first.
- **By itself.** Every 5 minutes the job brings the next cars to the standard, newest listed cars first, until every car is done (about a day for the whole fleet). A photo already at the standard is never made again unless you ask. **Program settings** > **Listings**: the daily Gemini limit (2000 calls), the calls kept for new uploads (50) and the switch.
- **Listings** > **Photo standard** (Admin and Fleet) shows each car: photos at the standard out of all, AI angles, flagged photos and the last run. **Redo this car now** makes all of its photos again at once; **Redo every car** makes every photo of every car again. **Redo photos with Gemini** on a car page does the same as Redo this car now.

## The first photo: plain, with a model, or a flyer

On a listing, under **First photo**, choose what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit. Switch any time; the other photos stay as they are.

- **Plain car**: the cover photo as it is (the default).
- **With a model**: a car-show photo made by the image model, with a fully clothed adult model beside the car. It needs the image model; until it is made (or when the image model is not there) the plain cover shows, and the listing says why.
- **Flyer**: the cover photo with a band like a printed flyer: the car, the price a day from its live rates, the call to action, a badge and the logo. When the price, the words or the cover photo change, it is made again by itself within 10 minutes; the plain cover shows meanwhile.

**Make it again** makes the chosen one again. The words of the flyer and the description of the model are in **Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings** (First photo "flyer" and First photo "with a model"); {car}, {price}, {weekly} and {monthly} are filled for each car.

## Marketing photos in other scenes

For Marketplace and social posts, a car''s outside photos can be made again in other scenes. The website keeps its own photos in the dark showroom: a marketing set never replaces them.

1. On a listing, under **Marketing photos**, choose a scene, or **Mix: a different scene on each photo**, and press **Make the marketing set**.
2. The copies show as they are made. The dark showroom and the plain white studio are made by the site when the image model is not there; the photographic scenes (a bright showroom, a city street at night, the Toronto waterfront, a parking garage, Highway, a scenic road, Brick building) need the image model, and say so on the copy when it is not there.
3. **Download (ZIP)** takes the set; the Marketplace kit''s **With scenes (ZIP)** takes the same set.

**Settings** > **Program settings** > **Marketing scenes** lists the scenes. A scene made in a real place has a photo of that place: Brick building picks its photo by itself: the widest outside photo, as taken, of the shareholders'' own cars. To use another, press **Change the reference photo** and pick one (the shareholders'' cars'' photos come first), or upload one. The scenes'' names and words are in the **Marketing scenes** setting.

## Extra photos

A photo that fits no shot is an extra photo. Under the shots, **Extra outside photos** (put on the studio background) and **Extra inside and detail photos** (touched up) each take any number at once. They count toward the 10 photos, get the same plate check, and come after the standard shots on the car''s page.

1. In the review, **Extra photos, in their order on the car page** lists them.
2. Drag a photo by its handle (⋮⋮), or press **Earlier** or **Later**.
3. Press **Save the order**.

## Fix a cut-out

When the background removal cuts badly (a mirror or a wheel missing, background left beside the car), press **Edit the cut-out** under the outside photo.

1. **Cut-out** shows the car over the photo as taken, shown faintly. Choose **Erase** and brush over what should go, or **Restore** and brush over what the cut-out took off. Set **Brush size** and **Zoom**; when zoomed, **Move the view** pans. **Undo** takes back the last stroke.
2. **On the studio** shows the car on the studio background. Drag the car to move it and use **Size** to make it larger or smaller. **Centre and full size** puts it back.
3. Press **Save as a new version**. The photo is made again in about a minute; the version before and the photo as taken are kept. **Reset to the automatic cut-out** starts again from the automatic one.

> Good to know: If the car did not move, the plate check carries over: a photo marked no plate visible stays so, and a covered plate is covered again on the new photo when the review is open. If the car moved, check the plate again. A photo made before cut-outs were kept shows **Make the cut-out** first; the editor opens by itself when it is ready.

Every photo also gets a light touch-up by itself (exposure, levels, a little contrast and colour, mild sharpening), never enough to change the paint colour or hide a scratch. Turn it off for one photo with **Use original colours** under it (the photo is made again; approve it again), or for every photo in Admin > Settings > **Program settings** (Listings) with **Auto-enhance listing photos**. The photo as uploaded is always kept.
## Import photos from a Google Drive link

The owner often hands over a car''s photos as a public Google Drive folder, or one big folder with a folder per make and then per car. You do not download them: paste the link.

**One car.** On the car''s listing, under the capture, **Import photos from a Google Drive link**. Paste the folder link (shared with Anyone with the link) and press **Import the photos**. Every photo in the folder, and in the folders inside it, is added to this car as if you had pressed Add photos: each is sorted to its shot (else filed as an extra photo, in file-name order), put on the studio background and checked for its plate. The box under the link, **Submit the listing for processing when its photos are in**, is on by default.

**Many cars.** **Cars** > **Import photos from Drive** (a button on Vehicles). Paste the top folder''s link and press **Read the folder**. The page walks every folder and proposes a car for each folder that holds photos, from the year, make, model, colour and plate in the folder names (the make folder above counts; 01 Motors partner cars come first). Check the table: tick or untick **Import**, change the car in the list (the likely cars come first), leave out a folder with **Do not import this folder**. A line marked **Check this one** matched two alike cars. Then press **Import N photos from M folders**.

1. The page follows the import by itself. You can leave it and come back: it runs in the background.
2. The end shows the summary: imported, skipped and failed, and why for each (a file over 15 MB, a file that is not a photo, the same photo already on the car, a folder not shared).
3. **Try the failed photos again** takes only the ones that failed. Pressing Import on the same link again never adds a photo twice: a Drive file already on the car is skipped, and so is the same picture under another name. A photo you took off the car can be imported again.

> Good to know: JPG, PNG, HEIC and WebP only (HEIC and WebP are made JPEG first). At most 15 MB a photo, 600 photos, 400 folders and 4 GB in one import. Drive is asked politely, one photo at a time; a big import takes a while.

> Good to know: Without a key, Drive shows only the first 50 files of a folder on its public page; a folder with more is read in full when Drive allows it. In **Settings**, the **Photo import from Google Drive** box takes a Google API key with the Drive API on (after it is saved only its last 4 characters are shown, and it is never written to the change log): with it, folders of any size are read and photos download without Drive''s warning pages.

## Test bookings and deleting a car

1. On a booking made only to try the site, press **Mark as a test booking** (Admins only; the reason is optional). **Make it a real booking again** undoes it.
2. A car whose bookings are all test bookings can be deleted: the test bookings and their test payments go with it, and a copy is kept in the archive of deleted requests.
3. A car with a real booking cannot be deleted.

## Pickup from owner and return to owner (release 28)

On a car''s page, **Pickup from owner and return to owner** records the car''s condition when CarmaCars picks it up from its owner or gives it back: the date and time, km, fuel, many photos at once with the suggested angles, and notes. **Add photos** adds more to a record later. The owner sees these records read only on the car''s page in their portal. They are the baseline condition for any dispute.

## Incident cards (release 34)
**Cars** > **Vehicles** > **Incident cards** prints the card for each car: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, the support number from Settings, a roadside number when there is one, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. Open a car and press **Incident card** to print only that car; on the list, **Print all cars** prints them all, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks, ready to laminate. Under Fleet insurance policy press **Add the policy** (the insurer, the policy number, the dates, the named insured, the roadside number on the slip) and choose the uploaded slip if you have one: it is printed as it is, otherwise the fields are. The card never shows a premium. Fleet staff print the same cards from their portal.

## Field jobs, shifts and who gets a job

**Cars**, then **Field jobs**, is the board Fleet uses, with every action Fleet has. Shifts are published by themselves from the shift template in Program settings (one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 every second day by default, 14 days ahead, only forward from the latest shift), with a shift of its own for any handover or return no shift covers; **Publish shifts** adds more by hand, and a shift you cancel is not published again. Field staff take them. **Missing check-in and check-out**, on the same page, lists every past rental without its photos and readings, with **Give to field staff**. Jobs go on shifts, not on people: each job is put on the shift covering its time (or that day''s), whoever holds the shift does it (several people share the jobs, least busy first), a shift nobody holds keeps its jobs for whoever claims it, and work lands only on days with shifts (work due on a day without shifts moves to the day before, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day; the booking''s own times never change). A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning on the board and on the booking. **To a shift** moves a job to another shift. You can give a job to a field person on a shift that day or to an Admin, take it off with **Unassign** (tick **Tell them** to let them know), and an Admin who holds a job opens it on the field portal. A person who has not passed the academy cannot be given a job or take a shift. A shift with jobs and nobody on it within 24 hours alerts Fleet and the Admins once.


### Shifts in your Google Calendar (release 50)

At the bottom of **Field jobs**, **Add shifts, townhalls and interviews to Google Calendar** gives you a private calendar link with every field shift, 14 days back to 60 days ahead: the day, the start and end (Toronto time), who claimed it or Open, the tasks on it and a link back to it. It also has the weekly townhall (the next 8 meetings) and every booked interview call with its time, the applicant''s first name, the role and the call link. No email is sent.

1. Press **Make my calendar link**.
2. Press **Add to Google Calendar**, then **Add** in Google. Or **Copy link** and add it in another calendar app by URL.
3. Google refreshes a subscribed calendar on its own schedule, every few hours, so a change can take that long to show.
4. Keep the link to yourself. **Regenerate link** makes a new one and stops the old one; **Turn off** stops it.

## Every view generated from the car''s photos (release 47)

Every car shows nine generated views: front three-quarter (always first), front, side profile, rear three-quarter, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats and trunk. Gemini makes each one from references, so the car is the real car and the room looks like a real showroom.

- **What Gemini is sent.** The car''s own photos (its exact colour, trim and wheels); when it has fewer than three, or none of that side, its newest check-in and check-out photos as well (only as references: they are never shown on the site). Then the sample view of that angle (for the camera position only), the stock photo of the model, and for an outside view the showroom background plate. The words describe each angle: camera height, lens, crop, the car centred, 45 degrees for a three-quarter. Plates blurred, no text, no logos added.
- **The check.** A second Gemini look compares the result with the real photos (same car, colour, wheels and trim, nothing warped, not a render) and with the angle. A refused view is made again, twice, told what was wrong; still refused, it is flagged (release 50: only views that passed are on the site).
- **The real photos.** They stay in the car''s record and on the Admin car page, marked as they were; the site shows the generated view of an angle in place of the real one only once it has passed. Generated views are marked **AI generated** for staff only.
- **By itself.** Every 5 minutes the job takes the front three-quarter of every car first (newest listed first), then the other angles, within the daily Gemini limit (about a day for the whole fleet). **Program settings** > **Listings**: the switch for the generated views.
- **Listings** > **Photo standard** shows each car''s **Generated set** (views made out of nine, being made, flagged, and "from check-in photos" when those were used). **Redo this car now** and **Redo every car** make the generated views again too; the views on the site stay until the new ones pass.
- **Showroom background plates** (**Program settings**, Admin): the room for front, side and rear views. Gemini made them once and a second look confirmed each looks like a real photo. Upload a real photo of a showroom (empty floor in the middle, no people, cars, signs or logos) to replace one or all three; **Make a new one** has Gemini make it again.

## The studio set: every car photographed the same way (release 48)

Every car gets the same nine views, as if all were photographed in one studio on one day: the same angle, camera height, lens and framing for each view, the car facing the same way as the sample covers (the front three-quarter and the side with the nose to the left), plates taken off cleanly, the car itself unchanged.

- The scene: every car stands in the same scene so the covers line up as you scroll: the dark dealership with the CarmaCars sign on the wall by default, with the model''s name on the wall behind the car on the first photo. **Program settings** > **Listings**: the scene for every car. On a car, **Studio photos** > **Scene** picks another for that car only (highway, brick building and the other marketing scenes).
- No photo of an angle? Gemini makes it from the car''s other photos. A car with no photo at all gets its outside views from the stock photo of its model, in its own colour.
- One set everywhere: once a car''s front three-quarter is made, the site shows only its made views, in the standard order, the front three-quarter first: the same photo on the home page, the search cards, the car page, the partner feeds and in the sitemap. The real photos stay in the car''s record.
- The check: Gemini checks each view against the car''s own photos: the same car (model, colour, wheels), the right angle, the nose the right way, the old background gone (the site also measures it), no readable plate. Smaller doubts (framing, a part the photos do not show) stop only the first two tries.
- On a car, **Studio photos** shows each view beside the car''s own photos of that angle, marked **AI**. **Make again** makes one view again; **Take off the site** and **Put on the site**.
- **Listings** > **Photo standard** shows the fleet''s progress: views made out of all, cars with their studio cover, and about how many days are left at Gemini''s daily limit.
- Marketing set: **Make the marketing set** uses the studio views (the same angle and cover as the site) in the scene you choose, plus up to three lifestyle shots: an adult model with the car, styled like a luxury car advert, always fully dressed and tasteful. Each is marked **AI**; tick **In the ZIP** for the photos you want in a post. A lifestyle shot Gemini declines is skipped.
- Background plates (**Program settings**, Admin): one set per scene. Choose the scene, then upload a real photo of the place to replace one or all three.

## Studio renders first (release 48)

- Every car gets the full studio set made from its own photos: same colour, wheels and trim, the same framing for every car.
- On the site the renders come first, in this order: side profile (the nose to the left, the cover), front three-quarter, front, rear three-quarter, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats, trunk. The car''s own photos follow, on the same branded background. They are never hidden.
- A render goes live as soon as it passes the photo check. There is no approval step. To change one, open the car, **Studio photos**, then **Make again** or **Take off the site**. Taking the side profile off makes the next render the cover.
- The car page says **Rendered photos** above the gallery, with **See its real photos**.
- New cars get their renders by themselves. To do every published car now: **Listings**, **Photo standard**, **Render every published car**. The line beside it shows how many cars are done. It works within the image model''s daily limit.
- When a car''s set is live, the owner gets an email and an alert ("Your car has new studio photos"), and Fleet gets "Studio photos live" in the next digest. Look the photos over.
- The Cars filter lists one model per family (for example CLA-Class or 3 Series). The trim shows on the car. A car whose model family is not recognised is listed in **Data health**: fix the typo, or ask for the family to be added.

## One look: studio renders only (release 50)

- **The site shows only studio renders that passed the studio gate.** The car page, the cards, the home hero and its sections, the landing and area pages, the partner feeds, the social preview image and the car picture in emails all use the same renders. A car''s own photos, the drawn sample photos and other cars'' photos are never shown to the public.
- **The studio gate.** After the Gemini check, the site puts the car exactly on its view''s size and position (the same for every car), then compares the wall, the floor and the shadow under the car with the scene''s one background plate (the same plate for every outside view), and checks the view and the way the nose points. A refused view is made again, told why; after three tries it is flagged with the reasons on **Photo standard**.
- No render yet: the car shows one **Photos coming soon** photo of the empty studio until its side profile passes. Its own photos stay in the car''s record, for the renders and for staff.
- **Studio grid.** **Listings** > **Photo standard** > **Studio grid** shows every published car''s nine views side by side, with **Live**, **Being made**, **Gate refused** or **Flagged** and the reasons, so a view that drifts from the others is easy to spot. Use **Make again** on the car''s **Studio photos** to redo one.', 'Fleet and listings', 'Vehicles, the listing pipeline, similar cars and covering licence plates.',
  'Vehicles is the fleet. Listings turns a car into a page on carmacars.ca in four steps: photos, covered plates, a review, and live on the site.

## Vehicles

**Cars** > **Vehicles**

1. Filter by status; More filters has who supplies the car, retired cars and the mode. Each row shows the plate, class, owner, mode, status, listing and daily rate.
2. Search by plate, model or owner. **Cars** > **Rates for many cars** changes the rates of many cars at once.
3. Open a car for its tabs: Overview, Rates, Fees and coverage, Calendar, Listing, and Owner, documents, tracker. The Tracker card links to Fleet tracking.

![](/guides/img/admin-08-vehicles-desktop-46461f49.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 900; address: carmacars.ca/admin/vehicles; pins: 1 74.3 31.1, 2 37.5 24.3, 3 48.6 52.4")

## Set a car''s rates and kilometres

Open the car, then the **Rates** tab. Everything on it saves together, in one step.

1. Type the four rates. Only the daily rate is needed: an empty weekend rate is the daily rate, an empty weekly rate is 6 days at the daily rate, and an empty monthly rate is 22 days.
2. Kilometres: keep **Use the defaults** (the kilometres a day in Settings, Kilometre choices, and the extra kilometre rate in Fee defaults for the car''s class), or choose **Custom for this car** and type them.
3. Check the deposit (the class default is filled in), and the delivery and pickup fees: each is one way, an empty pickup fee is the delivery fee, and 0 means not offered.
4. Read What renters pay under the fields: real prices for a weekend, a few weekdays, a week and a month, worked out the way bookings are priced. Press **Save the rates**.

| Rate | What it means |
| --- | --- |
| Daily rate | A price per day, for each day that starts on a Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday or Thursday |
| Weekend rate | A price per day, not for the whole weekend: each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday. Friday 10 am to Sunday 10 am is 2 days at this rate; Sunday to Monday is a daily day |
| Weekly rate | The price for 7 days. Rentals of 7 to 29 days cost this for each 7 days, counted by the day. A 1 to 6 day rental never costs more |
| Monthly rate | The price for 30 days. A 7 to 29 day rental never costs more |

5. Lead-time pricing for this car, below the rates: **Program settings** (the tiers there), **Off for this car**, or **Its own tiers** (a table like the one in Program settings). Press **Save**.
6. **Price limits**, beside them: the lowest and highest daily rate the owner accepts. **This car** sets the car''s own; the owner''s line sets them for every car of that owner (a car''s own come first, field by field). Empty is no limit. Press **Save price limits**. Owners set the same limits in their portal.

> Good to know: Price limits hold the rental a day (after lead-time pricing, the non-refundable discount, a discount, a promo code or a price typed by hand; never fees, add-ons or tax) between the minimum and the maximum: one line, "Minimum daily rate for this car" or "Maximum daily rate for this car", brings it back. Never on an Owner Booking or a booking billed to an insurer. To price one request outside them, open its review screen, **More options**, tick **Allow a price outside the car''s price limits (Admin only)** and say why: it is kept on the booking and in the audit log. Untick it and the limits apply again.

> Tip: A problem shows on its own field, in words, as you type. When similar cars have rates, a line suggests them with Use these; it is only a hint. The same fields are on **Add a car**, so a car can be added with its rates in one pass.

## Fleet tracking

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, the **Fleet tracking** tab. Fleet staff have the same map as **Fleet map** in their menu; customer service, Sales and Finance open it from **Find a car** (**Car map**) and field staff under **Map**, read only: every staff member sees where the cars are, and only Admins and fleet staff mark alerts as seen. Every car on the same map as the Live map, with who has it. A car''s page and a booking''s page show **Where the car is** (or **No tracker yet**). Each owner sees the location and trips of their own cars in the owner portal, never the renter or the booking.

1. The four numbers: cars on rent, moving, parked, and open alerts.
2. The map shows each car as its photo in a ring: green moving (the arrow is its heading), yellow engine on, blue parked, orange not reporting. The list beside it has every car with its renter, booking, when it is due back (late in red) and its state.
3. Press a car on the map or in the list for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery, whether the tracker has the car''s power, and the trip under way.
4. **Alerts**: speeding, left Ontario, left your zone, still driving after the return time, low tracker battery, unplugged and not reporting. Each also comes to the bell and, with phone alerts on, under Urgent alerts. Press **Show** to see where, **Seen** when it is handled, or **Mark all as seen**.
5. **Trips by booking**: each booking''s trips, kilometres and top speed (red at the speeding level). Press the last trip to draw its route on the map.

## Pair a tracker with a car

1. A new tracker that reports shows under **Trackers**, "Reporting, not on a car yet". Press **Pair**, choose the car and the install date.
2. Or press **Pair a tracker** and type its device ID (the IMEI or serial number on the tracker).
3. The install date starts the Tracker Fee on the owner''s invoice when the car has none yet. A replacement tracker keeps the car''s first date; the old tracker is taken off by itself.
4. **Remove** takes a tracker off a car (tick "faulty" for a broken one). The Tracker Fee is not changed.

## Tracking settings

Below the trackers: the speeding level (140 km/h), the minutes of grace after the return time (15), the low battery level (20%), the hours before "not reporting" (6), the Ontario alert, and one optional zone (a name, its centre and a radius in km). History keeps a moving car''s position once a minute for 90 days, trips and alerts for 365 days (at most 365: the privacy policy keeps tracker data 12 months).

1. Demo mode (off): simulated cars drive the GTA''s highways here and on the Live map, for a demonstration. Nothing is saved. Turn it off before the trackers go live.
2. **Make the ingest key**: the relay or tracker service signs every batch of positions with it. It is shown once; making a new one stops the old one at once.

> Tip: The Live map shows the same cars with its Fleet layer (tick Fleet).

## Tracker events, evidence and pound flags (release 48)

Below the map on the **Fleet tracking** tab of **Cars**. It is off until the trackers are installed: an Admin turns on **Tracker events** under **Tracker event settings**.

On, each event makes one alert per car, kind and 30 minutes (never a flood), an evidence record, and a notice to the renter and to the car''s owner:

- **Speeding over 180, 220 or 300 km/h**: one record per event, at the highest limit reached, with that limit''s speeding charge of Settings > Program ($500, $1,000 and $2,500 plus HST by default). One event is one charge: 226 km/h is $1,000, not $500 plus $1,000. The renter is told what the Tracker recorded, the charge and the clause (rental agreement 10.5).
- **Over the speeding alert level** (140 km/h) and **harsh driving**: a friendly heads-up to the renter, no charge.
- **Left Ontario**, **driving after the return time**, a tracker unplugged or tampered with: a notice with the clause. No set charge.
- **Left Canada**: urgent, once per crossing. Admins and on-duty Fleet get an alert, an email and a text at once (always on), Fleet gets an urgent To do, and the renter is told that leaving Canada needs written approval (rental agreement 10.1). Leaving Ontario for another province or a state reaches the same people the same way.
- **Driving at night** (off unless you turn it on): staff and the owner only. The agreement sets no curfew.
- **At a pound**: see Pound flags below.

The **Tracker events** table shows each record: when, the car and booking, the speed and the map point, where it came from, how many readings it keeps, its seal (a SHA-256), the charge and the clause, and who was told.

1. To bill a speeding record, press **Charge** on its row (an Admin or Finance). The charge is added to the booking with the evidence record attached, and it is taken from the deposit first.
2. The record goes into the dispute pack by itself, with the notice the renter got.

**Pound flags**: a car whose tracker parks inside a pound lot''s radius for 20 minutes is flagged. Fleet gets an urgent To do and alert, Fleet and Admins an email, and the renter is told to call.

1. Call the lot (its phone and hours are on the flag), then the renter. Keep the receipts.
2. Press **Record the path**: the non-return charge ($1,000) or the theft recovery charge ($1,500) with the tow, impound and storage costs, **Recovered, nothing to charge**, or **Not a pound**. Write what happened.
3. A charge still waits for its other evidence (the final late notice, the receipt) like every fee.

**Pound lots**: the known Ontario lots, with name, address, phone and hours. It starts with the lots the Toronto and Peel police publish.

1. Press **Find the pins from the addresses** once; a lot with no pin cannot flag a car.
2. **Edit** a lot to add its hours, fix its details or type its pin, and tick **I checked these details with the lot**.
3. **Add a lot** for any other pound you know of.

> Note: The renter''s notice about a charge is always sent. The renter can mute the heads-up, and the owner can mute their alerts, in their own notification settings.

## The listing pipeline

Open **Cars** > **Listings**. A draft waiting for review shows Needs review.

1. Each row shows the car, plate, state, photos and the work done on it so far.
2. Press **Start a listing** to begin one for a car that has none.
3. Open a car to review it.

![](/guides/img/admin-09-listings-desktop-970819b6.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 560; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings; pins: 1 53.5 37.0, 2 87.2 21.1, 3 32.6 37.0")

## Review a listing

1. Steps to go live shows four numbered steps: **1 Photos** (how many of the required photos are in, 14 for most cars, 13 for a two-seater with no rear seats), **2 Cover plates**, **3 Review** and **4 Live on the site**. Each says what it needs and has one button to where it is done; the step to do now is in red. A step that stopped (a photo edit or the copy) shows under them with **Retry**.
2. Similar cars on file lists possible duplicates. Press **Not a duplicate** or **Same car**. An open flag does not keep the car off the site; only Same car does.
3. The copy is written by itself from the car''s facts and published when it passes the checks: nothing to type. To change a line, press Change; that field is then locked and kept by every new version.
4. Under Photos, each public photo shows its plate state: Plate not checked, Plate covered or No plate visible.

![](/guides/img/admin-10-listing-review-desktop-352745fd.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1100; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449; pins: 1 20.6 16.6, 2 86.1 47.5, 3 19.9 106.8, 4 74.9 106.8")

## Cover the licence plate

The plates are checked by themselves. Every photo is looked at by the vision model within the day''s free AI share: a plate it finds is blurred so no character can be read (the photo shows Covered automatically, with how sure it was), a photo with no plate is marked No plate visible (No plate seen automatically), and a photo it is not sure of stays Plate not checked for you. While photos wait, the Photos card says how many. A wrong decision: press **Undo** on the photo (the photo as it was comes back, Plate not checked), or **Not a plate: no plate visible** on a cover put where there is no plate.

To cover a plate yourself, press **Cover the plate** on the photo. The editor opens right under it.

1. Check the box over the plate, or press **Suggest the plate**.
2. Drag over a plate to draw a box. Drag a box to move it, or its corner to resize it.
3. The plate is blurred so no character can be read, only over the plate itself, with rounded corners and a soft edge. Nothing is drawn on a plate. A car with no front plate gets no box there. The studio photos Gemini makes have no plate at all: it is taken off cleanly, and a bumper without a plate is left as it is.
4. Press **Save the covered photo**. **Clear the boxes** starts over.
5. No plate in the shot? Press **No plate visible on this photo**.

![](/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-desktop-4219ad93.jpg "desktop; size: 690 703; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449; pins: 1 42.5 83.8, 2 49.6 29.9, 3 4.3 77.4, 4 15.5 83.8, 5 18.1 91.2")

> Tip: The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately. Keyboard: N adds a box, the arrows move it, Shift and the arrows resize it, Delete removes it.

## Publish

1. A real car that is not on the site is a line on To do: press **Set rates and publish**. The daily rate is filled in (the car''s own, or the suggested rate from similar cars or the class); change it if you like and press **Publish now**.
2. On the car itself, the Listing tab has **Publish now**; each open item of its checklist has a button to where it is done.
3. From a listing review: press **Approve and publish**, **Approve, publish later**, or **Send back** with what to fix.

> Watch out: The plate check never holds a car back: a real photo whose plate is not checked stays private (the other photos, or the sample photos, show instead) and goes public by itself once its plate is covered or marked not visible. Listings already live show "Plate not checked" on such photos.

## Photos filed under the wrong shot, and interior windows

1. On the Photos card, each shot lists its photos. A photo filed under the wrong shot: press **Remove** under it, then **Remove it**. The shot is free again: take or pick the right photo. The removed photo is kept privately and the removal is in the history. A live listing''s photos change in the review instead (Reject).
2. Dashboard and seat photos: what shows through the windows is replaced by the studio background when the cut is clean (a quality check: some but not most of the frame seen through, high in the frame, a few clean regions, sharp edges). Otherwise the windows are blurred, and the photo is marked windows blurred. Nothing to do.
3. A car with 2 seats or fewer needs no Rear seats photo.

## A listing without photos yet: sample photos

A car can be listed before its photos are taken. Until then the site shows a sample photo.

1. Submit the listing without photos. The listing copy is still written for you from the car''s details.
2. The car page and the car''s card show a sample photo, captioned "Sample photo", so renters know it is not this car. Staff see "Using sample photos" on the car and in Listings.
3. Publishing does not wait for a plate check: a sample photo has no plate.
4. Add the real photos when they are taken. Once real photos are approved they replace the sample at once; nothing else to do.

## Sample photos

**Settings** > **Sample photos**. The pictures a car shows until its real photos are in.

1. Every body type has a built-in picture (sedan, SUV, truck, van, coupe, hatchback, electric car).
2. Add your own: choose the Body type, and a Make and Model if the photo is of that exact model, pick the Photo, and press **Add the photo**.
3. The most specific photo wins: make and model, then make and body type, then body type. **Turn off** or **Delete** a photo you no longer want.
4. Cars using sample photos lists the cars still waiting for real photos. Each real car showing sample photos is also a line on To do, with **Add photos**.

![](/guides/img/admin-36-sample-photos-desktop-55c64070.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 812; address: carmacars.ca/admin/settings/sample-photos; pins: 4 26.8 28.9")

## Publish now, and new cars published by themselves

Nothing between a new car and the site has to be finished first: the car goes on the site, and what is still open shows on its checklist.

1. **Settings** > **Program**, **Publish new cars automatically** (on by default): a new real car goes on the site by itself as soon as it has its year, make and model and its rates, when it is added with rates, when its rates are saved, when it is added for an owner, or when an owner''s application is approved.
2. Otherwise open the car: its Listing tab says why it is not on the site and has **Publish now**. A car with no rates yet is published with the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults in Program settings); change them later on the Rates tab.
3. Every real car has its listing from the moment it is added, as a draft. It shows in Listings and in Not on the site yet until it is published.
4. An owner''s own application waits for your decision before its car is published by itself; Publish now still works.
5. A car taken off the site by staff, or scheduled for a later date, is never published by itself: press **Publish now**.

## The checklist: what is still open on a listed car

Open items never stop publishing. They show as warnings on the car''s Listing tab and after Publish now.

| Item | What it means |
| --- | --- |
| Paperwork | Ownership permit, registry forms, agreements signed, Forms C and D, upfront payment, registry visit, tracker, safety certificate |
| Insurance | Not on the fleet insurance policy yet: the car can be booked, but not handed over |
| Details | Colour, body, seats, gearbox: the car page leaves out what is missing |
| Photos | No real photos: sample photos stand in. A photo whose plate is not checked stays private until it is |
| No VIN yet | A car added by its plate alone: add the VIN when you have it |
| Possible duplicate | An open flag in Similar cars. Only Same car keeps the car off the site |
| Owner terms | The management fee (Revenue Share) and fees not set: a request uses the owner''s terms or the standard grid |

## The fleet policy rule at handover

A program owner''s car is listed and can be requested, offered and paid for while its paperwork is open. It is never handed over until the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet insurance policy.

- Staff see a warning on a request and an offer for a car not on the policy yet.
- The handover refuses the car until the insurer''s confirmation is recorded (Owners and onboarding). The field app says so on the job.
- Only real states keep a car off the site: retired, left the program, out of service, Turo only, bookings turned off, a self-managed owner in arrears, or a paused listing.

## Cars on sample photos

**Cars**, **Listings** ends with **Cars on sample photos**: each real car whose page still shows sample photos, with its newest handover photos (the check-in and check-out photos field staff take).

1. Where a handover photographed the car, press **Use the handover photos**. They go into the car''s listing as if taken on the capture screen.
2. When every required shot is there, the listing is submitted: Gemini makes each photo from the original, then the listing waits for your review like any other.
3. A car with no handover photos yet gets them at its next handover, or press **Start a listing** and take them.

> Good to know: The listing photos use no Cloudflare image processing: Gemini makes every photo and the site makes the sizes.

## A car''s registration and documents

Open the car, then **Owner & documents**. The **Registration** card:

1. Correct the **VIN** (it is checked: 17 characters, the check digit, not on another car; decoded again for the body style and trim), the **Year** and the **Body style**.
2. Type the **Ontario permit number** and the date the **Plate sticker expires**. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before; save the new date after the renewal and the task closes.
3. Under **Documents**, choose the kind (**Ownership permit**, Safety Standards Certificate, owner''s insurance, other), pick the photo or PDF and press **Upload**. The ownership permit clears that item of the owner''s checklist.
4. For the **Safety Standards Certificate**, also type its number, the date it was issued and the date it expires. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before it expires; upload the new certificate with its dates and the task closes. It is a document on the car, not a service record, and nothing is billed to the owner.
5. **Add a car** takes the ownership permit and the Safety Standards Certificate too, under **Documents (optional)**.

## A car added under the wrong owner

Open the car, Overview, **Who supplies the car**, **Move to another owner**. Choose the owner, or **CarmaCars (owner not known yet)**: the car becomes a company car, with no owner schedule or terms.

- The car''s unsigned owner application and vehicle schedule are withdrawn (kept in the history), and its draft owner invoices are deleted. Nobody is notified.
- It is refused once anything for the car is signed, issued, paid or on a statement.

### The VIN from the car, not typed

Every VIN field (Add a car, Add a car for an owner, the car''s **Registration**, **Start a listing**) has **Scan the barcode** and **Photo of the VIN**. Scan the barcode in the driver''s door frame or at the bottom of the windshield: the phone''s camera reads it by itself. Or take a photo of the VIN plate or sticker: the barcode in it is read first, else the photo is read for the printed VIN. The VIN is checked (17 characters, the check digit; I, O and Q become 1 and 0) and decoded as when you type it. Check it against the car before saving.

### Photos in any order

**Add photos** on the listing takes any number of photos at once from the camera roll. Each is sorted to its shot by itself (front three-quarter, sides, rear, dashboard, seats and the rest); a shot that already has its photo sends the new one to the extra photos, so nothing is replaced by accident. The shots are a guide, not a rule: a listing is complete with 10 photos that can go on the site and one outside photo for the cover. Outside photos get the studio background: the car is cropped to its edges and placed big in the frame with its wheels on the floor and a soft shadow under the tyres, and any corner watermark or caption beside the car is left out. Inside and detail photos are kept as taken; when one has a watermark, a logo or caption text on it, the edge with the mark is cut off by itself, and a photo whose mark cannot be cut off (one in the middle) stays off the site until you replace it. **Cover the plate** opens on every outside photo with the plate box suggested; check it and save.

Outside photos made before the newest framing (the car small in the frame, or without the model''s name behind it) are made again with **Frame the outside photos again** above the photos of the listing, then **Yes, frame again**. The cover and the main outside views get the model''s name lettered behind the car, as on the sample photos (for example CLA, C CLASS, AMG GT). The photos leave the site until their plates are checked again: the plate box is suggested on the new photos; check each and cover it. On a published listing each goes back on the site once its plate is checked.

## Showroom photos

Outside photos go in the CarmaCars showroom by themselves. When a real photographed room is stored (dealership or studio photos licensed for commercial use, fetched once from Wikimedia Commons with their author and licence kept), the car stands in it: about 70% of the width, its wheels on the room''s floor, a soft shadow and a faint reflection under it, its light matched to the room, and no sign or lettering on the real wall. Program settings > Listings has the switch (Photographed showroom rooms, on), the car''s width and the cut-out quality floor: a cut-out that is not clean enough (pieces, a blurry or ragged edge) is never placed in a room, the real photo is used instead (its plate covered as usual) and the photo says so. Without a stored room it is the drawn dark showroom: a simple dark dealership with linear lights in the ceiling, a slatted wood wall between two light strips with a big lit CarmaCars sign, and a polished dark floor with the car''s reflection and a shadow under each tyre. Every angle of a car is in the same room, and the cover has the model''s name in metal letters on the wall under the sign. The image model may relight the car or turn it slightly; a photo that shows another car, model or colour is not used. **Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings** has the switch (Showroom photos, on), the image model that makes the photos look photographed, and its daily limit. Past the limit, or when the image model is not available, the site makes the showroom itself for free, and the photo says why under it.

- A car whose photos were made on the black studio: press **Apply showroom to this car** above its photos, then **Yes, apply**.
- Every car at once: **Listings** > **Showroom photos** > **Apply showroom to every car**, then **Yes, every car**.
- Under a photo in the showroom: **Redo** makes it again, **Back to the original** puts back the version before the showroom.

A car that stays where it was keeps its plate check. When the image model made the photo, check the plate again: the photo is off the site until you do. Photos made in the first showroom are made again in the new one with **Apply showroom to this car** or **Apply showroom to every car**.

## Failed photos

The site makes the photo sizes itself: the image service is asked only to cut the car out (**Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings**: the switch to let the image service make every photo step is off). When the image service is busy or over its allowance, the photo still goes on the site from the original and is made again later. A listing marked Failed has **Retry failed photos** in its note; **Retry failed photos** at the top does every listing. They are made again a few at a time, and the listing leaves Failed when they are done.

## The primary photo is always the front exterior (release 43)

The first photo of every car on the site, in the cards, the feeds and the Marketplace kit is its exterior at the standard angle (front three-quarter, in the dark showroom). An inside photo is never ahead of an outside one, and the cover mark follows by itself whenever photos are added, made again or reordered.

- **Primary photo is not exterior** is a flag and a filter in **Cars** > **Vehicles**: it marks a car whose first photo is an inside one because its best outside photo is not on the site yet, or it has none. Add or approve an outside photo and the flag clears by itself.
- **Redo photos with Gemini** on the car page makes every photo of the car again from its original with Gemini, and generates its missing angles. A photo Gemini cannot make well stays off the site, flagged. It needs the image model switched on in Program settings, Listings.
- The same press checks the car''s **Other detail** photos again: an outside view filed there is moved to the outside photos (the front three-quarter becomes the first photo) and made in the showroom. This is what clears the flag on a car that showed nothing to redo.
- Every outside photo has the same room behind it: Gemini replaces the whole background from the original photo.
- Every plate is blurred; nothing is drawn on it and there is no text anywhere else. Inside photos stay sharp from front to back.
- **Redo every car with Gemini** (Listings, Showroom photos; Admin and Fleet) is the same as **Redo every car** on the Photo standard card.

## The photo standard: every photo made by Gemini (release 45)

Every listing photo is made by Gemini from the original photo, never from a cut-out. Outside photos get their whole background replaced by the CarmaCars showroom, with nothing of the place they were taken in left. Inside photos are cleaned up (no clutter) and sharp from front to back. Every plate is blurred so no character can be read; no plate is drawn and there is no text anywhere else on the photo.

- **The check.** A second Gemini look compares each new photo with the original and refuses it when the old background shows, the car is warped, another colour or model, has parts added or missing, a plate can be read, or there is text anywhere. The site also checks the edges are the dark showroom. A refused photo is made again, twice; then it stays off the site and is counted as flagged.
- **Missing angles.** Every car shows the standard set: front three-quarter, front, side profile, rear three-quarter, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats and trunk. An angle the car has no photo of is generated by Gemini from the car''s own photos, in the same showroom, and marked **AI generated** on the listing (staff only). A real photo of that angle replaces it by itself.
- **The order.** The front three-quarter is always first, then the other outside photos, then the inside ones. A car whose first photo would be an inside one shows no photos and cannot be published until it has an outside one; its front three-quarter is generated first.
- **By itself.** Every 5 minutes the job brings the next cars to the standard, newest listed cars first, until every car is done (about a day for the whole fleet). A photo already at the standard is never made again unless you ask. **Program settings** > **Listings**: the daily Gemini limit (2000 calls), the calls kept for new uploads (50) and the switch.
- **Listings** > **Photo standard** (Admin and Fleet) shows each car: photos at the standard out of all, AI angles, flagged photos and the last run. **Redo this car now** makes all of its photos again at once; **Redo every car** makes every photo of every car again. **Redo photos with Gemini** on a car page does the same as Redo this car now.

## The first photo: plain, with a model, or a flyer

On a listing, under **First photo**, choose what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit. Switch any time; the other photos stay as they are.

- **Plain car**: the cover photo as it is (the default).
- **With a model**: a car-show photo made by the image model, with a fully clothed adult model beside the car. It needs the image model; until it is made (or when the image model is not there) the plain cover shows, and the listing says why.
- **Flyer**: the cover photo with a band like a printed flyer: the car, the price a day from its live rates, the call to action, a badge and the logo. When the price, the words or the cover photo change, it is made again by itself within 10 minutes; the plain cover shows meanwhile.

**Make it again** makes the chosen one again. The words of the flyer and the description of the model are in **Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings** (First photo "flyer" and First photo "with a model"); {car}, {price}, {weekly} and {monthly} are filled for each car.

## Marketing photos in other scenes

For Marketplace and social posts, a car''s outside photos can be made again in other scenes. The website keeps its own photos in the dark showroom: a marketing set never replaces them.

1. On a listing, under **Marketing photos**, choose a scene, or **Mix: a different scene on each photo**, and press **Make the marketing set**.
2. The copies show as they are made. The dark showroom and the plain white studio are made by the site when the image model is not there; the photographic scenes (a bright showroom, a city street at night, the Toronto waterfront, a parking garage, Highway, a scenic road, Brick building) need the image model, and say so on the copy when it is not there.
3. **Download (ZIP)** takes the set; the Marketplace kit''s **With scenes (ZIP)** takes the same set.

**Settings** > **Program settings** > **Marketing scenes** lists the scenes. A scene made in a real place has a photo of that place: Brick building picks its photo by itself: the widest outside photo, as taken, of the shareholders'' own cars. To use another, press **Change the reference photo** and pick one (the shareholders'' cars'' photos come first), or upload one. The scenes'' names and words are in the **Marketing scenes** setting.

## Extra photos

A photo that fits no shot is an extra photo. Under the shots, **Extra outside photos** (put on the studio background) and **Extra inside and detail photos** (touched up) each take any number at once. They count toward the 10 photos, get the same plate check, and come after the standard shots on the car''s page.

1. In the review, **Extra photos, in their order on the car page** lists them.
2. Drag a photo by its handle (⋮⋮), or press **Earlier** or **Later**.
3. Press **Save the order**.

## Fix a cut-out

When the background removal cuts badly (a mirror or a wheel missing, background left beside the car), press **Edit the cut-out** under the outside photo.

1. **Cut-out** shows the car over the photo as taken, shown faintly. Choose **Erase** and brush over what should go, or **Restore** and brush over what the cut-out took off. Set **Brush size** and **Zoom**; when zoomed, **Move the view** pans. **Undo** takes back the last stroke.
2. **On the studio** shows the car on the studio background. Drag the car to move it and use **Size** to make it larger or smaller. **Centre and full size** puts it back.
3. Press **Save as a new version**. The photo is made again in about a minute; the version before and the photo as taken are kept. **Reset to the automatic cut-out** starts again from the automatic one.

> Good to know: If the car did not move, the plate check carries over: a photo marked no plate visible stays so, and a covered plate is covered again on the new photo when the review is open. If the car moved, check the plate again. A photo made before cut-outs were kept shows **Make the cut-out** first; the editor opens by itself when it is ready.

Every photo also gets a light touch-up by itself (exposure, levels, a little contrast and colour, mild sharpening), never enough to change the paint colour or hide a scratch. Turn it off for one photo with **Use original colours** under it (the photo is made again; approve it again), or for every photo in Admin > Settings > **Program settings** (Listings) with **Auto-enhance listing photos**. The photo as uploaded is always kept.
## Import photos from a Google Drive link

The owner often hands over a car''s photos as a public Google Drive folder, or one big folder with a folder per make and then per car. You do not download them: paste the link.

**One car.** On the car''s listing, under the capture, **Import photos from a Google Drive link**. Paste the folder link (shared with Anyone with the link) and press **Import the photos**. Every photo in the folder, and in the folders inside it, is added to this car as if you had pressed Add photos: each is sorted to its shot (else filed as an extra photo, in file-name order), put on the studio background and checked for its plate. The box under the link, **Submit the listing for processing when its photos are in**, is on by default.

**Many cars.** **Cars** > **Import photos from Drive** (a button on Vehicles). Paste the top folder''s link and press **Read the folder**. The page walks every folder and proposes a car for each folder that holds photos, from the year, make, model, colour and plate in the folder names (the make folder above counts; 01 Motors partner cars come first). Check the table: tick or untick **Import**, change the car in the list (the likely cars come first), leave out a folder with **Do not import this folder**. A line marked **Check this one** matched two alike cars. Then press **Import N photos from M folders**.

1. The page follows the import by itself. You can leave it and come back: it runs in the background.
2. The end shows the summary: imported, skipped and failed, and why for each (a file over 15 MB, a file that is not a photo, the same photo already on the car, a folder not shared).
3. **Try the failed photos again** takes only the ones that failed. Pressing Import on the same link again never adds a photo twice: a Drive file already on the car is skipped, and so is the same picture under another name. A photo you took off the car can be imported again.

> Good to know: JPG, PNG, HEIC and WebP only (HEIC and WebP are made JPEG first). At most 15 MB a photo, 600 photos, 400 folders and 4 GB in one import. Drive is asked politely, one photo at a time; a big import takes a while.

> Good to know: Without a key, Drive shows only the first 50 files of a folder on its public page; a folder with more is read in full when Drive allows it. In **Settings**, the **Photo import from Google Drive** box takes a Google API key with the Drive API on (after it is saved only its last 4 characters are shown, and it is never written to the change log): with it, folders of any size are read and photos download without Drive''s warning pages.

## Test bookings and deleting a car

1. On a booking made only to try the site, press **Mark as a test booking** (Admins only; the reason is optional). **Make it a real booking again** undoes it.
2. A car whose bookings are all test bookings can be deleted: the test bookings and their test payments go with it, and a copy is kept in the archive of deleted requests.
3. A car with a real booking cannot be deleted.

## Pickup from owner and return to owner (release 28)

On a car''s page, **Pickup from owner and return to owner** records the car''s condition when CarmaCars picks it up from its owner or gives it back: the date and time, km, fuel, many photos at once with the suggested angles, and notes. **Add photos** adds more to a record later. The owner sees these records read only on the car''s page in their portal. They are the baseline condition for any dispute.

## Incident cards (release 34)
**Cars** > **Vehicles** > **Incident cards** prints the card for each car: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, the support number from Settings, a roadside number when there is one, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. Open a car and press **Incident card** to print only that car; on the list, **Print all cars** prints them all, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks, ready to laminate. Under Fleet insurance policy press **Add the policy** (the insurer, the policy number, the dates, the named insured, the roadside number on the slip) and choose the uploaded slip if you have one: it is printed as it is, otherwise the fields are. The card never shows a premium. Fleet staff print the same cards from their portal.

## Field jobs, shifts and who gets a job

**Cars**, then **Field jobs**, is the board Fleet uses, with every action Fleet has. Shifts are paused (release 50): none is published by itself (Program settings, Shifts published by themselves, off), the open shifts nobody claimed were cancelled, and the claimed ones stay with their jobs. **Publish shifts** still adds one by hand. A job goes on a shift somebody works first (a person on it who has passed the academy basics), else on an open shift; a job on a shift nobody works moves within the hour once a worked shift is near. A job with no shift near stays unassigned, and those with nobody to work them give Fleet one To do, **field job(s) have no shift anybody works**. Every job still goes on a shift and to its person (Who gets an automatic job: the least busy): a shift of its own day first; on a day without one, a pickup goes on the shift before it and a return on the shift after it; work not done when a shift ends moves to the next shift every hour. Switched back on, shifts are published by themselves from the shift template (one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 every second day by default, 14 days ahead, only forward from the latest shift), with a shift of its own for any handover or return no shift covers, and a shift you cancel is not published again. Field staff take them. **Missing check-in and check-out**, on the same page, lists every past rental without its photos and readings, with **Give to field staff**. Jobs go on shifts, not on people: each job is put on the shift covering its time (or that day''s), whoever holds the shift does it (several people share the jobs, least busy first), a shift nobody holds keeps its jobs for whoever claims it, and work lands only on days with shifts (work due on a day without shifts moves to the day before, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day; the booking''s own times never change). A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning on the board and on the booking. **To a shift** moves a job to another shift. You can give a job to a field person on a shift that day or to an Admin, take it off with **Unassign** (tick **Tell them** to let them know), and an Admin who holds a job opens it on the field portal. A person who has not passed the academy cannot be given a job or take a shift. A shift with jobs and nobody on it within 24 hours alerts Fleet and the Admins once.


### Shifts in your Google Calendar (release 50)

At the bottom of **Field jobs**, **Add shifts, townhalls and interviews to Google Calendar** gives you a private calendar link with every field shift, 14 days back to 60 days ahead: the day, the start and end (Toronto time), who claimed it or Open, the tasks on it and a link back to it. It also has the weekly townhall (the next 8 meetings) and every booked interview call with its time, the applicant''s first name, the role and the call link. No email is sent.

1. Press **Make my calendar link**.
2. Press **Add to Google Calendar**, then **Add** in Google. Or **Copy link** and add it in another calendar app by URL.
3. Google refreshes a subscribed calendar on its own schedule, every few hours, so a change can take that long to show.
4. Keep the link to yourself. **Regenerate link** makes a new one and stops the old one; **Turn off** stops it.

## Every view generated from the car''s photos (release 47)

Every car shows nine generated views in the order of the sample photos: front three-quarter (always first, the cover), side profile, rear three-quarter, front, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats and trunk. Gemini makes each car from references; the site puts it on the same dealership background, so every car stands in the same room.

- **What Gemini is sent.** The car''s listing photos (its exact colour, trim and wheels); when it has none of that side (outside or inside), its newest check-in and check-out photos instead (only as references: they are never shown on the site). Then the sample view of that angle (for the camera position only) and the stock photo of the model. Gemini makes the car alone on a flat key colour; it never draws the room. Plates taken off, no text, no logos added.
- **The check.** A second Gemini look compares the result with the real photos (same car, colour, wheels and trim, nothing warped, not a render) and with the angle. A refused view is made again, twice, told what was wrong; still refused, it is flagged (release 50: only views that passed are on the site).
- **The real photos.** They stay in the car''s record and on the Admin car page, marked as they were; the site shows the generated view of an angle in place of the real one only once it has passed. Generated views are marked **AI generated** for staff only.
- **By itself.** Every 5 minutes the job takes the front three-quarter of every car first (newest listed first), then the other angles, within the daily Gemini limit (about a day for the whole fleet). **Program settings** > **Listings**: the switch for the generated views.
- **Listings** > **Photo standard** shows each car''s **Generated set** (views made out of nine, being made, flagged, and "from check-in photos" when those were used). **Redo this car now** and **Redo every car** make the generated views again too; the views on the site stay until the new ones pass.
- **Showroom background plates** (**Program settings**, Admin): the room for front, side and rear views. Gemini made them once and a second look confirmed each looks like a real photo. Upload a real photo of a showroom (empty floor in the middle, no people, cars, signs or logos) to replace one or all three; **Make a new one** has Gemini make it again.

## The studio set: every car photographed the same way (release 48)

Every car gets the same nine views, as if all were photographed in one studio on one day: the same angle, camera height, lens and framing for each view, the car facing the same way as the sample covers (the front three-quarter and the side with the nose to the left), plates taken off cleanly, the car itself unchanged.

- The scene: every car stands in the same scene so the covers line up as you scroll: the dark dealership with the CarmaCars sign on the wall by default, with the model''s name on the wall behind the car on the first photo. **Program settings** > **Listings**: the scene for every car. On a car, **Studio photos** > **Scene** picks another for that car only (highway, brick building and the other marketing scenes).
- No photo of an angle? Gemini makes it from the car''s other photos. A car with no photo at all gets its outside views from the stock photo of its model, in its own colour.
- One set everywhere: once a car''s front three-quarter is made, the site shows only its made views, in the standard order, the front three-quarter first: the same photo on the home page, the search cards, the car page, the partner feeds and in the sitemap. The real photos stay in the car''s record.
- The check: Gemini checks each view against the car''s own photos: the same car (model, colour, wheels), the right angle, the nose the right way, the old background gone (the site also measures it), no readable plate. Smaller doubts (framing, a part the photos do not show) stop only the first two tries.
- On a car, **Studio photos** shows each view beside the car''s own photos of that angle, marked **AI**. **Make again** makes one view again; **Take off the site** and **Put on the site**.
- **Listings** > **Photo standard** shows the fleet''s progress: views made out of all, cars with their studio cover, and about how many days are left at Gemini''s daily limit.
- Marketing set: **Make the marketing set** uses the studio views (the same angle and cover as the site) in the scene you choose, plus up to three lifestyle shots: an adult model with the car, styled like a luxury car advert, always fully dressed and tasteful. Each is marked **AI**; tick **In the ZIP** for the photos you want in a post. A lifestyle shot Gemini declines is skipped.
- Background plates (**Program settings**, Admin): one set per scene. Choose the scene, then upload a real photo of the place to replace one or all three.

## Studio renders first (release 48)

- Every car gets the full studio set made from its own photos: same colour, wheels and trim, the same framing for every car.
- On the site the views come first, in the sample photos'' order: front three-quarter (the cover), side profile, rear three-quarter, front, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats, trunk. Up to six of the car''s real outside photos follow, each cut out on the same dealership background. The real photos themselves stay in the car''s record.
- A render goes live as soon as it passes the photo check. There is no approval step. To change one, open the car, **Studio photos**, then **Make again** or **Take off the site**. Taking the side profile off makes the next render the cover.
- The car page says **Rendered photos** above the gallery, with **See its real photos**.
- New cars get their renders by themselves. To do every published car now: **Listings**, **Photo standard**, **Render every published car**. The line beside it shows how many cars are done. It works within the image model''s daily limit.
- When a car''s set is live, the owner gets an email and an alert ("Your car has new studio photos"), and Fleet gets "Studio photos live" in the next digest. Look the photos over.
- The Cars filter lists one model per family (for example CLA-Class or 3 Series). The trim shows on the car. A car whose model family is not recognised is listed in **Data health**: fix the typo, or ask for the family to be added.

## One look: studio renders only (release 50)

- Once a car has a studio view that passed, the site shows its studio views: the car page, the cards, the landing and area pages, the partner feeds, the social preview image and the car picture in emails. The car''s own photos are shown only cut out on the studio background.
- The studio (R50 hotfix 2): the site checks that the background is one flat key colour and the whole car is in the frame, before anything else is paid. Then Gemini checks the car, the view, the way the nose points and the plates against the real photos. Then the site cuts the car out and puts it on the dealership background with the CarmaCars sign, at its view''s size and place. The background is one image, exactly the same for every view of every car (no car name on the wall).
- The views are exactly the sample photos'' angles, in the same order: front three-quarter (the cover), side, rear three-quarter, front, rear, dashboard, seats, wheel. A view the car has no photo of is made by Gemini from the car''s other photos (its listing photos, else its check-in and check-out photos), the same paint, rims and trim. Then up to six of the car''s real outside photos follow, each cut out on the same background. A refused view is made again, told why, after 20 minutes, then an hour; after three tries it is flagged with the reasons on **Photo standard**.
- Home, heroes and sample cards: where a section or a card shows a sample car, a real car takes its place only as a cutout (the car alone on the section''s own picture, or on the studio background on a card), never its full photo with its background.
- The cost guard: Each Gemini image counts in the daily photo budget (Program settings). One view gets at most 3 image calls a day. When the last 24 hours took more than 8 image calls for each view that passed, the studio pauses for a day and the Admins get an alert. **Photo standard** shows the calls, the spend and the pause; clear **Listing photo r48 paused at** in Program settings to start again sooner. A Gemini check that gives no verdict is recorded with its cause (the error Google sent, an answer cut off, or no answer in time).
- No view passed yet: the car shows its photos as before (its own photos, or the sample photos with their caption), never the empty studio. Its own photos stay in the car''s record, for the views and for staff.
- **Studio grid.** **Listings** > **Photo standard** > **Studio grid** shows every published car''s views side by side, with **Live**, **Being made**, **Gate refused** or **Flagged** and the reasons, so a view that drifts from the others is easy to spot. Use **Make again** on the car''s **Studio photos** to redo one..

## Add old photos
**Cars** > **Check-in visits** > **Add old photos** is the same screen field staff, Fleet and customer service use: photos of an earlier check-in or check-out onto its booking, for every booking picked up or returned in the last `old_photos_days` (60), whoever handled it. One booking at a time, or **A pile of photos** sorted by the time each was taken and the plate read from it. Each photo shows on the photo report as "added later by" the person with its capture time; nobody outside the team is told. The windows are in Settings > Program settings > Field jobs and handovers: `old_photos_days`, `old_photos_match_hours`, `old_photos_group_minutes`.
',
  '<p class="gd-p">Vehicles is the fleet. Listings turns a car into a page on carmacars.ca in four steps: photos, covered plates, a review, and live on the site.</p><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-vehicles" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Vehicles</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b></p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Filter by status; More filters has who supplies the car, retired cars and the mode. Each row shows the plate, class, owner, mode, status, listing and daily rate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Search by plate, model or owner. <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Rates for many cars</b> changes the rates of many cars at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open a car for its tabs: Overview, Rates, Fees and coverage, Calendar, Listing, and Owner, documents, tracker. The Tracker card links to Fleet tracking.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/vehicles</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/900"><img src="/guides/img/admin-08-vehicles-desktop-46461f49.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="900"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:74.3%;top:31.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:37.5%;top:24.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:48.6%;top:52.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-set-a-car-s-rates-and-kilometres" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Set a car&#39;s rates and kilometres</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, then the <b class="gd-ui">Rates</b> tab. Everything on it saves together, in one step.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Type the four rates. Only the daily rate is needed: an empty weekend rate is the daily rate, an empty weekly rate is 6 days at the daily rate, and an empty monthly rate is 22 days.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Kilometres: keep <b class="gd-ui">Use the defaults</b> (the kilometres a day in Settings, Kilometre choices, and the extra kilometre rate in Fee defaults for the car&#39;s class), or choose <b class="gd-ui">Custom for this car</b> and type them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Check the deposit (the class default is filled in), and the delivery and pickup fees: each is one way, an empty pickup fee is the delivery fee, and 0 means not offered.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Read What renters pay under the fields: real prices for a weekend, a few weekdays, a week and a month, worked out the way bookings are priced. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the rates</b>.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Rate</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Daily rate</td><td>A price per day, for each day that starts on a Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday or Thursday</td></tr><tr><td>Weekend rate</td><td>A price per day, not for the whole weekend: each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday. Friday 10 am to Sunday 10 am is 2 days at this rate; Sunday to Monday is a daily day</td></tr><tr><td>Weekly rate</td><td>The price for 7 days. Rentals of 7 to 29 days cost this for each 7 days, counted by the day. A 1 to 6 day rental never costs more</td></tr><tr><td>Monthly rate</td><td>The price for 30 days. A 7 to 29 day rental never costs more</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol" start="5"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Lead-time pricing for this car, below the rates: <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> (the tiers there), <b class="gd-ui">Off for this car</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Its own tiers</b> (a table like the one in Program settings). Press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Price limits</b>, beside them: the lowest and highest daily rate the owner accepts. <b class="gd-ui">This car</b> sets the car&#39;s own; the owner&#39;s line sets them for every car of that owner (a car&#39;s own come first, field by field). Empty is no limit. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save price limits</b>. Owners set the same limits in their portal.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Price limits hold the rental a day (after lead-time pricing, the non-refundable discount, a discount, a promo code or a price typed by hand; never fees, add-ons or tax) between the minimum and the maximum: one line, &quot;Minimum daily rate for this car&quot; or &quot;Maximum daily rate for this car&quot;, brings it back. Never on an Owner Booking or a booking billed to an insurer. To price one request outside them, open its review screen, <b class="gd-ui">More options</b>, tick <b class="gd-ui">Allow a price outside the car&#39;s price limits (Admin only)</b> and say why: it is kept on the booking and in the audit log. Untick it and the limits apply again.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A problem shows on its own field, in words, as you type. When similar cars have rates, a line suggests them with Use these; it is only a hint. The same fields are on <b class="gd-ui">Add a car</b>, so a car can be added with its rates in one pass.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-fleet-tracking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fleet tracking</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Fleet tracking</b> tab. Fleet staff have the same map as <b class="gd-ui">Fleet map</b> in their menu; customer service, Sales and Finance open it from <b class="gd-ui">Find a car</b> (<b class="gd-ui">Car map</b>) and field staff under <b class="gd-ui">Map</b>, read only: every staff member sees where the cars are, and only Admins and fleet staff mark alerts as seen. Every car on the same map as the Live map, with who has it. A car&#39;s page and a booking&#39;s page show <b class="gd-ui">Where the car is</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">No tracker yet</b>). Each owner sees the location and trips of their own cars in the owner portal, never the renter or the booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The four numbers: cars on rent, moving, parked, and open alerts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The map shows each car as its photo in a ring: green moving (the arrow is its heading), yellow engine on, blue parked, orange not reporting. The list beside it has every car with its renter, booking, when it is due back (late in red) and its state.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press a car on the map or in the list for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery, whether the tracker has the car&#39;s power, and the trip under way.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Alerts</b>: speeding, left Ontario, left your zone, still driving after the return time, low tracker battery, unplugged and not reporting. Each also comes to the bell and, with phone alerts on, under Urgent alerts. Press <b class="gd-ui">Show</b> to see where, <b class="gd-ui">Seen</b> when it is handled, or <b class="gd-ui">Mark all as seen</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Trips by booking</b>: each booking&#39;s trips, kilometres and top speed (red at the speeding level). Press the last trip to draw its route on the map.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-pair-a-tracker-with-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pair a tracker with a car</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A new tracker that reports shows under <b class="gd-ui">Trackers</b>, &quot;Reporting, not on a car yet&quot;. Press <b class="gd-ui">Pair</b>, choose the car and the install date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Or press <b class="gd-ui">Pair a tracker</b> and type its device ID (the IMEI or serial number on the tracker).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The install date starts the Tracker Fee on the owner&#39;s invoice when the car has none yet. A replacement tracker keeps the car&#39;s first date; the old tracker is taken off by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes a tracker off a car (tick &quot;faulty&quot; for a broken one). The Tracker Fee is not changed.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-tracking-settings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tracking settings</h2><p class="gd-p">Below the trackers: the speeding level (140 km/h), the minutes of grace after the return time (15), the low battery level (20%), the hours before &quot;not reporting&quot; (6), the Ontario alert, and one optional zone (a name, its centre and a radius in km). History keeps a moving car&#39;s position once a minute for 90 days, trips and alerts for 365 days (at most 365: the privacy policy keeps tracker data 12 months).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Demo mode (off): simulated cars drive the GTA&#39;s highways here and on the Live map, for a demonstration. Nothing is saved. Turn it off before the trackers go live.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Make the ingest key</b>: the relay or tracker service signs every batch of positions with it. It is shown once; making a new one stops the old one at once.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The Live map shows the same cars with its Fleet layer (tick Fleet).</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-tracker-events-evidence-and-pound-flags-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tracker events, evidence and pound flags (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">Below the map on the <b class="gd-ui">Fleet tracking</b> tab of <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>. It is off until the trackers are installed: an Admin turns on <b class="gd-ui">Tracker events</b> under <b class="gd-ui">Tracker event settings</b>.</p><p class="gd-p">On, each event makes one alert per car, kind and 30 minutes (never a flood), an evidence record, and a notice to the renter and to the car&#39;s owner:</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Speeding over 180, 220 or 300 km/h</b>: one record per event, at the highest limit reached, with that limit&#39;s speeding charge of Settings &gt; Program ($500, $1,000 and $2,500 plus HST by default). One event is one charge: 226 km/h is $1,000, not $500 plus $1,000. The renter is told what the Tracker recorded, the charge and the clause (rental agreement 10.5).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Over the speeding alert level</b> (140 km/h) and <b class="gd-ui">harsh driving</b>: a friendly heads-up to the renter, no charge.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Left Ontario</b>, <b class="gd-ui">driving after the return time</b>, a tracker unplugged or tampered with: a notice with the clause. No set charge.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Left Canada</b>: urgent, once per crossing. Admins and on-duty Fleet get an alert, an email and a text at once (always on), Fleet gets an urgent To do, and the renter is told that leaving Canada needs written approval (rental agreement 10.1). Leaving Ontario for another province or a state reaches the same people the same way.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Driving at night</b> (off unless you turn it on): staff and the owner only. The agreement sets no curfew.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">At a pound</b>: see Pound flags below.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">The <b class="gd-ui">Tracker events</b> table shows each record: when, the car and booking, the speed and the map point, where it came from, how many readings it keeps, its seal (a SHA-256), the charge and the clause, and who was told.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">To bill a speeding record, press <b class="gd-ui">Charge</b> on its row (an Admin or Finance). The charge is added to the booking with the evidence record attached, and it is taken from the deposit first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The record goes into the dispute pack by itself, with the notice the renter got.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Pound flags</b>: a car whose tracker parks inside a pound lot&#39;s radius for 20 minutes is flagged. Fleet gets an urgent To do and alert, Fleet and Admins an email, and the renter is told to call.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Call the lot (its phone and hours are on the flag), then the renter. Keep the receipts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Record the path</b>: the non-return charge ($1,000) or the theft recovery charge ($1,500) with the tow, impound and storage costs, <b class="gd-ui">Recovered, nothing to charge</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Not a pound</b>. Write what happened.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A charge still waits for its other evidence (the final late notice, the receipt) like every fee.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Pound lots</b>: the known Ontario lots, with name, address, phone and hours. It starts with the lots the Toronto and Peel police publish.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Find the pins from the addresses</b> once; a lot with no pin cannot flag a car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> a lot to add its hours, fix its details or type its pin, and tick <b class="gd-ui">I checked these details with the lot</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a lot</b> for any other pound you know of.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Note</span><div>The renter&#39;s notice about a charge is always sent. The renter can mute the heads-up, and the owner can mute their alerts, in their own notification settings.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-listing-pipeline" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The listing pipeline</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>. A draft waiting for review shows Needs review.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each row shows the car, plate, state, photos and the work done on it so far.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b> to begin one for a car that has none.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open a car to review it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/560"><img src="/guides/img/admin-09-listings-desktop-970819b6.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="560"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:53.5%;top:37%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:87.2%;top:21.1%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:32.6%;top:37%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-review-a-listing" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Review a listing</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Steps to go live shows four numbered steps: <b class="gd-ui">1 Photos</b> (how many of the required photos are in, 14 for most cars, 13 for a two-seater with no rear seats), <b class="gd-ui">2 Cover plates</b>, <b class="gd-ui">3 Review</b> and <b class="gd-ui">4 Live on the site</b>. Each says what it needs and has one button to where it is done; the step to do now is in red. A step that stopped (a photo edit or the copy) shows under them with <b class="gd-ui">Retry</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Similar cars on file lists possible duplicates. Press <b class="gd-ui">Not a duplicate</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Same car</b>. An open flag does not keep the car off the site; only Same car does.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The copy is written by itself from the car&#39;s facts and published when it passes the checks: nothing to type. To change a line, press Change; that field is then locked and kept by every new version.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Under Photos, each public photo shows its plate state: Plate not checked, Plate covered or No plate visible.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1100"><img src="/guides/img/admin-10-listing-review-desktop-352745fd.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1100"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.6%;top:16.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:86.1%;top:47.5%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.9%;top:100%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:74.9%;top:100%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-cover-the-licence-plate" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cover the licence plate</h2><p class="gd-p">The plates are checked by themselves. Every photo is looked at by the vision model within the day&#39;s free AI share: a plate it finds is blurred so no character can be read (the photo shows Covered automatically, with how sure it was), a photo with no plate is marked No plate visible (No plate seen automatically), and a photo it is not sure of stays Plate not checked for you. While photos wait, the Photos card says how many. A wrong decision: press <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> on the photo (the photo as it was comes back, Plate not checked), or <b class="gd-ui">Not a plate: no plate visible</b> on a cover put where there is no plate.</p><p class="gd-p">To cover a plate yourself, press <b class="gd-ui">Cover the plate</b> on the photo. The editor opens right under it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Check the box over the plate, or press <b class="gd-ui">Suggest the plate</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Drag over a plate to draw a box. Drag a box to move it, or its corner to resize it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The plate is blurred so no character can be read, only over the plate itself, with rounded corners and a soft edge. Nothing is drawn on a plate. A car with no front plate gets no box there. The studio photos Gemini makes have no plate at all: it is taken off cleanly, and a bumper without a plate is left as it is.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the covered photo</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Clear the boxes</b> starts over.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">No plate in the shot? Press <b class="gd-ui">No plate visible on this photo</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:690/703"><img src="/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-desktop-4219ad93.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="690" height="703"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:42.5%;top:83.8%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:49.6%;top:29.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:4.3%;top:77.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:15.5%;top:83.8%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:18.1%;top:91.2%" aria-hidden="true">5</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately. Keyboard: N adds a box, the arrows move it, Shift and the arrows resize it, Delete removes it.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-publish" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Publish</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A real car that is not on the site is a line on To do: press <b class="gd-ui">Set rates and publish</b>. The daily rate is filled in (the car&#39;s own, or the suggested rate from similar cars or the class); change it if you like and press <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On the car itself, the Listing tab has <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>; each open item of its checklist has a button to where it is done.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">From a listing review: press <b class="gd-ui">Approve and publish</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Approve, publish later</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Send back</b> with what to fix.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>The plate check never holds a car back: a real photo whose plate is not checked stays private (the other photos, or the sample photos, show instead) and goes public by itself once its plate is covered or marked not visible. Listings already live show &quot;Plate not checked&quot; on such photos.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-photos-filed-under-the-wrong-shot-and-interior-windows" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Photos filed under the wrong shot, and interior windows</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the Photos card, each shot lists its photos. A photo filed under the wrong shot: press <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> under it, then <b class="gd-ui">Remove it</b>. The shot is free again: take or pick the right photo. The removed photo is kept privately and the removal is in the history. A live listing&#39;s photos change in the review instead (Reject).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Dashboard and seat photos: what shows through the windows is replaced by the studio background when the cut is clean (a quality check: some but not most of the frame seen through, high in the frame, a few clean regions, sharp edges). Otherwise the windows are blurred, and the photo is marked windows blurred. Nothing to do.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car with 2 seats or fewer needs no Rear seats photo.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-listing-without-photos-yet-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A listing without photos yet: sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p">A car can be listed before its photos are taken. Until then the site shows a sample photo.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Submit the listing without photos. The listing copy is still written for you from the car&#39;s details.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The car page and the car&#39;s card show a sample photo, captioned &quot;Sample photo&quot;, so renters know it is not this car. Staff see &quot;Using sample photos&quot; on the car and in Listings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Publishing does not wait for a plate check: a sample photo has no plate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add the real photos when they are taken. Once real photos are approved they replace the sample at once; nothing else to do.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sample photos</b>. The pictures a car shows until its real photos are in.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every body type has a built-in picture (sedan, SUV, truck, van, coupe, hatchback, electric car).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Add your own: choose the Body type, and a Make and Model if the photo is of that exact model, pick the Photo, and press <b class="gd-ui">Add the photo</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The most specific photo wins: make and model, then make and body type, then body type. <b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Delete</b> a photo you no longer want.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Cars using sample photos lists the cars still waiting for real photos. Each real car showing sample photos is also a line on To do, with <b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/settings/sample-photos</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/812"><img src="/guides/img/admin-36-sample-photos-desktop-55c64070.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="812"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:26.8%;top:28.9%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-publish-now-and-new-cars-published-by-themselves" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Publish now, and new cars published by themselves</h2><p class="gd-p">Nothing between a new car and the site has to be finished first: the car goes on the site, and what is still open shows on its checklist.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Publish new cars automatically</b> (on by default): a new real car goes on the site by itself as soon as it has its year, make and model and its rates, when it is added with rates, when its rates are saved, when it is added for an owner, or when an owner&#39;s application is approved.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Otherwise open the car: its Listing tab says why it is not on the site and has <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>. A car with no rates yet is published with the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults in Program settings); change them later on the Rates tab.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Every real car has its listing from the moment it is added, as a draft. It shows in Listings and in Not on the site yet until it is published.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An owner&#39;s own application waits for your decision before its car is published by itself; Publish now still works.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A car taken off the site by staff, or scheduled for a later date, is never published by itself: press <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-checklist-what-is-still-open-on-a-listed-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The checklist: what is still open on a listed car</h2><p class="gd-p">Open items never stop publishing. They show as warnings on the car&#39;s Listing tab and after Publish now.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Paperwork</td><td>Ownership permit, registry forms, agreements signed, Forms C and D, upfront payment, registry visit, tracker, safety certificate</td></tr><tr><td>Insurance</td><td>Not on the fleet insurance policy yet: the car can be booked, but not handed over</td></tr><tr><td>Details</td><td>Colour, body, seats, gearbox: the car page leaves out what is missing</td></tr><tr><td>Photos</td><td>No real photos: sample photos stand in. A photo whose plate is not checked stays private until it is</td></tr><tr><td>No VIN yet</td><td>A car added by its plate alone: add the VIN when you have it</td></tr><tr><td>Possible duplicate</td><td>An open flag in Similar cars. Only Same car keeps the car off the site</td></tr><tr><td>Owner terms</td><td>The management fee (Revenue Share) and fees not set: a request uses the owner&#39;s terms or the standard grid</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-fleet-policy-rule-at-handover" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The fleet policy rule at handover</h2><p class="gd-p">A program owner&#39;s car is listed and can be requested, offered and paid for while its paperwork is open. It is never handed over until the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet insurance policy.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Staff see a warning on a request and an offer for a car not on the policy yet.</li><li>The handover refuses the car until the insurer&#39;s confirmation is recorded (Owners and onboarding). The field app says so on the job.</li><li>Only real states keep a car off the site: retired, left the program, out of service, Turo only, bookings turned off, a self-managed owner in arrears, or a paused listing.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-cars-on-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cars on sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> ends with <b class="gd-ui">Cars on sample photos</b>: each real car whose page still shows sample photos, with its newest handover photos (the check-in and check-out photos field staff take).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Where a handover photographed the car, press <b class="gd-ui">Use the handover photos</b>. They go into the car&#39;s listing as if taken on the capture screen.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">When every required shot is there, the listing is submitted: Gemini makes each photo from the original, then the listing waits for your review like any other.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car with no handover photos yet gets them at its next handover, or press <b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b> and take them.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The listing photos use no Cloudflare image processing: Gemini makes every photo and the site makes the sizes.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-car-s-registration-and-documents" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car&#39;s registration and documents</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, then <b class="gd-ui">Owner &amp; documents</b>. The <b class="gd-ui">Registration</b> card:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Correct the <b class="gd-ui">VIN</b> (it is checked: 17 characters, the check digit, not on another car; decoded again for the body style and trim), the <b class="gd-ui">Year</b> and the <b class="gd-ui">Body style</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Type the <b class="gd-ui">Ontario permit number</b> and the date the <b class="gd-ui">Plate sticker expires</b>. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before; save the new date after the renewal and the task closes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Under <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b>, choose the kind (<b class="gd-ui">Ownership permit</b>, Safety Standards Certificate, owner&#39;s insurance, other), pick the photo or PDF and press <b class="gd-ui">Upload</b>. The ownership permit clears that item of the owner&#39;s checklist.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">For the <b class="gd-ui">Safety Standards Certificate</b>, also type its number, the date it was issued and the date it expires. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before it expires; upload the new certificate with its dates and the task closes. It is a document on the car, not a service record, and nothing is billed to the owner.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a car</b> takes the ownership permit and the Safety Standards Certificate too, under <b class="gd-ui">Documents (optional)</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-car-added-under-the-wrong-owner" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car added under the wrong owner</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, Overview, <b class="gd-ui">Who supplies the car</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Move to another owner</b>. Choose the owner, or <b class="gd-ui">CarmaCars (owner not known yet)</b>: the car becomes a company car, with no owner schedule or terms.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The car&#39;s unsigned owner application and vehicle schedule are withdrawn (kept in the history), and its draft owner invoices are deleted. Nobody is notified.</li><li>It is refused once anything for the car is signed, issued, paid or on a statement.</li></ul><h3 class="gd-h3">The VIN from the car, not typed</h3><p class="gd-p">Every VIN field (Add a car, Add a car for an owner, the car&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Registration</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b>) has <b class="gd-ui">Scan the barcode</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Photo of the VIN</b>. Scan the barcode in the driver&#39;s door frame or at the bottom of the windshield: the phone&#39;s camera reads it by itself. Or take a photo of the VIN plate or sticker: the barcode in it is read first, else the photo is read for the printed VIN. The VIN is checked (17 characters, the check digit; I, O and Q become 1 and 0) and decoded as when you type it. Check it against the car before saving.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Photos in any order</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b> on the listing takes any number of photos at once from the camera roll. Each is sorted to its shot by itself (front three-quarter, sides, rear, dashboard, seats and the rest); a shot that already has its photo sends the new one to the extra photos, so nothing is replaced by accident. The shots are a guide, not a rule: a listing is complete with 10 photos that can go on the site and one outside photo for the cover. Outside photos get the studio background: the car is cropped to its edges and placed big in the frame with its wheels on the floor and a soft shadow under the tyres, and any corner watermark or caption beside the car is left out. Inside and detail photos are kept as taken; when one has a watermark, a logo or caption text on it, the edge with the mark is cut off by itself, and a photo whose mark cannot be cut off (one in the middle) stays off the site until you replace it. <b class="gd-ui">Cover the plate</b> opens on every outside photo with the plate box suggested; check it and save.</p><p class="gd-p">Outside photos made before the newest framing (the car small in the frame, or without the model&#39;s name behind it) are made again with <b class="gd-ui">Frame the outside photos again</b> above the photos of the listing, then <b class="gd-ui">Yes, frame again</b>. The cover and the main outside views get the model&#39;s name lettered behind the car, as on the sample photos (for example CLA, C CLASS, AMG GT). The photos leave the site until their plates are checked again: the plate box is suggested on the new photos; check each and cover it. On a published listing each goes back on the site once its plate is checked.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-showroom-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Showroom photos</h2><p class="gd-p">Outside photos go in the CarmaCars showroom by themselves. When a real photographed room is stored (dealership or studio photos licensed for commercial use, fetched once from Wikimedia Commons with their author and licence kept), the car stands in it: about 70% of the width, its wheels on the room&#39;s floor, a soft shadow and a faint reflection under it, its light matched to the room, and no sign or lettering on the real wall. Program settings &gt; Listings has the switch (Photographed showroom rooms, on), the car&#39;s width and the cut-out quality floor: a cut-out that is not clean enough (pieces, a blurry or ragged edge) is never placed in a room, the real photo is used instead (its plate covered as usual) and the photo says so. Without a stored room it is the drawn dark showroom: a simple dark dealership with linear lights in the ceiling, a slatted wood wall between two light strips with a big lit CarmaCars sign, and a polished dark floor with the car&#39;s reflection and a shadow under each tyre. Every angle of a car is in the same room, and the cover has the model&#39;s name in metal letters on the wall under the sign. The image model may relight the car or turn it slightly; a photo that shows another car, model or colour is not used. <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> has the switch (Showroom photos, on), the image model that makes the photos look photographed, and its daily limit. Past the limit, or when the image model is not available, the site makes the showroom itself for free, and the photo says why under it.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A car whose photos were made on the black studio: press <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to this car</b> above its photos, then <b class="gd-ui">Yes, apply</b>.</li><li>Every car at once: <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Showroom photos</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to every car</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Yes, every car</b>.</li><li>Under a photo in the showroom: <b class="gd-ui">Redo</b> makes it again, <b class="gd-ui">Back to the original</b> puts back the version before the showroom.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">A car that stays where it was keeps its plate check. When the image model made the photo, check the plate again: the photo is off the site until you do. Photos made in the first showroom are made again in the new one with <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to this car</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to every car</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-failed-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Failed photos</h2><p class="gd-p">The site makes the photo sizes itself: the image service is asked only to cut the car out (<b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>: the switch to let the image service make every photo step is off). When the image service is busy or over its allowance, the photo still goes on the site from the original and is made again later. A listing marked Failed has <b class="gd-ui">Retry failed photos</b> in its note; <b class="gd-ui">Retry failed photos</b> at the top does every listing. They are made again a few at a time, and the listing leaves Failed when they are done.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-primary-photo-is-always-the-front-exterior-release-43" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The primary photo is always the front exterior (release 43)</h2><p class="gd-p">The first photo of every car on the site, in the cards, the feeds and the Marketplace kit is its exterior at the standard angle (front three-quarter, in the dark showroom). An inside photo is never ahead of an outside one, and the cover mark follows by itself whenever photos are added, made again or reordered.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Primary photo is not exterior</b> is a flag and a filter in <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>: it marks a car whose first photo is an inside one because its best outside photo is not on the site yet, or it has none. Add or approve an outside photo and the flag clears by itself.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Redo photos with Gemini</b> on the car page makes every photo of the car again from its original with Gemini, and generates its missing angles. A photo Gemini cannot make well stays off the site, flagged. It needs the image model switched on in Program settings, Listings.</li><li>The same press checks the car&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Other detail</b> photos again: an outside view filed there is moved to the outside photos (the front three-quarter becomes the first photo) and made in the showroom. This is what clears the flag on a car that showed nothing to redo.</li><li>Every outside photo has the same room behind it: Gemini replaces the whole background from the original photo.</li><li>Every plate is blurred; nothing is drawn on it and there is no text anywhere else. Inside photos stay sharp from front to back.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Redo every car with Gemini</b> (Listings, Showroom photos; Admin and Fleet) is the same as <b class="gd-ui">Redo every car</b> on the Photo standard card.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-photo-standard-every-photo-made-by-gemini-release-45" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The photo standard: every photo made by Gemini (release 45)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every listing photo is made by Gemini from the original photo, never from a cut-out. Outside photos get their whole background replaced by the CarmaCars showroom, with nothing of the place they were taken in left. Inside photos are cleaned up (no clutter) and sharp from front to back. Every plate is blurred so no character can be read; no plate is drawn and there is no text anywhere else on the photo.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">The check.</b> A second Gemini look compares each new photo with the original and refuses it when the old background shows, the car is warped, another colour or model, has parts added or missing, a plate can be read, or there is text anywhere. The site also checks the edges are the dark showroom. A refused photo is made again, twice; then it stays off the site and is counted as flagged.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Missing angles.</b> Every car shows the standard set: front three-quarter, front, side profile, rear three-quarter, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats and trunk. An angle the car has no photo of is generated by Gemini from the car&#39;s own photos, in the same showroom, and marked <b class="gd-ui">AI generated</b> on the listing (staff only). A real photo of that angle replaces it by itself.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">The order.</b> The front three-quarter is always first, then the other outside photos, then the inside ones. A car whose first photo would be an inside one shows no photos and cannot be published until it has an outside one; its front three-quarter is generated first.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">By itself.</b> Every 5 minutes the job brings the next cars to the standard, newest listed cars first, until every car is done (about a day for the whole fleet). A photo already at the standard is never made again unless you ask. <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>: the daily Gemini limit (2000 calls), the calls kept for new uploads (50) and the switch.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Photo standard</b> (Admin and Fleet) shows each car: photos at the standard out of all, AI angles, flagged photos and the last run. <b class="gd-ui">Redo this car now</b> makes all of its photos again at once; <b class="gd-ui">Redo every car</b> makes every photo of every car again. <b class="gd-ui">Redo photos with Gemini</b> on a car page does the same as Redo this car now.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-first-photo-plain-with-a-model-or-a-flyer" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The first photo: plain, with a model, or a flyer</h2><p class="gd-p">On a listing, under <b class="gd-ui">First photo</b>, choose what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit. Switch any time; the other photos stay as they are.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Plain car</b>: the cover photo as it is (the default).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">With a model</b>: a car-show photo made by the image model, with a fully clothed adult model beside the car. It needs the image model; until it is made (or when the image model is not there) the plain cover shows, and the listing says why.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Flyer</b>: the cover photo with a band like a printed flyer: the car, the price a day from its live rates, the call to action, a badge and the logo. When the price, the words or the cover photo change, it is made again by itself within 10 minutes; the plain cover shows meanwhile.</li></ul><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Make it again</b> makes the chosen one again. The words of the flyer and the description of the model are in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> (First photo &quot;flyer&quot; and First photo &quot;with a model&quot;); {car}, {price}, {weekly} and {monthly} are filled for each car.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-marketing-photos-in-other-scenes" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Marketing photos in other scenes</h2><p class="gd-p">For Marketplace and social posts, a car&#39;s outside photos can be made again in other scenes. The website keeps its own photos in the dark showroom: a marketing set never replaces them.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a listing, under <b class="gd-ui">Marketing photos</b>, choose a scene, or <b class="gd-ui">Mix: a different scene on each photo</b>, and press <b class="gd-ui">Make the marketing set</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The copies show as they are made. The dark showroom and the plain white studio are made by the site when the image model is not there; the photographic scenes (a bright showroom, a city street at night, the Toronto waterfront, a parking garage, Highway, a scenic road, Brick building) need the image model, and say so on the copy when it is not there.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Download (ZIP)</b> takes the set; the Marketplace kit&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">With scenes (ZIP)</b> takes the same set.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Marketing scenes</b> lists the scenes. A scene made in a real place has a photo of that place: Brick building picks its photo by itself: the widest outside photo, as taken, of the shareholders&#39; own cars. To use another, press <b class="gd-ui">Change the reference photo</b> and pick one (the shareholders&#39; cars&#39; photos come first), or upload one. The scenes&#39; names and words are in the <b class="gd-ui">Marketing scenes</b> setting.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-extra-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Extra photos</h2><p class="gd-p">A photo that fits no shot is an extra photo. Under the shots, <b class="gd-ui">Extra outside photos</b> (put on the studio background) and <b class="gd-ui">Extra inside and detail photos</b> (touched up) each take any number at once. They count toward the 10 photos, get the same plate check, and come after the standard shots on the car&#39;s page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">In the review, <b class="gd-ui">Extra photos, in their order on the car page</b> lists them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Drag a photo by its handle (⋮⋮), or press <b class="gd-ui">Earlier</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Later</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the order</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-fix-a-cut-out" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fix a cut-out</h2><p class="gd-p">When the background removal cuts badly (a mirror or a wheel missing, background left beside the car), press <b class="gd-ui">Edit the cut-out</b> under the outside photo.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Cut-out</b> shows the car over the photo as taken, shown faintly. Choose <b class="gd-ui">Erase</b> and brush over what should go, or <b class="gd-ui">Restore</b> and brush over what the cut-out took off. Set <b class="gd-ui">Brush size</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Zoom</b>; when zoomed, <b class="gd-ui">Move the view</b> pans. <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> takes back the last stroke.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">On the studio</b> shows the car on the studio background. Drag the car to move it and use <b class="gd-ui">Size</b> to make it larger or smaller. <b class="gd-ui">Centre and full size</b> puts it back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save as a new version</b>. The photo is made again in about a minute; the version before and the photo as taken are kept. <b class="gd-ui">Reset to the automatic cut-out</b> starts again from the automatic one.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>If the car did not move, the plate check carries over: a photo marked no plate visible stays so, and a covered plate is covered again on the new photo when the review is open. If the car moved, check the plate again. A photo made before cut-outs were kept shows <b class="gd-ui">Make the cut-out</b> first; the editor opens by itself when it is ready.</div></aside><p class="gd-p">Every photo also gets a light touch-up by itself (exposure, levels, a little contrast and colour, mild sharpening), never enough to change the paint colour or hide a scratch. Turn it off for one photo with <b class="gd-ui">Use original colours</b> under it (the photo is made again; approve it again), or for every photo in Admin &gt; Settings &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> (Listings) with <b class="gd-ui">Auto-enhance listing photos</b>. The photo as uploaded is always kept.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-import-photos-from-a-google-drive-link" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Import photos from a Google Drive link</h2><p class="gd-p">The owner often hands over a car&#39;s photos as a public Google Drive folder, or one big folder with a folder per make and then per car. You do not download them: paste the link.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">One car.</b> On the car&#39;s listing, under the capture, <b class="gd-ui">Import photos from a Google Drive link</b>. Paste the folder link (shared with Anyone with the link) and press <b class="gd-ui">Import the photos</b>. Every photo in the folder, and in the folders inside it, is added to this car as if you had pressed Add photos: each is sorted to its shot (else filed as an extra photo, in file-name order), put on the studio background and checked for its plate. The box under the link, <b class="gd-ui">Submit the listing for processing when its photos are in</b>, is on by default.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Many cars.</b> <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Import photos from Drive</b> (a button on Vehicles). Paste the top folder&#39;s link and press <b class="gd-ui">Read the folder</b>. The page walks every folder and proposes a car for each folder that holds photos, from the year, make, model, colour and plate in the folder names (the make folder above counts; 01 Motors partner cars come first). Check the table: tick or untick <b class="gd-ui">Import</b>, change the car in the list (the likely cars come first), leave out a folder with <b class="gd-ui">Do not import this folder</b>. A line marked <b class="gd-ui">Check this one</b> matched two alike cars. Then press <b class="gd-ui">Import N photos from M folders</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The page follows the import by itself. You can leave it and come back: it runs in the background.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The end shows the summary: imported, skipped and failed, and why for each (a file over 15 MB, a file that is not a photo, the same photo already on the car, a folder not shared).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Try the failed photos again</b> takes only the ones that failed. Pressing Import on the same link again never adds a photo twice: a Drive file already on the car is skipped, and so is the same picture under another name. A photo you took off the car can be imported again.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>JPG, PNG, HEIC and WebP only (HEIC and WebP are made JPEG first). At most 15 MB a photo, 600 photos, 400 folders and 4 GB in one import. Drive is asked politely, one photo at a time; a big import takes a while.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Without a key, Drive shows only the first 50 files of a folder on its public page; a folder with more is read in full when Drive allows it. In <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Photo import from Google Drive</b> box takes a Google API key with the Drive API on (after it is saved only its last 4 characters are shown, and it is never written to the change log): with it, folders of any size are read and photos download without Drive&#39;s warning pages.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-test-bookings-and-deleting-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Test bookings and deleting a car</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a booking made only to try the site, press <b class="gd-ui">Mark as a test booking</b> (Admins only; the reason is optional). <b class="gd-ui">Make it a real booking again</b> undoes it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A car whose bookings are all test bookings can be deleted: the test bookings and their test payments go with it, and a copy is kept in the archive of deleted requests.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car with a real booking cannot be deleted.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-pickup-from-owner-and-return-to-owner-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pickup from owner and return to owner (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">On a car&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Pickup from owner and return to owner</b> records the car&#39;s condition when CarmaCars picks it up from its owner or gives it back: the date and time, km, fuel, many photos at once with the suggested angles, and notes. <b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b> adds more to a record later. The owner sees these records read only on the car&#39;s page in their portal. They are the baseline condition for any dispute.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-incident-cards-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Incident cards (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Incident cards</b> prints the card for each car: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, the support number from Settings, a roadside number when there is one, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. Open a car and press <b class="gd-ui">Incident card</b> to print only that car; on the list, <b class="gd-ui">Print all cars</b> prints them all, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks, ready to laminate. Under Fleet insurance policy press <b class="gd-ui">Add the policy</b> (the insurer, the policy number, the dates, the named insured, the roadside number on the slip) and choose the uploaded slip if you have one: it is printed as it is, otherwise the fields are. The card never shows a premium. Fleet staff print the same cards from their portal.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-field-jobs-shifts-and-who-gets-a-job" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Field jobs, shifts and who gets a job</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Field jobs</b>, is the board Fleet uses, with every action Fleet has. Shifts are paused (release 50): none is published by itself (Program settings, Shifts published by themselves, off), the open shifts nobody claimed were cancelled, and the claimed ones stay with their jobs. <b class="gd-ui">Publish shifts</b> still adds one by hand. A job goes on a shift somebody works first (a person on it who has passed the academy basics), else on an open shift; a job on a shift nobody works moves within the hour once a worked shift is near. A job with no shift near stays unassigned, and those with nobody to work them give Fleet one To do, <b class="gd-ui">field job(s) have no shift anybody works</b>. Every job still goes on a shift and to its person (Who gets an automatic job: the least busy): a shift of its own day first; on a day without one, a pickup goes on the shift before it and a return on the shift after it; work not done when a shift ends moves to the next shift every hour. Switched back on, shifts are published by themselves from the shift template (one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 every second day by default, 14 days ahead, only forward from the latest shift), with a shift of its own for any handover or return no shift covers, and a shift you cancel is not published again. Field staff take them. <b class="gd-ui">Missing check-in and check-out</b>, on the same page, lists every past rental without its photos and readings, with <b class="gd-ui">Give to field staff</b>. Jobs go on shifts, not on people: each job is put on the shift covering its time (or that day&#39;s), whoever holds the shift does it (several people share the jobs, least busy first), a shift nobody holds keeps its jobs for whoever claims it, and work lands only on days with shifts (work due on a day without shifts moves to the day before, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day; the booking&#39;s own times never change). A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning on the board and on the booking. <b class="gd-ui">To a shift</b> moves a job to another shift. You can give a job to a field person on a shift that day or to an Admin, take it off with <b class="gd-ui">Unassign</b> (tick <b class="gd-ui">Tell them</b> to let them know), and an Admin who holds a job opens it on the field portal. A person who has not passed the academy cannot be given a job or take a shift. A shift with jobs and nobody on it within 24 hours alerts Fleet and the Admins once.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Shifts in your Google Calendar (release 50)</h3><p class="gd-p">At the bottom of <b class="gd-ui">Field jobs</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Add shifts, townhalls and interviews to Google Calendar</b> gives you a private calendar link with every field shift, 14 days back to 60 days ahead: the day, the start and end (Toronto time), who claimed it or Open, the tasks on it and a link back to it. It also has the weekly townhall (the next 8 meetings) and every booked interview call with its time, the applicant&#39;s first name, the role and the call link. No email is sent.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Make my calendar link</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add to Google Calendar</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Add</b> in Google. Or <b class="gd-ui">Copy link</b> and add it in another calendar app by URL.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Google refreshes a subscribed calendar on its own schedule, every few hours, so a change can take that long to show.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Keep the link to yourself. <b class="gd-ui">Regenerate link</b> makes a new one and stops the old one; <b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> stops it.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-every-view-generated-from-the-car-s-photos-release-47" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Every view generated from the car&#39;s photos (release 47)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every car shows nine generated views in the order of the sample photos: front three-quarter (always first, the cover), side profile, rear three-quarter, front, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats and trunk. Gemini makes each car from references; the site puts it on the same dealership background, so every car stands in the same room.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">What Gemini is sent.</b> The car&#39;s listing photos (its exact colour, trim and wheels); when it has none of that side (outside or inside), its newest check-in and check-out photos instead (only as references: they are never shown on the site). Then the sample view of that angle (for the camera position only) and the stock photo of the model. Gemini makes the car alone on a flat key colour; it never draws the room. Plates taken off, no text, no logos added.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">The check.</b> A second Gemini look compares the result with the real photos (same car, colour, wheels and trim, nothing warped, not a render) and with the angle. A refused view is made again, twice, told what was wrong; still refused, it is flagged (release 50: only views that passed are on the site).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">The real photos.</b> They stay in the car&#39;s record and on the Admin car page, marked as they were; the site shows the generated view of an angle in place of the real one only once it has passed. Generated views are marked <b class="gd-ui">AI generated</b> for staff only.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">By itself.</b> Every 5 minutes the job takes the front three-quarter of every car first (newest listed first), then the other angles, within the daily Gemini limit (about a day for the whole fleet). <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>: the switch for the generated views.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Photo standard</b> shows each car&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Generated set</b> (views made out of nine, being made, flagged, and &quot;from check-in photos&quot; when those were used). <b class="gd-ui">Redo this car now</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Redo every car</b> make the generated views again too; the views on the site stay until the new ones pass.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Showroom background plates</b> (<b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b>, Admin): the room for front, side and rear views. Gemini made them once and a second look confirmed each looks like a real photo. Upload a real photo of a showroom (empty floor in the middle, no people, cars, signs or logos) to replace one or all three; <b class="gd-ui">Make a new one</b> has Gemini make it again.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-studio-set-every-car-photographed-the-same-way-release-4" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The studio set: every car photographed the same way (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every car gets the same nine views, as if all were photographed in one studio on one day: the same angle, camera height, lens and framing for each view, the car facing the same way as the sample covers (the front three-quarter and the side with the nose to the left), plates taken off cleanly, the car itself unchanged.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The scene: every car stands in the same scene so the covers line up as you scroll: the dark dealership with the CarmaCars sign on the wall by default, with the model&#39;s name on the wall behind the car on the first photo. <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>: the scene for every car. On a car, <b class="gd-ui">Studio photos</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Scene</b> picks another for that car only (highway, brick building and the other marketing scenes).</li><li>No photo of an angle? Gemini makes it from the car&#39;s other photos. A car with no photo at all gets its outside views from the stock photo of its model, in its own colour.</li><li>One set everywhere: once a car&#39;s front three-quarter is made, the site shows only its made views, in the standard order, the front three-quarter first: the same photo on the home page, the search cards, the car page, the partner feeds and in the sitemap. The real photos stay in the car&#39;s record.</li><li>The check: Gemini checks each view against the car&#39;s own photos: the same car (model, colour, wheels), the right angle, the nose the right way, the old background gone (the site also measures it), no readable plate. Smaller doubts (framing, a part the photos do not show) stop only the first two tries.</li><li>On a car, <b class="gd-ui">Studio photos</b> shows each view beside the car&#39;s own photos of that angle, marked <b class="gd-ui">AI</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Make again</b> makes one view again; <b class="gd-ui">Take off the site</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Put on the site</b>.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Photo standard</b> shows the fleet&#39;s progress: views made out of all, cars with their studio cover, and about how many days are left at Gemini&#39;s daily limit.</li><li>Marketing set: <b class="gd-ui">Make the marketing set</b> uses the studio views (the same angle and cover as the site) in the scene you choose, plus up to three lifestyle shots: an adult model with the car, styled like a luxury car advert, always fully dressed and tasteful. Each is marked <b class="gd-ui">AI</b>; tick <b class="gd-ui">In the ZIP</b> for the photos you want in a post. A lifestyle shot Gemini declines is skipped.</li><li>Background plates (<b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b>, Admin): one set per scene. Choose the scene, then upload a real photo of the place to replace one or all three.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-studio-renders-first-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Studio renders first (release 48)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Every car gets the full studio set made from its own photos: same colour, wheels and trim, the same framing for every car.</li><li>On the site the views come first, in the sample photos&#39; order: front three-quarter (the cover), side profile, rear three-quarter, front, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats, trunk. Up to six of the car&#39;s real outside photos follow, each cut out on the same dealership background. The real photos themselves stay in the car&#39;s record.</li><li>A render goes live as soon as it passes the photo check. There is no approval step. To change one, open the car, <b class="gd-ui">Studio photos</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Make again</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Take off the site</b>. Taking the side profile off makes the next render the cover.</li><li>The car page says <b class="gd-ui">Rendered photos</b> above the gallery, with <b class="gd-ui">See its real photos</b>.</li><li>New cars get their renders by themselves. To do every published car now: <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Photo standard</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Render every published car</b>. The line beside it shows how many cars are done. It works within the image model&#39;s daily limit.</li><li>When a car&#39;s set is live, the owner gets an email and an alert (&quot;Your car has new studio photos&quot;), and Fleet gets &quot;Studio photos live&quot; in the next digest. Look the photos over.</li><li>The Cars filter lists one model per family (for example CLA-Class or 3 Series). The trim shows on the car. A car whose model family is not recognised is listed in <b class="gd-ui">Data health</b>: fix the typo, or ask for the family to be added.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-one-look-studio-renders-only-release-50" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">One look: studio renders only (release 50)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Once a car has a studio view that passed, the site shows its studio views: the car page, the cards, the landing and area pages, the partner feeds, the social preview image and the car picture in emails. The car&#39;s own photos are shown only cut out on the studio background.</li><li>The studio (R50 hotfix 2): the site checks that the background is one flat key colour and the whole car is in the frame, before anything else is paid. Then Gemini checks the car, the view, the way the nose points and the plates against the real photos. Then the site cuts the car out and puts it on the dealership background with the CarmaCars sign, at its view&#39;s size and place. The background is one image, exactly the same for every view of every car (no car name on the wall).</li><li>The views are exactly the sample photos&#39; angles, in the same order: front three-quarter (the cover), side, rear three-quarter, front, rear, dashboard, seats, wheel. A view the car has no photo of is made by Gemini from the car&#39;s other photos (its listing photos, else its check-in and check-out photos), the same paint, rims and trim. Then up to six of the car&#39;s real outside photos follow, each cut out on the same background. A refused view is made again, told why, after 20 minutes, then an hour; after three tries it is flagged with the reasons on <b class="gd-ui">Photo standard</b>.</li><li>Home, heroes and sample cards: where a section or a card shows a sample car, a real car takes its place only as a cutout (the car alone on the section&#39;s own picture, or on the studio background on a card), never its full photo with its background.</li><li>The cost guard: Each Gemini image counts in the daily photo budget (Program settings). One view gets at most 3 image calls a day. When the last 24 hours took more than 8 image calls for each view that passed, the studio pauses for a day and the Admins get an alert. <b class="gd-ui">Photo standard</b> shows the calls, the spend and the pause; clear <b class="gd-ui">Listing photo r48 paused at</b> in Program settings to start again sooner. A Gemini check that gives no verdict is recorded with its cause (the error Google sent, an answer cut off, or no answer in time).</li><li>No view passed yet: the car shows its photos as before (its own photos, or the sample photos with their caption), never the empty studio. Its own photos stay in the car&#39;s record, for the views and for staff.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Studio grid.</b> <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Photo standard</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Studio grid</b> shows every published car&#39;s views side by side, with <b class="gd-ui">Live</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Being made</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Gate refused</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Flagged</b> and the reasons, so a view that drifts from the others is easy to spot. Use <b class="gd-ui">Make again</b> on the car&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Studio photos</b> to redo one..</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-add-old-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add old photos</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Check-in visits</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Add old photos</b> is the same screen field staff, Fleet and customer service use: photos of an earlier check-in or check-out onto its booking, for every booking picked up or returned in the last <span class="gd-url">old_photos_days</span> (60), whoever handled it. One booking at a time, or <b class="gd-ui">A pile of photos</b> sorted by the time each was taken and the plate read from it. Each photo shows on the photo report as &quot;added later by&quot; the person with its capture time; nobody outside the team is told. The windows are in Settings &gt; Program settings &gt; Field jobs and handovers: <span class="gd-url">old_photos_days</span>, <span class="gd-url">old_photos_match_hours</span>, <span class="gd-url">old_photos_group_minutes</span>.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'owner-money', 'chapter', 'owners-and-onboarding', 'Owner fee invoices are issued on the notice day and debited on the 15th. Invoices of any amount are made by hand, as drafts first. Statements are built, approved and issued each month, and payouts follow.

## Owner invoices

**Money** > **Owner money**, the **Invoices** tab. Every owner invoice, drafts and voids included. The same list is on each owner''s and each application''s Invoices tab.

1. Filter by Drafts, Open, Partly paid, Paid, Failed, In arrears or Void, or search by invoice number or owner. Open an invoice to see everything about it.
2. **New invoice** makes an invoice of any amount for an owner''s car, for example a registration fee of $123.45.
3. The monthly run and tracker invoices: **Run the monthly invoices** issues the invoices for the 15th by hand, for a missed month (never twice); **Issue all tracker invoices** bills the Tracker Install for each car waiting for its tracker.

![](/guides/img/admin-14-owner-invoices-desktop-dc4ed1f1.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1060; address: carmacars.ca/admin/invoices; pins: 1 83.3 22.4, 2 41.7 35.7, 3 29.0 43.4")

## Make, edit and issue an invoice

A new invoice is a draft: the owner sees nothing and it is never debited until you issue it.

1. Choose the car, a title (for example Registration fee) and, if you like, the due date (empty: 7 days after it is issued). Each line: the description, the quantity, the unit amount to the cent, HST on or off, and a note. **Add a line** for more.
2. **Save as draft** to come back to it, or **Save and issue** to send it now. On a draft''s page, **Issue and email** sends it.
3. Paid another way? Press **Already paid outside the platform** on the invoice: choose how (e-Transfer, cash, cheque, bank transfer or card outside the platform), the date and the reference. A draft is issued without the invoice email first, the payment is recorded, and the owner gets no email unless you tick **Email the owner a receipt**. To record a smaller or extra payment, press **Record payment**. The page lists the payments with their receipts, the automatic debits, the emails sent and the history.
4. **Resend email** sends the invoice again. **PDF** opens it as a PDF.

## Correct an issued invoice

An issued invoice is never edited. You void it and issue a corrected one.

1. Press **Void**, write the reason (the owner reads it), keep Make a corrected invoice from it ticked, and press **Void the invoice**. Its scheduled debit is cancelled and the owner is told.
2. The corrected invoice opens as a draft with the same lines. Fix the amounts and press **Save and issue**.
3. Already paid? Void the payment first, or press **Credit note** for the amount to give back: it gets its own number and the owner sees it.

Invoices issued before October 20, 2026 at the old default (for example $904.00, or $1,017.00 when the Insurance Fee was $450.00) are not changed by themselves. Where an owner agreed another amount, void them and reissue at the agreed amount.

## The automatic debit

The debit runs by itself. Your job is to watch for payments the bank sends back and owners with no bank debit set up.

:::flow
Notice day | Invoices issued, one notice per owner, 10 days before
Debit day | The 15th from 6:00: one debit per invoice
Cleared | The invoice is paid
Returned, insufficient funds | The Late Fee (5% of the unpaid insurance, plus HST) is added once; the same amount is tried again within 30 days
Returned for another reason | No retry and no Late Fee: the debit pauses and you get a task
:::

1. The tiles show the next debit day and notice day, scheduled, processing, cleared and returned debits.
2. How it runs explains the policy in words, read from Program settings.
3. Scheduled and processing lists each debit. **Pause** holds one (a reason is needed).
4. Owners lists each owner''s bank debit. Use **Pause**, **Resume**, **Send a notice now** or, with no bank debit set up, **Send the sign-up link**.

![](/guides/img/admin-15-owner-debits-desktop-f65f061a.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 920; address: carmacars.ca/admin/debits; pins: 1 21.8 21.7, 2 21.5 35.5, 3 91.5 75.4, 4 84.7 94.7")

5. Results: each debit, cleared or returned, with the bank''s reason.
6. Run log: each notice and debit run, with its counts.
7. Notices sent: who was told what, for which debit day.

![](/guides/img/admin-15-owner-debits-desktop-8d4682bc.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 520; address: carmacars.ca/admin/debits; pins: 5 11.0 14.4, 6 10.2 52.3, 7 15.4 89.8")

Insufficient funds: the Late Fee (5% of the unpaid insurance, plus HST; $50.00 on an invoice with no insurance) is added to that invoice once and collected with the owner''s next debit, and the original amount is tried again within 30 days, as section 4.4 of the Enrollment Agreement sets out. The retry is never more than the original amount. Returned again: the invoice is in arrears and you get a task. Any debit missed (returned for another reason, too late to retry, or a retry still waiting) comes off the owner''s next revenue statement by itself: when the statement is built, the invoice goes in arrears (a waiting retry is cancelled) and the statement deducts it. Nothing to do.

> Watch out: Returned for any other reason (account closed, payment stopped, no authorization): there is no retry and no Late Fee. The owner''s debit pauses, the owner gets an email asking them to fix the account or pay another way, and you get a task. A debit is never more than its notice said. An owner with no bank debit set up gets an email on the notice day and you get a task; nothing is debited for them.

## Before the debit day: the Debit preview

The top of the Debits tab shows the coming debit day.

1. **Debit preview** lists each owner with something to debit: the total, whether a bank debit is set up, whether the notice went, and each invoice in one line: the amount, the car, the fee (monthly fee, first and last month, tracker install, adjustment, late fee), the period and how it was worked out, such as "prorated: 20 of 30 days". The line opens the invoice.
2. Something looks wrong? Press **Hold** beside the owner and give the reason. Nothing is debited for that owner until you press **Resume**.
3. **Fee check** compares the month''s invoices with each car''s signed terms: no monthly fee on a flat monthly payment, a Turo-Only car, a shareholder''s car or a company car, nothing before the Enrollment Date, and the amount the terms give. It changes nothing: void and reissue an invoice that does not match. Each production deploy prints the same check.

## When a debit can''t go ahead

You get one email: "Can''t collect $X from the owner: the reason". The reasons are the words of the owner guide: no bank debit set up, owner cancelled the debit at their bank, amount went up after the notice, the bank sent the payment back. The email lists each amount in one line and has one button that fixes it.

1. **Send the sign-up link** opens the Debits tab on that owner. Press **Send the sign-up link** again there: the owner gets the email to set up their bank debit.
2. **Send a new notice** opens the same place with **Send a new notice** for the new amount.
3. **Open the invoice** opens the invoice to record a payment made another way.

## Owner statements

**Money** > **Owner money**, the **Statements** tab

1. Press **Build all for a month** (or **Build one**).
2. Open each draft. Check it, **Rebuild** after a correction, **Preview PDF**, then **Approve**.
3. Press **Issue to the owner**. **Reissue** sends a corrected copy; **CSV** exports it.

![](/guides/img/admin-16-statements-desktop-43a313ea.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 400; address: carmacars.ca/admin/statements; pins: 1 79.9 27.3")

![An approved statement: the owner gets it by email with the PDF on the 10th, and payouts follow under Payouts.](/guides/img/admin-17-statement-desktop-106ee57f.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 520; address: carmacars.ca/admin/statements/2eedf660-50ce-4bd9-86d6-01bbe149c000; pins: 3 86.0 22.7")

## Staff commissions

**Money** > **Company**, the **Commissions** tab. Nothing is paid automatically.

:::flow
Not earned yet | The rental is ahead, or not paid in full
Pending approval | Completed and paid in full; a Sales month once it has ended
Approved | You approved it; the staff member is told
Paid | You recorded the payment; the staff member is told
Reversed | Cancelled, refunded or charged back; after payment it comes off the next payment
:::

1. By person shows each staff member''s month (Sales: rental days of 100 and the tier), what is not earned yet, pending approval, approved and paid.
2. Press **Approve** on a person (everything that may be approved now) or on one commission.
3. Press **Record a payment**: choose how it was paid (e-Transfer, bank transfer, Wise, cash, the monthly pay statement or another way), the reference and the date.
4. **Prices to review** lists prices typed by hand; **Sourcing claims** lists staff who say they sourced a website request; **Payments made** lists each payment.
5. **Owner requests** lists the commission each salesperson asks for an owner they brought in: a flat amount, or a percent of the company''s share or of the cars'' rental revenue, for a number of months or for as long as the car is with us. Press **Approve**, **Change and approve** (your terms, with a note) or **Decline**. Nothing accrues before you approve. A flat amount is earned at the owner''s first paid rental, once; a percent on each paid rental of the owner''s cars in the time approved. Each then comes to the list above for approval.
6. Who sourced an owner: the owner''s page, **Sourced by**. Only an Admin changes it, with a reason. A waiting request of the person before is withdrawn; an approved one, with what it has not paid yet, goes to the new person.

|  | Commission |
| --- | --- |
| Sales | By rental days of the month: under 50 days 10%, from 50 days 15%, from 100 days 20%, on all that month''s rentals |
| An owner a salesperson brought in | The request you approved. A CarmaCars expense, never deducted before Owner Revenue; none on CarmaCars'', a partner''s or a shareholder''s cars |
| Field staff | 10% (also the field referral fee). Customer service, Fleet and Finance staff get no sales credit or commission, ever: their help is credited as Helped by on the booking and on their scorecard |
| Base | The rental charge before tax, after discounts, with late extra days; never delivery, kilometres, add-ons or anything else bought. Only a refund of the rental charge comes off |
| On the owner statement | An owner''s car: deducted with the kickbacks before Owner Revenue, its own line on the statement. A partner''s car: from CarmaCars'' commission. A CarmaCars-owned car: a CarmaCars expense |

> Tip: A commission that changes after an owner statement was built (a refund, or the month''s Sales tier) goes on the owner''s next statement as an adjustment line.

## Field pay

**Money** > **Company**, the **Field pay** tab. Field staff clock in and out on their phones (My hours); you run the pay every two weeks. Nothing is paid automatically.

:::flow
Clocked in and out | Field staff press Clock in and Clock out; Fleet or you fix a forgotten clock-out
Pay run started | Hours times the hourly rate, plus the approved commissions
Approved | The figures are frozen, the period''s hours are locked, the statements are numbered
Paid | You recorded how each person was paid; they get their statement by email
:::

1. The tab **Pay run** shows the current two-week period (Sunday to Saturday: the first day is Settings > Program, Field pay). **Earlier period** and **Later period** move between periods.
2. After the period ends, press **Start the payroll**: one line for each person with hours times their hourly rate, plus the staff commissions and referral fees approved by the end of the period (see Staff commissions). **Refresh the figures** takes in a change made since.
3. Press **Approve**. The period''s hours are locked, each line gets a statement number and the figures are frozen. Someone still clocked in blocks it: fix their shift under **Hours** first. **Withdraw** takes an approved run back while no payment is recorded.
4. Press **Record payment** on a line: choose e-Transfer, bank transfer or cash, the reference (not needed for cash) and the date. The commissions in the line are marked paid and the person gets their pay statement by email (**Send again** repeats it). The statement''s number opens its PDF; **CSV** gives the run for your accountant.
5. **Hours** lists everyone''s shifts of the period. **Add hours** enters a shift for someone who forgot to clock in, **Change** fixes one and **Remove** takes one out. Each needs a reason and is kept in a log. Fleet does the same under Field hours but sees no pay.
6. **Hourly rates** shows each person''s rate: CA$18.00 an hour unless you give them their own with **Set the rate** (a reason is needed). A pay run keeps the rate it was started with.

|  | Field pay |
| --- | --- |
| Overtime | Off. Settings > Program, Field pay: pay overtime, after 44 hours in a week, at 150% of the rate |
| Vacation pay | Off. Settings > Program, Field pay: vacation pay (Ontario: 4%) adds that share of wages, overtime and commissions to each statement |
| Deductions | None are worked out: income tax, CPP, EI and the employer''s contributions are for your accountant. Each statement says so |
| Commissions that net to nothing | A person whose approved commissions add up to nothing or less (a clawback) is not paid them this period: they carry to the next |

> Tip: A shift of more than 16 hours (a setting) is refused, and so are hours that overlap another shift of the same person. The field staff member sees their hours and statements under My hours on their phone.

## Company model

Money > **Company model** is the CarmaCars model workbook, live: the actuals, the forecast and the pro forma on one page. Admins only (not Finance). Never share it: investors have their own sheets in the investor portal.

1. **Forecast**: the latest actual month, the EBITDA break-even month, the next 12 months'' EBITDA and the lowest cash, a chart of EBITDA and cash, and 36 months marked A (actual) or F (forecast): cars, utilization, revenue per rented day, revenue, costs, EBITDA, investor returns, tax and cash.
2. **Actuals**: filled in by themselves every hour from the bookings, payments, payouts, expenses and investments. Rental earned is spread over each rental''s days (before HST, insurer-billed and renter-billed apart, placeholders left out), with fees by kind, cash received by method, rentals and rented days, owner and partner shares, commissions, kickbacks, expenses by category and investor payouts. **Refresh actuals now** recomputes them at once.
3. **Pro forma 5 years**: each year''s income statement, cash flow and key figures.
4. **Assumptions**: growth, the utilization ramp, rates, monthly costs, hires, planned capital raises, the fleet insurance premium and tax. Press **Save the assumptions**; the forecast, the pro forma and the download use them at once. A field marked "From the actuals" left blank uses the latest complete month.
5. **Download as Excel**: the full internal workbook with live formulas and the current actuals.

> Tip: Enter the fleet insurance premium under Assumptions; until then it counts as $0 and profit is overstated. Enter each month''s costs in Money > Expenses: a cost line with nothing entered for an actual month uses the assumption, marked est.

## Payroll for everyone (release 35)

**Money** > **Payroll** is one run every two weeks for the field staff (hours) and for customer service, Fleet and Finance (salary).

1. A salaried person is paid their monthly salary x 12 / 26, for the days they were employed in the period. The salary is their own (**Set the salary**, with a reason), else the monthly pay they were hired at, else their role''s (Program settings, va_salary_defaults), in US dollars unless set otherwise.
2. Finance prepares it: **Start the payroll**, **Add a bonus or deduction** with the reason, then **Send for approval**. You get an alert.
3. You press **Approve**, then **Record all payments** (one method and reference; each stub number is added to it) or **Record payment** line by line. Each person gets their stub by email and in their portal.

> Tip: Admin > Team also has **Schedules** (each role''s days and hours, anyone''s own, who is late today) and **KPIs** (every staff member''s KPIs for a week against the targets in Program settings).

> Good to know: The townhall page: pick the craziest story, enter the week''s social media figures, add the recording link, and mark anyone present or absent. Staff who miss two townhalls in a row are locked until you press **Unlock** on the staff list.

> Good to know: Meetings, on the townhall page, lists the last eight townhalls and the next four. A townhall nobody attended is recorded as not held and counts nobody absent. **This townhall did not happen** does the same for a past one (its absences and alerts are cleared, and a lockout it caused is lifted). **Cancel this townhall** on an upcoming one sends no reminders for it; **Put it back on** undoes that.

> Good to know: Each renter and lead shows an Intent card (hot, warm or cold, with the budget, car, length, dates, urgency, delivery and coverage they mentioned). The live map shows it on each pin. An AI reading fills the gaps within the free daily allowance only (Program settings, intent_ai_enabled).

> Good to know: Investors see Search traction under the deck: Google clicks and impressions of the last 28 days, indexed pages and the weekly trend. Type the indexed pages from Search Console on the investor deck page under Investors (no API exists for it).

## Company statements

**Money** > **Company**, the **Monthly statements** tab: CarmaCars'' own monthly statement, in twelve sections.

1. Choose the month. The tiles show revenue, fees, refunds, expenses and the company net.
2. Switch between Total, Per owner and Per vehicle.
3. Download **PDF**, **PDF by owner** or **PDF by vehicle**, or press **Email me the PDFs**.
4. **Finalize** freezes the month. **Rebuild** works until then.

![](/guides/img/admin-18-company-statements-desktop-8e2738ed.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 760; address: carmacars.ca/admin/reports; pins: 1 20.8 28.0, 2 19.4 59.3, 3 77.1 15.5, 4 46.9 15.5")

### Fees taken from the revenue statement
On an owner''s page, the **Fees** button sets **How fees are paid**: **Bank debit** (the default) or **Take from revenue statement**. Taken from the statement, the owner''s invoices (not the upfront one) are not debited: the next owner statement pays each one from the payout, as far as it goes, with the line "Invoice INV-..., paid from statement". Approved, the invoice reads **Paid from statement**, or part paid with the rest on the next statement. An invoice still owing 2 months after its billing date goes back to the bank debit after the usual notice, and you get the task **Invoice ... back to the bank debit**.

### The flat-rate agreements
An owner whose every car is on a flat monthly payment signs the **Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement** instead of the standard one (the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement and Forms A to D are the same). The owner''s page says which set applies. When the pay model changes, the signed Enrollment Agreement ends and the owner signs the new one in the owner portal; changed back before signing, the signed one is in force again. The lawyer approved the flat-rate set: Program settings > **Flat-rate agreements awaiting lawyer OK** is off, and is turned on only to mark a new text still under review. Owners can sign either way.

## How it''s paid: bank debit or deducted from payouts

Every owner invoice is paid one of two ways: **Bank debit on the 15th**, or **Deduct from payouts** (taken from the owner''s monthly payouts until paid, never debited).

1. On an invoice, **How it''s paid**, **Change**. A draft changed to Deduct from payouts is issued without the debit email.
2. Each monthly statement deducts as much as the payout allows and shows it to the owner as a deduction; the rest waits for the next statement. The invoice screen shows what was deducted and what is left.
3. For the first and last month, choose **Deduct from payouts** on the Terms tab (or at approval).
4. On the Terms tab, **Charge the agreed one-off fees** makes one invoice for a car from the one-off fees agreed on the owner''s terms (all, or the ones you name), deducted from payouts or debited.

## Referral links between owners (release 28)

When one owner referred another, open the referrer''s **Terms** tab, **Referral links**, **This owner referred another owner**: choose the owner referred and the share in basis points (1000 = 10 points of the revenue the management fee is taken from). Set the referred owner''s own fee on their Terms as usual (for example a 40% management fee and $350 a month per car). Every statement of the referrer then has a **Referral share** line per referred car; it is paid from CarmaCars'' share, never the referred owner''s payout. With **sees the cars** on, the referrer finds **Cars you referred** in their owner portal: bookings, use and revenue, read only, without the other owner''s details. **End** stops the link; shares already earned are still paid.

## Statement periods (release 35)

Statements run from the 8th of one month to the 7th of the next, and the payout on the 10th covers them. A rental that crosses the cutoff, or a long weekly or biweekly rental, is paid for the days inside each period, never twice. Each statement lists amounts still uncollected from the renter separately; they are paid on the statement after they are collected.

## The owner forecast (release 48)

Each owner sees a **Forecast** on their Home: the next 12 months of each car, projected occupancy and projected owner revenue (before fees). Open an owner in **Owners**: the **Overview** shows the same **Forecast**.

1. Every car starts from the GTA seasonal curve: **Settings** > **Program settings**, **Owner forecast: the GTA seasonal curve** (a factor for each month, jan to dec, 1.00 is an average month) and **Owner forecast: the occupancy of an average month** (60% by default). A month''s curve is the average month times its factor.
2. Once a car has 3 full months on the program, its own occupancy is blended in: its own level (each month''s occupancy divided by that month''s factor) times the month''s factor, weighted half after 3 months, two thirds after 6, four fifths after 12. The season always stays in.
3. Bookings hidden from the owner (an insurer replacement hidden from them, or one never shown), test bookings and the owner''s own trips are not counted.
4. Projected owner revenue: occupancy times the days of the month times the car''s owner revenue per booked day, from its own statements of the last 12 months, else its daily rate less the Revenue Share.

Every owner statement (the owner''s page, yours and the PDF) has a **Forecast** line: next month against the statement''s month, higher or lower, by how many points and about how much owner revenue, and why (the season).

> Tip: Change a factor when the season moves (a big event, a new airport route): every owner''s forecast follows on their next visit.

## Owner-use charges (release 48)

1. The charges of a booking an owner makes of their own car (for themselves or for someone else) are billed to the owner by themselves: damage up to the deductible, tickets, tolls, fuel, kilometres, cleaning, smoking, a late return and the other fees. Add them as on any rental (the return, the Money tab); a fee that needs evidence waits for it, as always.
2. Nothing goes on a renter statement. About 15 minutes after a charge is ready it is put on an owner invoice titled "Charges on your booking", issued and due the same day.
3. It is collected in this order: the owner''s card on file at once; with no card, a bank debit started the same day (not the 15th); with no method, or when the charge fails, the owner gets the invoice with the pay link and reminders every 2 days.
4. An invoice still unpaid after 7 days, or at the statement cut-off (the 7th) if that comes first, is deducted from the owner''s next statement.
5. The owner gets an email and an alert at each step, listing each charge with its evidence. A failed charge also alerts Admins.
6. The booking''s **Money** tab shows **Charges billed to the owner**: the charges waiting for evidence, and each invoice with what is open, how it is being collected and the day it would be deducted from the statement.
7. The days are in **Settings** > **Program settings** > **Owner-use charges and the Late Fee on unpaid insurance**.

## Late Fee on unpaid insurance (release 48)

1. An owner''s Late Fee on insurance is 5% of the unpaid insurance of the invoice (it was $50 per vehicle). It is added once, as its own line, when the debit of the 15th fails or the invoice is unpaid the day after its due date.
2. The fee carries HST by default (it is a penalty, not insurance; insurance itself has none). Ask the accountant; the switch is in Program settings.
3. The unpaid insurance and the fee are deducted from the owner''s next statement by themselves, as two lines: the invoice, and "Late Fee, invoice INV-n".
4. The owner is reminded 3 days before the due date and told when the fee is added. An invoice with no insurance on it keeps the flat Late Fee.
5. The updated owner agreement (4.4 and Schedule B) is published for owners to accept (it is listed with the other terms under Settings), without signing again.

## Finance dashboard and the bank (release 49)

**Company** > **Finance** (the first tab of Company; Finance has the same page under **Money** > **Finance**) is the money of the business on one page, read only: each figure opens the page where it is worked.

1. **Cash position**: the bank balance from the latest RBC import, Stripe''s balance (available and pending) and its payouts on the way, and **Free cash**: all of that less the deposits held as cash, the owner payouts due, the refunds owed and the HST owed. An account whose balance is more than a week old is marked: import this week''s download.
2. **Money in** and **Money out** for the month (Earlier month, Later month): rentals and charges taken, owner fees, insurers, tips (for the staff, never revenue); owner payouts due and paid on the 10th, commissions, expenses with HST and refunds.
3. **Held for others**: deposits held as cash (owed back unless applied), deposit holds on cards (not money in the bank), what is kept back for claims and tolls, and refunds owed.
4. **HST** for the quarter: collected (renters, owners, insurers) less paid (expenses, payouts to registered owners) is what is owed. An Insurance Fee never carries HST: a line that does is listed in red to correct.
5. **Renter balances overdue** (past the statement''s 7 days) and **Insurer invoices unpaid** by age (0 to 30, 31 to 60, 61 to 90, over 90 days).
6. **Twelve months**: money in, money out and net by month, beside the monthly statement''s net where one is built.

**Bank lines** is the reconciliation:

1. In RBC online banking open the account, **Download transactions**, CSV or OFX (OFX also has the balance), and drop the file on **Import from RBC online banking**. The file stays on your computer; only its lines are saved, with the last four digits of the account. Importing the same days again adds nothing. With a CSV, type the balance shown in online banking.
2. A line that fits exactly one record matches by itself: money in to a Stripe payout, an e-Transfer, bank transfer or cheque recorded on a booking or owner invoice, or an insurer invoice; money out to an owner payout, a commission or referral partner payout, an expense or a refund sent by transfer.
3. **No match**: **Match** shows the records that fit (amount, and a date within a few days), nearest first: pick one. Nothing fits: record the payment, payout or expense first, then match. **Set aside** a bank fee or a transfer between CarmaCars accounts, saying what it is. **Undo** takes a reason.
4. A line with no match after two days is a To do for Finance and in the Finance morning email; matching it closes the To do. Every step is in the audit log.
', 'Owner money', 'Owner invoices (drafts, void and reissue, credit notes), the automatic debit, statements, payouts and the company statement.',
  'Owner fee invoices are issued on the notice day and debited on the 15th. Invoices of any amount are made by hand, as drafts first. Statements are built, approved and issued each month, and payouts follow.

## Owner invoices

**Money** > **Owner money**, the **Invoices** tab. Every owner invoice, drafts and voids included. The same list is on each owner''s and each application''s Invoices tab.

1. Filter by Drafts, Open, Partly paid, Paid, Failed, In arrears or Void, or search by invoice number or owner. Open an invoice to see everything about it.
2. **New invoice** makes an invoice of any amount for an owner''s car, for example a registration fee of $123.45.
3. The monthly run and tracker invoices: **Run the monthly invoices** issues the invoices for the 15th by hand, for a missed month (never twice); **Issue all tracker invoices** bills the Tracker Install for each car waiting for its tracker.

![](/guides/img/admin-14-owner-invoices-desktop-dc4ed1f1.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1060; address: carmacars.ca/admin/invoices; pins: 1 83.3 22.4, 2 41.7 35.7, 3 29.0 43.4")

## Make, edit and issue an invoice

A new invoice is a draft: the owner sees nothing and it is never debited until you issue it.

1. Choose the car, a title (for example Registration fee) and, if you like, the due date (empty: 7 days after it is issued). Each line: the description, the quantity, the unit amount to the cent, HST on or off, and a note. **Add a line** for more.
2. **Save as draft** to come back to it, or **Save and issue** to send it now. On a draft''s page, **Issue and email** sends it.
3. Paid another way? Press **Already paid outside the platform** on the invoice: choose how (e-Transfer, cash, cheque, bank transfer or card outside the platform), the date and the reference. A draft is issued without the invoice email first, the payment is recorded, and the owner gets no email unless you tick **Email the owner a receipt**. To record a smaller or extra payment, press **Record payment**. The page lists the payments with their receipts, the automatic debits, the emails sent and the history.
4. **Resend email** sends the invoice again. **PDF** opens it as a PDF.

## Correct an issued invoice

An issued invoice is never edited. You void it and issue a corrected one.

1. Press **Void**, write the reason (the owner reads it), keep Make a corrected invoice from it ticked, and press **Void the invoice**. Its scheduled debit is cancelled and the owner is told.
2. The corrected invoice opens as a draft with the same lines. Fix the amounts and press **Save and issue**.
3. Already paid? Void the payment first, or press **Credit note** for the amount to give back: it gets its own number and the owner sees it.

Invoices issued before October 20, 2026 at the old default (for example $904.00, or $1,017.00 when the Insurance Fee was $450.00) are not changed by themselves. Where an owner agreed another amount, void them and reissue at the agreed amount.

## The automatic debit

The debit runs by itself. Your job is to watch for payments the bank sends back and owners with no bank debit set up.

:::flow
Notice day | Invoices issued, one notice per owner, 10 days before
Debit day | The 15th from 6:00: one debit per invoice
Cleared | The invoice is paid
Returned, insufficient funds | The Late Fee (5% of the unpaid insurance, plus HST) is added once; the same amount is tried again within 30 days
Returned for another reason | No retry and no Late Fee: the debit pauses and you get a task
:::

1. The tiles show the next debit day and notice day, scheduled, processing, cleared and returned debits.
2. How it runs explains the policy in words, read from Program settings.
3. Scheduled and processing lists each debit. **Pause** holds one (a reason is needed).
4. Owners lists each owner''s bank debit. Use **Pause**, **Resume**, **Send a notice now** or, with no bank debit set up, **Send the sign-up link**.

![](/guides/img/admin-15-owner-debits-desktop-f65f061a.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 920; address: carmacars.ca/admin/debits; pins: 1 21.8 21.7, 2 21.5 35.5, 3 91.5 75.4, 4 84.7 94.7")

5. Results: each debit, cleared or returned, with the bank''s reason.
6. Run log: each notice and debit run, with its counts.
7. Notices sent: who was told what, for which debit day.

![](/guides/img/admin-15-owner-debits-desktop-8d4682bc.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 520; address: carmacars.ca/admin/debits; pins: 5 11.0 14.4, 6 10.2 52.3, 7 15.4 89.8")

Insufficient funds: the Late Fee (5% of the unpaid insurance, plus HST; $50.00 on an invoice with no insurance) is added to that invoice once and collected with the owner''s next debit, and the original amount is tried again within 30 days, as section 4.4 of the Enrollment Agreement sets out. The retry is never more than the original amount. Returned again: the invoice is in arrears and you get a task. Any debit missed (returned for another reason, too late to retry, or a retry still waiting) comes off the owner''s next revenue statement by itself: when the statement is built, the invoice goes in arrears (a waiting retry is cancelled) and the statement deducts it. Nothing to do.

> Watch out: Returned for any other reason (account closed, payment stopped, no authorization): there is no retry and no Late Fee. The owner''s debit pauses, the owner gets an email asking them to fix the account or pay another way, and you get a task. A debit is never more than its notice said. An owner with no bank debit set up gets an email on the notice day and you get a task; nothing is debited for them.

## Before the debit day: the Debit preview

The top of the Debits tab shows the coming debit day.

1. **Debit preview** lists each owner with something to debit: the total, whether a bank debit is set up, whether the notice went, and each invoice in one line: the amount, the car, the fee (monthly fee, first and last month, tracker install, adjustment, late fee), the period and how it was worked out, such as "prorated: 20 of 30 days". The line opens the invoice.
2. Something looks wrong? Press **Hold** beside the owner and give the reason. Nothing is debited for that owner until you press **Resume**.
3. **Fee check** compares the month''s invoices with each car''s signed terms: no monthly fee on a flat monthly payment, a Turo-Only car, a shareholder''s car or a company car, nothing before the Enrollment Date, and the amount the terms give. It changes nothing: void and reissue an invoice that does not match. Each production deploy prints the same check.

## When a debit can''t go ahead

You get one email: "Can''t collect $X from the owner: the reason". The reasons are the words of the owner guide: no bank debit set up, owner cancelled the debit at their bank, amount went up after the notice, the bank sent the payment back. The email lists each amount in one line and has one button that fixes it.

1. **Send the sign-up link** opens the Debits tab on that owner. Press **Send the sign-up link** again there: the owner gets the email to set up their bank debit.
2. **Send a new notice** opens the same place with **Send a new notice** for the new amount.
3. **Open the invoice** opens the invoice to record a payment made another way.

## Owner statements

**Money** > **Owner money**, the **Statements** tab

1. Press **Build all for a month** (or **Build one**).
2. Open each draft. Check it, **Rebuild** after a correction, **Preview PDF**, then **Approve**.
3. Press **Issue to the owner**. **Reissue** sends a corrected copy; **CSV** exports it.

![](/guides/img/admin-16-statements-desktop-43a313ea.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 400; address: carmacars.ca/admin/statements; pins: 1 79.9 27.3")

![An approved statement: the owner gets it by email with the PDF on the 10th, and payouts follow under Payouts.](/guides/img/admin-17-statement-desktop-106ee57f.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 520; address: carmacars.ca/admin/statements/2eedf660-50ce-4bd9-86d6-01bbe149c000; pins: 3 86.0 22.7")

## Staff commissions

**Money** > **Company**, the **Commissions** tab. Nothing is paid automatically.

:::flow
Not earned yet | The rental is ahead, or not paid in full
Pending approval | Completed and paid in full; a Sales month once it has ended
Approved | You approved it; the staff member is told
Paid | You recorded the payment; the staff member is told
Reversed | Cancelled, refunded or charged back; after payment it comes off the next payment
:::

1. By person shows each staff member''s month (Sales: rental days of 100 and the tier), what is not earned yet, pending approval, approved and paid.
2. Press **Approve** on a person (everything that may be approved now) or on one commission.
3. Press **Record a payment**: choose how it was paid (e-Transfer, bank transfer, Wise, cash, the monthly pay statement or another way), the reference and the date.
4. **Prices to review** lists prices typed by hand; **Sourcing claims** lists staff who say they sourced a website request; **Payments made** lists each payment.
5. **Owner requests** lists the commission each salesperson asks for an owner they brought in: a flat amount, or a percent of the company''s share or of the cars'' rental revenue, for a number of months or for as long as the car is with us. Press **Approve**, **Change and approve** (your terms, with a note) or **Decline**. Nothing accrues before you approve. A flat amount is earned at the owner''s first paid rental, once; a percent on each paid rental of the owner''s cars in the time approved. Each then comes to the list above for approval.
6. Who sourced an owner: the owner''s page, **Sourced by**. Only an Admin changes it, with a reason. A waiting request of the person before is withdrawn; an approved one, with what it has not paid yet, goes to the new person.

|  | Commission |
| --- | --- |
| Sales | By rental days of the month: under 50 days 10%, from 50 days 15%, from 100 days 20%, on all that month''s rentals |
| An owner a salesperson brought in | The request you approved. A CarmaCars expense, never deducted before Owner Revenue; none on CarmaCars'', a partner''s or a shareholder''s cars |
| Field staff | 10% (also the field referral fee). Customer service, Fleet and Finance staff get no sales credit or commission, ever: their help is credited as Helped by on the booking and on their scorecard |
| Base | The rental charge before tax, after discounts, with late extra days; never delivery, kilometres, add-ons or anything else bought. Only a refund of the rental charge comes off |
| On the owner statement | An owner''s car: deducted with the kickbacks before Owner Revenue, its own line on the statement. A partner''s car: from CarmaCars'' commission. A CarmaCars-owned car: a CarmaCars expense |

> Tip: A commission that changes after an owner statement was built (a refund, or the month''s Sales tier) goes on the owner''s next statement as an adjustment line.

## Field pay

**Money** > **Company**, the **Field pay** tab. Field staff clock in and out on their phones (My hours); you run the pay every two weeks. Nothing is paid automatically.

:::flow
Clocked in and out | Field staff press Clock in and Clock out; Fleet or you fix a forgotten clock-out
Pay run started | Hours times the hourly rate, plus the approved commissions
Approved | The figures are frozen, the period''s hours are locked, the statements are numbered
Paid | You recorded how each person was paid; they get their statement by email
:::

1. The tab **Pay run** shows the current two-week period (Sunday to Saturday: the first day is Settings > Program, Field pay). **Earlier period** and **Later period** move between periods.
2. After the period ends, press **Start the payroll**: one line for each person with hours times their hourly rate, plus the staff commissions and referral fees approved by the end of the period (see Staff commissions). **Refresh the figures** takes in a change made since.
3. Press **Approve**. The period''s hours are locked, each line gets a statement number and the figures are frozen. Someone still clocked in blocks it: fix their shift under **Hours** first. **Withdraw** takes an approved run back while no payment is recorded.
4. Press **Record payment** on a line: choose e-Transfer, bank transfer or cash, the reference (not needed for cash) and the date. The commissions in the line are marked paid and the person gets their pay statement by email (**Send again** repeats it). The statement''s number opens its PDF; **CSV** gives the run for your accountant.
5. **Hours** lists everyone''s shifts of the period. **Add hours** enters a shift for someone who forgot to clock in, **Change** fixes one and **Remove** takes one out. Each needs a reason and is kept in a log. Fleet does the same under Field hours but sees no pay.
6. **Hourly rates** shows each person''s rate: CA$18.00 an hour unless you give them their own with **Set the rate** (a reason is needed). A pay run keeps the rate it was started with.

|  | Field pay |
| --- | --- |
| Overtime | Off. Settings > Program, Field pay: pay overtime, after 44 hours in a week, at 150% of the rate |
| Vacation pay | Off. Settings > Program, Field pay: vacation pay (Ontario: 4%) adds that share of wages, overtime and commissions to each statement |
| Deductions | None are worked out: income tax, CPP, EI and the employer''s contributions are for your accountant. Each statement says so |
| Commissions that net to nothing | A person whose approved commissions add up to nothing or less (a clawback) is not paid them this period: they carry to the next |

> Tip: A shift of more than 16 hours (a setting) is refused, and so are hours that overlap another shift of the same person. The field staff member sees their hours and statements under My hours on their phone.

## Company model

Money > **Company model** is the CarmaCars model workbook, live: the actuals, the forecast and the pro forma on one page. Admins only (not Finance). Never share it: investors have their own sheets in the investor portal.

1. **Forecast**: the latest actual month, the EBITDA break-even month, the next 12 months'' EBITDA and the lowest cash, a chart of EBITDA and cash, and 36 months marked A (actual) or F (forecast): cars, utilization, revenue per rented day, revenue, costs, EBITDA, investor returns, tax and cash.
2. **Actuals**: filled in by themselves every hour from the bookings, payments, payouts, expenses and investments. Rental earned is spread over each rental''s days (before HST, insurer-billed and renter-billed apart, placeholders left out), with fees by kind, cash received by method, rentals and rented days, owner and partner shares, commissions, kickbacks, expenses by category and investor payouts. **Refresh actuals now** recomputes them at once.
3. **Pro forma 5 years**: each year''s income statement, cash flow and key figures.
4. **Assumptions**: growth, the utilization ramp, rates, monthly costs, hires, planned capital raises, the fleet insurance premium and tax. Press **Save the assumptions**; the forecast, the pro forma and the download use them at once. A field marked "From the actuals" left blank uses the latest complete month.
5. **Download as Excel**: the full internal workbook with live formulas and the current actuals.

> Tip: Enter the fleet insurance premium under Assumptions; until then it counts as $0 and profit is overstated. Enter each month''s costs in Money > Expenses: a cost line with nothing entered for an actual month uses the assumption, marked est.

## Payroll for everyone (release 35)

**Money** > **Payroll** is one run every two weeks for the field staff (hours) and for customer service, Fleet and Finance (salary).

1. A salaried person is paid their monthly salary x 12 / 26, for the days they were employed in the period. The salary is their own (**Set the salary**, with a reason), else the monthly pay they were hired at, else their role''s (Program settings, va_salary_defaults), in US dollars unless set otherwise.
2. Finance prepares it: **Start the payroll**, **Add a bonus or deduction** with the reason, then **Send for approval**. You get an alert.
3. You press **Approve**, then **Record all payments** (one method and reference; each stub number is added to it) or **Record payment** line by line. Each person gets their stub by email and in their portal.
4. A line marked **Held** is for a Field, customer service, Fleet or Finance person who has not passed the whole academy: **Record payment** is not offered, and **Record all payments** skips it and tells the person. It is never lost: the first **Record all payments** after they pass, or after you waive their academy (with a reason), pays it in full and notes the release on the line. **Commission held** beside **To pay** means only the commission, bonuses and referral fees wait (for anyone mid-academy); a commission payout to them is refused with the reason. Program settings, **Academy: hold pay for hours**, turns the hours part off.

> Tip: Admin > Team also has **Schedules** (each role''s days and hours, anyone''s own, who is late today) and **KPIs** (every staff member''s KPIs for a week against the targets in Program settings).

> Good to know: The townhall page: pick the craziest story, enter the week''s social media figures, add the recording link, and mark anyone present or absent. Staff who miss two townhalls in a row are locked until you press **Unlock** on the staff list.

> Good to know: Meetings, on the townhall page, lists the last eight townhalls and the next four. A townhall nobody attended is recorded as not held and counts nobody absent. **This townhall did not happen** does the same for a past one (its absences and alerts are cleared, and a lockout it caused is lifted). **Cancel this townhall** on an upcoming one sends no reminders for it; **Put it back on** undoes that.

> Good to know: Each renter and lead shows an Intent card (hot, warm or cold, with the budget, car, length, dates, urgency, delivery and coverage they mentioned). The live map shows it on each pin. An AI reading fills the gaps within the free daily allowance only (Program settings, intent_ai_enabled).

> Good to know: Investors see Search traction under the deck: Google clicks and impressions of the last 28 days, indexed pages and the weekly trend. Type the indexed pages from Search Console on the investor deck page under Investors (no API exists for it).

## Company statements

**Money** > **Company**, the **Monthly statements** tab: CarmaCars'' own monthly statement, in twelve sections.

1. Choose the month. The tiles show revenue, fees, refunds, expenses and the company net.
2. Switch between Total, Per owner and Per vehicle.
3. Download **PDF**, **PDF by owner** or **PDF by vehicle**, or press **Email me the PDFs**.
4. **Finalize** freezes the month. **Rebuild** works until then.

![](/guides/img/admin-18-company-statements-desktop-8e2738ed.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 760; address: carmacars.ca/admin/reports; pins: 1 20.8 28.0, 2 19.4 59.3, 3 77.1 15.5, 4 46.9 15.5")

### Fees taken from the revenue statement
On an owner''s page, the **Fees** button sets **How fees are paid**: **Bank debit** (the default) or **Take from revenue statement**. Taken from the statement, the owner''s invoices (not the upfront one) are not debited: the next owner statement pays each one from the payout, as far as it goes, with the line "Invoice INV-..., paid from statement". Approved, the invoice reads **Paid from statement**, or part paid with the rest on the next statement. An invoice still owing 2 months after its billing date goes back to the bank debit after the usual notice, and you get the task **Invoice ... back to the bank debit**.

### The flat-rate agreements
An owner whose every car is on a flat monthly payment signs the **Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement** instead of the standard one (the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement and Forms A to D are the same). The owner''s page says which set applies. When the pay model changes, the signed Enrollment Agreement ends and the owner signs the new one in the owner portal; changed back before signing, the signed one is in force again. The lawyer approved the flat-rate set: Program settings > **Flat-rate agreements awaiting lawyer OK** is off, and is turned on only to mark a new text still under review. Owners can sign either way.

## How it''s paid: bank debit or deducted from payouts

Every owner invoice is paid one of two ways: **Bank debit on the 15th**, or **Deduct from payouts** (taken from the owner''s monthly payouts until paid, never debited).

1. On an invoice, **How it''s paid**, **Change**. A draft changed to Deduct from payouts is issued without the debit email.
2. Each monthly statement deducts as much as the payout allows and shows it to the owner as a deduction; the rest waits for the next statement. The invoice screen shows what was deducted and what is left.
3. For the first and last month, choose **Deduct from payouts** on the Terms tab (or at approval).
4. On the Terms tab, **Charge the agreed one-off fees** makes one invoice for a car from the one-off fees agreed on the owner''s terms (all, or the ones you name), deducted from payouts or debited.

## Referral links between owners (release 28)

When one owner referred another, open the referrer''s **Terms** tab, **Referral links**, **This owner referred another owner**: choose the owner referred and the share in basis points (1000 = 10 points of the revenue the management fee is taken from). Set the referred owner''s own fee on their Terms as usual (for example a 40% management fee and $350 a month per car). Every statement of the referrer then has a **Referral share** line per referred car; it is paid from CarmaCars'' share, never the referred owner''s payout. With **sees the cars** on, the referrer finds **Cars you referred** in their owner portal: bookings, use and revenue, read only, without the other owner''s details. **End** stops the link; shares already earned are still paid.

## Statement periods (release 35)

Statements run from the 8th of one month to the 7th of the next, and the payout on the 10th covers them. A rental that crosses the cutoff, or a long weekly or biweekly rental, is paid for the days inside each period, never twice. Each statement lists amounts still uncollected from the renter separately; they are paid on the statement after they are collected.

## The owner forecast (release 48)

Each owner sees a **Forecast** on their Home: the next 12 months of each car, projected occupancy and projected owner revenue (before fees). Open an owner in **Owners**: the **Overview** shows the same **Forecast**.

1. Every car starts from the GTA seasonal curve: **Settings** > **Program settings**, **Owner forecast: the GTA seasonal curve** (a factor for each month, jan to dec, 1.00 is an average month) and **Owner forecast: the occupancy of an average month** (60% by default). A month''s curve is the average month times its factor.
2. Once a car has 3 full months on the program, its own occupancy is blended in: its own level (each month''s occupancy divided by that month''s factor) times the month''s factor, weighted half after 3 months, two thirds after 6, four fifths after 12. The season always stays in.
3. Bookings hidden from the owner (an insurer replacement hidden from them, or one never shown), test bookings and the owner''s own trips are not counted.
4. Projected owner revenue: occupancy times the days of the month times the car''s owner revenue per booked day, from its own statements of the last 12 months, else its daily rate less the Revenue Share.

Every owner statement (the owner''s page, yours and the PDF) has a **Forecast** line: next month against the statement''s month, higher or lower, by how many points and about how much owner revenue, and why (the season).

> Tip: Change a factor when the season moves (a big event, a new airport route): every owner''s forecast follows on their next visit.

## Owner-use charges (release 48)

1. The charges of a booking an owner makes of their own car (for themselves or for someone else) are billed to the owner by themselves: damage up to the deductible, tickets, tolls, fuel, kilometres, cleaning, smoking, a late return and the other fees. Add them as on any rental (the return, the Money tab); a fee that needs evidence waits for it, as always.
2. Nothing goes on a renter statement. About 15 minutes after a charge is ready it is put on an owner invoice titled "Charges on your booking", issued and due the same day.
3. It is collected in this order: the owner''s card on file at once; with no card, a bank debit started the same day (not the 15th); with no method, or when the charge fails, the owner gets the invoice with the pay link and reminders every 2 days.
4. An invoice still unpaid after 7 days, or at the statement cut-off (the 7th) if that comes first, is deducted from the owner''s next statement.
5. The owner gets an email and an alert at each step, listing each charge with its evidence. A failed charge also alerts Admins.
6. The booking''s **Money** tab shows **Charges billed to the owner**: the charges waiting for evidence, and each invoice with what is open, how it is being collected and the day it would be deducted from the statement.
7. The days are in **Settings** > **Program settings** > **Owner-use charges and the Late Fee on unpaid insurance**.

## Late Fee on unpaid insurance (release 48)

1. An owner''s Late Fee on insurance is 5% of the unpaid insurance of the invoice (it was $50 per vehicle). It is added once, as its own line, when the debit of the 15th fails or the invoice is unpaid the day after its due date.
2. The fee carries HST by default (it is a penalty, not insurance; insurance itself has none). Ask the accountant; the switch is in Program settings.
3. The unpaid insurance and the fee are deducted from the owner''s next statement by themselves, as two lines: the invoice, and "Late Fee, invoice INV-n".
4. The owner is reminded 3 days before the due date and told when the fee is added. An invoice with no insurance on it keeps the flat Late Fee.
5. The updated owner agreement (4.4 and Schedule B) is published for owners to accept (it is listed with the other terms under Settings), without signing again.

## Finance dashboard and the bank (release 49)

**Company** > **Finance** (the first tab of Company; Finance has the same page under **Money** > **Finance**) is the money of the business on one page, read only: each figure opens the page where it is worked.

1. **Cash position**: the bank balance from the latest RBC import, Stripe''s balance (available and pending) and its payouts on the way, and **Free cash**: all of that less the deposits held as cash, the owner payouts due, the refunds owed and the HST owed. An account whose balance is more than a week old is marked: import this week''s download.
2. **Money in** and **Money out** for the month (Earlier month, Later month): rentals and charges taken, owner fees, insurers, tips (for the staff, never revenue); owner payouts due and paid on the 10th, commissions, expenses with HST and refunds.
3. **Held for others**: deposits held as cash (owed back unless applied), deposit holds on cards (not money in the bank), what is kept back for claims and tolls, and refunds owed.
4. **HST** for the quarter: collected (renters, owners, insurers) less paid (expenses, payouts to registered owners) is what is owed. An Insurance Fee never carries HST: a line that does is listed in red to correct.
5. **Renter balances overdue** (past the statement''s 7 days) and **Insurer invoices unpaid** by age (0 to 30, 31 to 60, 61 to 90, over 90 days).
6. **Twelve months**: money in, money out and net by month, beside the monthly statement''s net where one is built.

**Bank lines** is the reconciliation:

1. In RBC online banking open the account, **Download transactions**, CSV or OFX (OFX also has the balance), and drop the file on **Import from RBC online banking**. The file stays on your computer; only its lines are saved, with the last four digits of the account. Importing the same days again adds nothing. With a CSV, type the balance shown in online banking.
2. A line that fits exactly one record matches by itself: money in to a Stripe payout, an e-Transfer, bank transfer or cheque recorded on a booking or owner invoice, or an insurer invoice; money out to an owner payout, a commission or referral partner payout, an expense or a refund sent by transfer.
3. **No match**: **Match** shows the records that fit (amount, and a date within a few days), nearest first: pick one. Nothing fits: record the payment, payout or expense first, then match. **Set aside** a bank fee or a transfer between CarmaCars accounts, saying what it is. **Undo** takes a reason.
4. A line with no match after two days is a To do for Finance and in the Finance morning email; matching it closes the To do. Every step is in the audit log.
