  '<p class="gd-p">Owner fee invoices are issued on the notice day and debited on the 15th. Invoices of any amount are made by hand, as drafts first. Statements are built, approved and issued each month, and payouts follow.</p><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-owner-invoices" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner invoices</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner money</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Invoices</b> tab. Every owner invoice, drafts and voids included. The same list is on each owner&#39;s and each application&#39;s Invoices tab.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Filter by Drafts, Open, Partly paid, Paid, Failed, In arrears or Void, or search by invoice number or owner. Open an invoice to see everything about it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">New invoice</b> makes an invoice of any amount for an owner&#39;s car, for example a registration fee of $123.45.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The monthly run and tracker invoices: <b class="gd-ui">Run the monthly invoices</b> issues the invoices for the 15th by hand, for a missed month (never twice); <b class="gd-ui">Issue all tracker invoices</b> bills the Tracker Install for each car waiting for its tracker.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/invoices</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1060"><img src="/guides/img/admin-14-owner-invoices-desktop-dc4ed1f1.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1060"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:83.3%;top:22.4%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:41.7%;top:35.7%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:29%;top:43.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-make-edit-and-issue-an-invoice" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Make, edit and issue an invoice</h2><p class="gd-p">A new invoice is a draft: the owner sees nothing and it is never debited until you issue it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the car, a title (for example Registration fee) and, if you like, the due date (empty: 7 days after it is issued). Each line: the description, the quantity, the unit amount to the cent, HST on or off, and a note. <b class="gd-ui">Add a line</b> for more.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Save as draft</b> to come back to it, or <b class="gd-ui">Save and issue</b> to send it now. On a draft&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Issue and email</b> sends it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Paid another way? Press <b class="gd-ui">Already paid outside the platform</b> on the invoice: choose how (e-Transfer, cash, cheque, bank transfer or card outside the platform), the date and the reference. A draft is issued without the invoice email first, the payment is recorded, and the owner gets no email unless you tick <b class="gd-ui">Email the owner a receipt</b>. To record a smaller or extra payment, press <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b>. The page lists the payments with their receipts, the automatic debits, the emails sent and the history.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Resend email</b> sends the invoice again. <b class="gd-ui">PDF</b> opens it as a PDF.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-correct-an-issued-invoice" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Correct an issued invoice</h2><p class="gd-p">An issued invoice is never edited. You void it and issue a corrected one.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Void</b>, write the reason (the owner reads it), keep Make a corrected invoice from it ticked, and press <b class="gd-ui">Void the invoice</b>. Its scheduled debit is cancelled and the owner is told.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The corrected invoice opens as a draft with the same lines. Fix the amounts and press <b class="gd-ui">Save and issue</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Already paid? Void the payment first, or press <b class="gd-ui">Credit note</b> for the amount to give back: it gets its own number and the owner sees it.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Invoices issued before October 20, 2026 at the old default (for example $904.00, or $1,017.00 when the Insurance Fee was $450.00) are not changed by themselves. Where an owner agreed another amount, void them and reissue at the agreed amount.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-the-automatic-debit" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The automatic debit</h2><p class="gd-p">The debit runs by itself. Your job is to watch for payments the bank sends back and owners with no bank debit set up.</p><ol class="gd-flow"><li><b>1</b><span>Notice day</span><em>Invoices issued, one notice per owner, 10 days before</em></li><li><b>2</b><span>Debit day</span><em>The 15th from 6:00: one debit per invoice</em></li><li><b>3</b><span>Cleared</span><em>The invoice is paid</em></li><li><b>4</b><span>Returned, insufficient funds</span><em>The Late Fee (5% of the unpaid insurance, plus HST) is added once; the same amount is tried again within 30 days</em></li><li><b>5</b><span>Returned for another reason</span><em>No retry and no Late Fee: the debit pauses and you get a task</em></li></ol><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The tiles show the next debit day and notice day, scheduled, processing, cleared and returned debits.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">How it runs explains the policy in words, read from Program settings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Scheduled and processing lists each debit. <b class="gd-ui">Pause</b> holds one (a reason is needed).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Owners lists each owner&#39;s bank debit. Use <b class="gd-ui">Pause</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Resume</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Send a notice now</b> or, with no bank debit set up, <b class="gd-ui">Send the sign-up link</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/debits</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/920"><img src="/guides/img/admin-15-owner-debits-desktop-f65f061a.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="920"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:21.8%;top:21.7%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:21.5%;top:35.5%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:91.5%;top:75.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:84.7%;top:94.7%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol" start="5"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Results: each debit, cleared or returned, with the bank&#39;s reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Run log: each notice and debit run, with its counts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Notices sent: who was told what, for which debit day.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/debits</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/520"><img src="/guides/img/admin-15-owner-debits-desktop-8d4682bc.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="520"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:11%;top:14.4%" aria-hidden="true">5</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:10.2%;top:52.3%" aria-hidden="true">6</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:15.4%;top:89.8%" aria-hidden="true">7</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">Insufficient funds: the Late Fee (5% of the unpaid insurance, plus HST; $50.00 on an invoice with no insurance) is added to that invoice once and collected with the owner&#39;s next debit, and the original amount is tried again within 30 days, as section 4.4 of the Enrollment Agreement sets out. The retry is never more than the original amount. Returned again: the invoice is in arrears and you get a task. Any debit missed (returned for another reason, too late to retry, or a retry still waiting) comes off the owner&#39;s next revenue statement by itself: when the statement is built, the invoice goes in arrears (a waiting retry is cancelled) and the statement deducts it. Nothing to do.</p><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Returned for any other reason (account closed, payment stopped, no authorization): there is no retry and no Late Fee. The owner&#39;s debit pauses, the owner gets an email asking them to fix the account or pay another way, and you get a task. A debit is never more than its notice said. An owner with no bank debit set up gets an email on the notice day and you get a task; nothing is debited for them.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-before-the-debit-day-the-debit-preview" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Before the debit day: the Debit preview</h2><p class="gd-p">The top of the Debits tab shows the coming debit day.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Debit preview</b> lists each owner with something to debit: the total, whether a bank debit is set up, whether the notice went, and each invoice in one line: the amount, the car, the fee (monthly fee, first and last month, tracker install, adjustment, late fee), the period and how it was worked out, such as &quot;prorated: 20 of 30 days&quot;. The line opens the invoice.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Something looks wrong? Press <b class="gd-ui">Hold</b> beside the owner and give the reason. Nothing is debited for that owner until you press <b class="gd-ui">Resume</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Fee check</b> compares the month&#39;s invoices with each car&#39;s signed terms: no monthly fee on a flat monthly payment, a Turo-Only car, a shareholder&#39;s car or a company car, nothing before the Enrollment Date, and the amount the terms give. It changes nothing: void and reissue an invoice that does not match. Each production deploy prints the same check.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-when-a-debit-can-t-go-ahead" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">When a debit can&#39;t go ahead</h2><p class="gd-p">You get one email: &quot;Can&#39;t collect $X from the owner: the reason&quot;. The reasons are the words of the owner guide: no bank debit set up, owner cancelled the debit at their bank, amount went up after the notice, the bank sent the payment back. The email lists each amount in one line and has one button that fixes it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Send the sign-up link</b> opens the Debits tab on that owner. Press <b class="gd-ui">Send the sign-up link</b> again there: the owner gets the email to set up their bank debit.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Send a new notice</b> opens the same place with <b class="gd-ui">Send a new notice</b> for the new amount.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Open the invoice</b> opens the invoice to record a payment made another way.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-owner-statements" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner statements</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner money</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Statements</b> tab</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Build all for a month</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Build one</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open each draft. Check it, <b class="gd-ui">Rebuild</b> after a correction, <b class="gd-ui">Preview PDF</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Issue to the owner</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Reissue</b> sends a corrected copy; <b class="gd-ui">CSV</b> exports it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/statements</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/400"><img src="/guides/img/admin-16-statements-desktop-43a313ea.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="400"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:79.9%;top:27.3%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/statements/2eedf660-50ce-4bd9-86d6-01bbe149c000</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/520"><img src="/guides/img/admin-17-statement-desktop-106ee57f.jpg" alt="An approved statement: the owner gets it by email with the PDF on the 10th, and payouts follow under Payouts." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="520"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:86%;top:22.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div><figcaption>An approved statement: the owner gets it by email with the PDF on the 10th, and payouts follow under Payouts.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-staff-commissions" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Staff commissions</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Company</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Commissions</b> tab. Nothing is paid automatically.</p><ol class="gd-flow"><li><b>1</b><span>Not earned yet</span><em>The rental is ahead, or not paid in full</em></li><li><b>2</b><span>Pending approval</span><em>Completed and paid in full; a Sales month once it has ended</em></li><li><b>3</b><span>Approved</span><em>You approved it; the staff member is told</em></li><li><b>4</b><span>Paid</span><em>You recorded the payment; the staff member is told</em></li><li><b>5</b><span>Reversed</span><em>Cancelled, refunded or charged back; after payment it comes off the next payment</em></li></ol><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">By person shows each staff member&#39;s month (Sales: rental days of 100 and the tier), what is not earned yet, pending approval, approved and paid.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> on a person (everything that may be approved now) or on one commission.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Record a payment</b>: choose how it was paid (e-Transfer, bank transfer, Wise, cash, the monthly pay statement or another way), the reference and the date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Prices to review</b> lists prices typed by hand; <b class="gd-ui">Sourcing claims</b> lists staff who say they sourced a website request; <b class="gd-ui">Payments made</b> lists each payment.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Owner requests</b> lists the commission each salesperson asks for an owner they brought in: a flat amount, or a percent of the company&#39;s share or of the cars&#39; rental revenue, for a number of months or for as long as the car is with us. Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Change and approve</b> (your terms, with a note) or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b>. Nothing accrues before you approve. A flat amount is earned at the owner&#39;s first paid rental, once; a percent on each paid rental of the owner&#39;s cars in the time approved. Each then comes to the list above for approval.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Who sourced an owner: the owner&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Sourced by</b>. Only an Admin changes it, with a reason. A waiting request of the person before is withdrawn; an approved one, with what it has not paid yet, goes to the new person.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">Commission</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sales</td><td>By rental days of the month: under 50 days 10%, from 50 days 15%, from 100 days 20%, on all that month&#39;s rentals</td></tr><tr><td>An owner a salesperson brought in</td><td>The request you approved. A CarmaCars expense, never deducted before Owner Revenue; none on CarmaCars&#39;, a partner&#39;s or a shareholder&#39;s cars</td></tr><tr><td>Field staff</td><td>10% (also the field referral fee). Customer service, Fleet and Finance staff get no sales credit or commission, ever: their help is credited as Helped by on the booking and on their scorecard</td></tr><tr><td>Base</td><td>The rental charge before tax, after discounts, with late extra days; never delivery, kilometres, add-ons or anything else bought. Only a refund of the rental charge comes off</td></tr><tr><td>On the owner statement</td><td>An owner&#39;s car: deducted with the kickbacks before Owner Revenue, its own line on the statement. A partner&#39;s car: from CarmaCars&#39; commission. A CarmaCars-owned car: a CarmaCars expense</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A commission that changes after an owner statement was built (a refund, or the month&#39;s Sales tier) goes on the owner&#39;s next statement as an adjustment line.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-field-pay" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Field pay</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Company</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Field pay</b> tab. Field staff clock in and out on their phones (My hours); you run the pay every two weeks. Nothing is paid automatically.</p><ol class="gd-flow"><li><b>1</b><span>Clocked in and out</span><em>Field staff press Clock in and Clock out; Fleet or you fix a forgotten clock-out</em></li><li><b>2</b><span>Pay run started</span><em>Hours times the hourly rate, plus the approved commissions</em></li><li><b>3</b><span>Approved</span><em>The figures are frozen, the period&#39;s hours are locked, the statements are numbered</em></li><li><b>4</b><span>Paid</span><em>You recorded how each person was paid; they get their statement by email</em></li></ol><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The tab <b class="gd-ui">Pay run</b> shows the current two-week period (Sunday to Saturday: the first day is Settings &gt; Program, Field pay). <b class="gd-ui">Earlier period</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Later period</b> move between periods.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">After the period ends, press <b class="gd-ui">Start the payroll</b>: one line for each person with hours times their hourly rate, plus the staff commissions and referral fees approved by the end of the period (see Staff commissions). <b class="gd-ui">Refresh the figures</b> takes in a change made since.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>. The period&#39;s hours are locked, each line gets a statement number and the figures are frozen. Someone still clocked in blocks it: fix their shift under <b class="gd-ui">Hours</b> first. <b class="gd-ui">Withdraw</b> takes an approved run back while no payment is recorded.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b> on a line: choose e-Transfer, bank transfer or cash, the reference (not needed for cash) and the date. The commissions in the line are marked paid and the person gets their pay statement by email (<b class="gd-ui">Send again</b> repeats it). The statement&#39;s number opens its PDF; <b class="gd-ui">CSV</b> gives the run for your accountant.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hours</b> lists everyone&#39;s shifts of the period. <b class="gd-ui">Add hours</b> enters a shift for someone who forgot to clock in, <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> fixes one and <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes one out. Each needs a reason and is kept in a log. Fleet does the same under Field hours but sees no pay.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hourly rates</b> shows each person&#39;s rate: CA$18.00 an hour unless you give them their own with <b class="gd-ui">Set the rate</b> (a reason is needed). A pay run keeps the rate it was started with.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">Field pay</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Overtime</td><td>Off. Settings &gt; Program, Field pay: pay overtime, after 44 hours in a week, at 150% of the rate</td></tr><tr><td>Vacation pay</td><td>Off. Settings &gt; Program, Field pay: vacation pay (Ontario: 4%) adds that share of wages, overtime and commissions to each statement</td></tr><tr><td>Deductions</td><td>None are worked out: income tax, CPP, EI and the employer&#39;s contributions are for your accountant. Each statement says so</td></tr><tr><td>Commissions that net to nothing</td><td>A person whose approved commissions add up to nothing or less (a clawback) is not paid them this period: they carry to the next</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A shift of more than 16 hours (a setting) is refused, and so are hours that overlap another shift of the same person. The field staff member sees their hours and statements under My hours on their phone.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-company-model" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Company model</h2><p class="gd-p">Money &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Company model</b> is the CarmaCars model workbook, live: the actuals, the forecast and the pro forma on one page. Admins only (not Finance). Never share it: investors have their own sheets in the investor portal.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Forecast</b>: the latest actual month, the EBITDA break-even month, the next 12 months&#39; EBITDA and the lowest cash, a chart of EBITDA and cash, and 36 months marked A (actual) or F (forecast): cars, utilization, revenue per rented day, revenue, costs, EBITDA, investor returns, tax and cash.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Actuals</b>: filled in by themselves every hour from the bookings, payments, payouts, expenses and investments. Rental earned is spread over each rental&#39;s days (before HST, insurer-billed and renter-billed apart, placeholders left out), with fees by kind, cash received by method, rentals and rented days, owner and partner shares, commissions, kickbacks, expenses by category and investor payouts. <b class="gd-ui">Refresh actuals now</b> recomputes them at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Pro forma 5 years</b>: each year&#39;s income statement, cash flow and key figures.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Assumptions</b>: growth, the utilization ramp, rates, monthly costs, hires, planned capital raises, the fleet insurance premium and tax. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the assumptions</b>; the forecast, the pro forma and the download use them at once. A field marked &quot;From the actuals&quot; left blank uses the latest complete month.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Download as Excel</b>: the full internal workbook with live formulas and the current actuals.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Enter the fleet insurance premium under Assumptions; until then it counts as $0 and profit is overstated. Enter each month&#39;s costs in Money &gt; Expenses: a cost line with nothing entered for an actual month uses the assumption, marked est.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-payroll-for-everyone-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Payroll for everyone (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Payroll</b> is one run every two weeks for the field staff (hours) and for customer service, Fleet and Finance (salary).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A salaried person is paid their monthly salary x 12 / 26, for the days they were employed in the period. The salary is their own (<b class="gd-ui">Set the salary</b>, with a reason), else the monthly pay they were hired at, else their role&#39;s (Program settings, va_salary_defaults), in US dollars unless set otherwise.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Finance prepares it: <b class="gd-ui">Start the payroll</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Add a bonus or deduction</b> with the reason, then <b class="gd-ui">Send for approval</b>. You get an alert.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">You press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Record all payments</b> (one method and reference; each stub number is added to it) or <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b> line by line. Each person gets their stub by email and in their portal.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A line marked <b class="gd-ui">Held</b> is for a Field, customer service, Fleet or Finance person who has not passed the whole academy: <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b> is not offered, and <b class="gd-ui">Record all payments</b> skips it and tells the person. It is never lost: the first <b class="gd-ui">Record all payments</b> after they pass, or after you waive their academy (with a reason), pays it in full and notes the release on the line. <b class="gd-ui">Commission held</b> beside <b class="gd-ui">To pay</b> means only the commission, bonuses and referral fees wait (for anyone mid-academy); a commission payout to them is refused with the reason. Program settings, <b class="gd-ui">Academy: hold pay for hours</b>, turns the hours part off.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Admin &gt; Team also has <b class="gd-ui">Schedules</b> (each role&#39;s days and hours, anyone&#39;s own, who is late today) and <b class="gd-ui">KPIs</b> (every staff member&#39;s KPIs for a week against the targets in Program settings).</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The townhall page: pick the craziest story, enter the week&#39;s social media figures, add the recording link, and mark anyone present or absent. Staff who miss two townhalls in a row are locked until you press <b class="gd-ui">Unlock</b> on the staff list.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Meetings, on the townhall page, lists the last eight townhalls and the next four. A townhall nobody attended is recorded as not held and counts nobody absent. <b class="gd-ui">This townhall did not happen</b> does the same for a past one (its absences and alerts are cleared, and a lockout it caused is lifted). <b class="gd-ui">Cancel this townhall</b> on an upcoming one sends no reminders for it; <b class="gd-ui">Put it back on</b> undoes that.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Each renter and lead shows an Intent card (hot, warm or cold, with the budget, car, length, dates, urgency, delivery and coverage they mentioned). The live map shows it on each pin. An AI reading fills the gaps within the free daily allowance only (Program settings, intent_ai_enabled).</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Investors see Search traction under the deck: Google clicks and impressions of the last 28 days, indexed pages and the weekly trend. Type the indexed pages from Search Console on the investor deck page under Investors (no API exists for it).</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-company-statements" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Company statements</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Company</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Monthly statements</b> tab: CarmaCars&#39; own monthly statement, in twelve sections.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the month. The tiles show revenue, fees, refunds, expenses and the company net.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Switch between Total, Per owner and Per vehicle.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Download <b class="gd-ui">PDF</b>, <b class="gd-ui">PDF by owner</b> or <b class="gd-ui">PDF by vehicle</b>, or press <b class="gd-ui">Email me the PDFs</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Finalize</b> freezes the month. <b class="gd-ui">Rebuild</b> works until then.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/reports</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/760"><img src="/guides/img/admin-18-company-statements-desktop-8e2738ed.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="760"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.8%;top:28%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.4%;top:59.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:77.1%;top:15.5%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:46.9%;top:15.5%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Fees taken from the revenue statement</h3><p class="gd-p">On an owner&#39;s page, the <b class="gd-ui">Fees</b> button sets <b class="gd-ui">How fees are paid</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Bank debit</b> (the default) or <b class="gd-ui">Take from revenue statement</b>. Taken from the statement, the owner&#39;s invoices (not the upfront one) are not debited: the next owner statement pays each one from the payout, as far as it goes, with the line &quot;Invoice INV-..., paid from statement&quot;. Approved, the invoice reads <b class="gd-ui">Paid from statement</b>, or part paid with the rest on the next statement. An invoice still owing 2 months after its billing date goes back to the bank debit after the usual notice, and you get the task <b class="gd-ui">Invoice ... back to the bank debit</b>.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">The flat-rate agreements</h3><p class="gd-p">An owner whose every car is on a flat monthly payment signs the <b class="gd-ui">Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement</b> instead of the standard one (the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement and Forms A to D are the same). The owner&#39;s page says which set applies. When the pay model changes, the signed Enrollment Agreement ends and the owner signs the new one in the owner portal; changed back before signing, the signed one is in force again. The lawyer approved the flat-rate set: Program settings &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Flat-rate agreements awaiting lawyer OK</b> is off, and is turned on only to mark a new text still under review. Owners can sign either way.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-how-it-s-paid-bank-debit-or-deducted-from-payouts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">How it&#39;s paid: bank debit or deducted from payouts</h2><p class="gd-p">Every owner invoice is paid one of two ways: <b class="gd-ui">Bank debit on the 15th</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Deduct from payouts</b> (taken from the owner&#39;s monthly payouts until paid, never debited).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On an invoice, <b class="gd-ui">How it&#39;s paid</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Change</b>. A draft changed to Deduct from payouts is issued without the debit email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each monthly statement deducts as much as the payout allows and shows it to the owner as a deduction; the rest waits for the next statement. The invoice screen shows what was deducted and what is left.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">For the first and last month, choose <b class="gd-ui">Deduct from payouts</b> on the Terms tab (or at approval).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On the Terms tab, <b class="gd-ui">Charge the agreed one-off fees</b> makes one invoice for a car from the one-off fees agreed on the owner&#39;s terms (all, or the ones you name), deducted from payouts or debited.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-referral-links-between-owners-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Referral links between owners (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">When one owner referred another, open the referrer&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Terms</b> tab, <b class="gd-ui">Referral links</b>, <b class="gd-ui">This owner referred another owner</b>: choose the owner referred and the share in basis points (1000 = 10 points of the revenue the management fee is taken from). Set the referred owner&#39;s own fee on their Terms as usual (for example a 40% management fee and $350 a month per car). Every statement of the referrer then has a <b class="gd-ui">Referral share</b> line per referred car; it is paid from CarmaCars&#39; share, never the referred owner&#39;s payout. With <b class="gd-ui">sees the cars</b> on, the referrer finds <b class="gd-ui">Cars you referred</b> in their owner portal: bookings, use and revenue, read only, without the other owner&#39;s details. <b class="gd-ui">End</b> stops the link; shares already earned are still paid.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-statement-periods-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Statement periods (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Statements run from the 8th of one month to the 7th of the next, and the payout on the 10th covers them. A rental that crosses the cutoff, or a long weekly or biweekly rental, is paid for the days inside each period, never twice. Each statement lists amounts still uncollected from the renter separately; they are paid on the statement after they are collected.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-the-owner-forecast-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The owner forecast (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">Each owner sees a <b class="gd-ui">Forecast</b> on their Home: the next 12 months of each car, projected occupancy and projected owner revenue (before fees). Open an owner in <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b>: the <b class="gd-ui">Overview</b> shows the same <b class="gd-ui">Forecast</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every car starts from the GTA seasonal curve: <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Owner forecast: the GTA seasonal curve</b> (a factor for each month, jan to dec, 1.00 is an average month) and <b class="gd-ui">Owner forecast: the occupancy of an average month</b> (60% by default). A month&#39;s curve is the average month times its factor.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Once a car has 3 full months on the program, its own occupancy is blended in: its own level (each month&#39;s occupancy divided by that month&#39;s factor) times the month&#39;s factor, weighted half after 3 months, two thirds after 6, four fifths after 12. The season always stays in.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Bookings hidden from the owner (an insurer replacement hidden from them, or one never shown), test bookings and the owner&#39;s own trips are not counted.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Projected owner revenue: occupancy times the days of the month times the car&#39;s owner revenue per booked day, from its own statements of the last 12 months, else its daily rate less the Revenue Share.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Every owner statement (the owner&#39;s page, yours and the PDF) has a <b class="gd-ui">Forecast</b> line: next month against the statement&#39;s month, higher or lower, by how many points and about how much owner revenue, and why (the season).</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Change a factor when the season moves (a big event, a new airport route): every owner&#39;s forecast follows on their next visit.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-owner-use-charges-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner-use charges (release 48)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The charges of a booking an owner makes of their own car (for themselves or for someone else) are billed to the owner by themselves: damage up to the deductible, tickets, tolls, fuel, kilometres, cleaning, smoking, a late return and the other fees. Add them as on any rental (the return, the Money tab); a fee that needs evidence waits for it, as always.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Nothing goes on a renter statement. About 15 minutes after a charge is ready it is put on an owner invoice titled &quot;Charges on your booking&quot;, issued and due the same day.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">It is collected in this order: the owner&#39;s card on file at once; with no card, a bank debit started the same day (not the 15th); with no method, or when the charge fails, the owner gets the invoice with the pay link and reminders every 2 days.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An invoice still unpaid after 7 days, or at the statement cut-off (the 7th) if that comes first, is deducted from the owner&#39;s next statement.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The owner gets an email and an alert at each step, listing each charge with its evidence. A failed charge also alerts Admins.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">The booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> tab shows <b class="gd-ui">Charges billed to the owner</b>: the charges waiting for evidence, and each invoice with what is open, how it is being collected and the day it would be deducted from the statement.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">The days are in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner-use charges and the Late Fee on unpaid insurance</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-late-fee-on-unpaid-insurance-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Late Fee on unpaid insurance (release 48)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">An owner&#39;s Late Fee on insurance is 5% of the unpaid insurance of the invoice (it was $50 per vehicle). It is added once, as its own line, when the debit of the 15th fails or the invoice is unpaid the day after its due date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The fee carries HST by default (it is a penalty, not insurance; insurance itself has none). Ask the accountant; the switch is in Program settings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The unpaid insurance and the fee are deducted from the owner&#39;s next statement by themselves, as two lines: the invoice, and &quot;Late Fee, invoice INV-n&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The owner is reminded 3 days before the due date and told when the fee is added. An invoice with no insurance on it keeps the flat Late Fee.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The updated owner agreement (4.4 and Schedule B) is published for owners to accept (it is listed with the other terms under Settings), without signing again.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-finance-dashboard-and-the-bank-release-49" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Finance dashboard and the bank (release 49)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Company</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Finance</b> (the first tab of Company; Finance has the same page under <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Finance</b>) is the money of the business on one page, read only: each figure opens the page where it is worked.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Cash position</b>: the bank balance from the latest RBC import, Stripe&#39;s balance (available and pending) and its payouts on the way, and <b class="gd-ui">Free cash</b>: all of that less the deposits held as cash, the owner payouts due, the refunds owed and the HST owed. An account whose balance is more than a week old is marked: import this week&#39;s download.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Money in</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Money out</b> for the month (Earlier month, Later month): rentals and charges taken, owner fees, insurers, tips (for the staff, never revenue); owner payouts due and paid on the 10th, commissions, expenses with HST and refunds.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Held for others</b>: deposits held as cash (owed back unless applied), deposit holds on cards (not money in the bank), what is kept back for claims and tolls, and refunds owed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">HST</b> for the quarter: collected (renters, owners, insurers) less paid (expenses, payouts to registered owners) is what is owed. An Insurance Fee never carries HST: a line that does is listed in red to correct.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Renter balances overdue</b> (past the statement&#39;s 7 days) and <b class="gd-ui">Insurer invoices unpaid</b> by age (0 to 30, 31 to 60, 61 to 90, over 90 days).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Twelve months</b>: money in, money out and net by month, beside the monthly statement&#39;s net where one is built.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Bank lines</b> is the reconciliation:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">In RBC online banking open the account, <b class="gd-ui">Download transactions</b>, CSV or OFX (OFX also has the balance), and drop the file on <b class="gd-ui">Import from RBC online banking</b>. The file stays on your computer; only its lines are saved, with the last four digits of the account. Importing the same days again adds nothing. With a CSV, type the balance shown in online banking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A line that fits exactly one record matches by itself: money in to a Stripe payout, an e-Transfer, bank transfer or cheque recorded on a booking or owner invoice, or an insurer invoice; money out to an owner payout, a commission or referral partner payout, an expense or a refund sent by transfer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">No match</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Match</b> shows the records that fit (amount, and a date within a few days), nearest first: pick one. Nothing fits: record the payment, payout or expense first, then match. <b class="gd-ui">Set aside</b> a bank fee or a transfer between CarmaCars accounts, saying what it is. <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> takes a reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A line with no match after two days is a To do for Finance and in the Finance morning email; matching it closes the To do. Every step is in the audit log.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'academy', 'chapter', 'demo-portals', 'Training for every staff function: paths of sections, lessons played and narrated in the browser (no video files are stored), and a quiz per section.

## Progress by staff member

1. Open **People** > **Academy**. Each staff member shows their paths, sections passed and the last quiz. Settings > Staff shows the same count in its Academy column.
2. Open a person: each section with lessons watched, best score, attempts and its state.
3. A section closed for them? Press **Open early**, give the reason and press **Open early** again. The reason is kept.

## Edit lessons and questions

1. Under Paths and sections, open a section. Changes apply at once for everyone.
2. **Edit the title** changes its name and what it covers.
3. Each lesson has **Preview** (the player) and **Edit the lesson**: the title and the scenes. A scene is a caption, the words the voice says, and its picture: a title, a chat between the renter and you, a list, steps, money rows or a rule; or a picture: a screen with numbered pins, a good and a bad photo side by side, a flow diagram, Do and Do not pairs or an icon list (each with its alt text). Every section ends with a lesson called **See it** of these pictures.
4. **Add a lesson**, **Delete** a lesson; each question has **Edit** (the question, the options, the right answer counted from 0, and why) and **Delete**; **Add a question** at the end. Every question also carries one funny wrong option (a joke, always wrong, never the right answer): it is added by itself when a question is saved, shows in the editor as "a joke, always wrong", and picking it scores nothing.

## The pass mark and the gate

- Settings > Program: Academy: pass mark of a quiz (80% by default).
- Academy gate (on by default): a section opens only once the one before it is passed, and a staff member who has not passed every path of their functions opens only the academy, the guide and their profile (and Welcome). Every staff account is held until it passes: new hires from one-step Hire from the start, and the staff already working from release 34; their progress so far is kept. Admins are never held. Off: the academy only records progress.
- Release 33 added a section at the end of each path on what changed in releases 28 to 32 (bookings, handovers and returns; licences, photos and agreements; money; cars and listings), with its quiz.
- Take the Admin path yourself from **Take the Admin path**.

## The gate, Welcome and waivers (release 34)

- A new hire signs in to **Welcome**: four steps in order (welcome, their profile and phone, the academy, then their first-day tasks). While they are held, Welcome, the academy, the guide and their profile are all they open; any other page brings them back to Welcome.
- Each person''s progress is on their academy page (Admin > Academy, their name) and on their candidate page in Hiring, on the card **Academy gate**: held or open, and the sections passed.
- **Waive the academy** on that card opens their portal at once without the academy. Give the reason: it is kept in the audit log. **Take the waiver back** holds them again until they pass.
- Release 34 added four sections, each with its quiz: pickups and returns (check-in is the pickup, Sign and pay, Book it now, overrides), money (Charge the renter, holds, owner invoices paid outside the platform), listing photos from a shared folder, and the caller panel with renter notes. Staff who already passed see the new sections on their academy page; they are not held by them.
- Each section names the guide chapters it was written from. When one of those chapters is published again, the section is listed under **To review: the guide changed** on Admin > Academy: check its lessons and quiz against the guide, then press **Mark reviewed**.

## The quiz rules (release 35)

- A quiz passes at 90% (Program settings). The questions come in a random order and open only after the section''s reading time.
- Under the pass mark, the person fixes the questions marked wrong once (they see which, not the right answers); that check is the try. After a failed try they wait 2 minutes, and may take a quiz 10 times a day. Answers given too fast are flagged to the Admins.
- An Admin can reset chosen sections for one person.
- New sections for a role are added to its path. Staff who had already passed their path keep a week before the new sections hold them, and nothing they passed is reset.

## The renter''s side and Ask the guide first (release 48)

- Every staff role, and the Admin path, has the new path **The renter''s side**: one section for each step of the renter guide, each scene showing the renter''s screen and opening that page of the guide (staff read it at `/staff/guide/renter`, you at **Guides** > Renter).
- Each role''s path has a section of worked examples from its own guide chapters (customer service, Sales, Fleet, Finance, field work, Admin), with the guide''s screenshots and a quiz drawn from the examples.
- New hires are enrolled on The renter''s side by one-step Hire like every path and pass it before their portal opens. Staff already working who had passed everything have 7 days, shown on their academy page, before the new sections hold them; nothing is reset.
- A lesson scene can show a guide screenshot: in **Edit the lesson**, the picture `shot` with the chapter (for example `renter/sign-and-pay`), the image file and a line.
- **Ask the guide first**: the Assistant panel in every staff portal names the guide chapter of the page. When a staff question is not answered by the guide, add the answer in **Settings** > **Guides**.

## Guide me

Every staff portal has **Guide me** at the top: it walks the person through a real workflow while they do it, on the live screens (send an offer, answer a request, record a payment, a pickup, a return and deposit review, approve an owner''s car, a field expense). It is off by default; each person can keep it on from its menu. You have it too.

**Academy**, **Guide me: walkthroughs in the live screens**: for the last 30 days, each staff member''s walkthroughs started, completed and stopped, and for each workflow the step people stop at most.
', 'Academy', 'Training paths by function: progress, opening a section early, editing lessons and questions, the gate.',
