**Academy**, **Guide me: walkthroughs in the live screens**: for the last 30 days, each staff member''s walkthroughs started, completed and stopped, and for each workflow the step people stop at most.

## The basics, payouts and stuck pages (release 50)

1. The basics are the first sections of each path (Sales in person 6, Sales remote 5; marked Basics). Passed, they open a salesperson''s portal, work and leads. Field, customer service, Fleet and Finance staff need the full academy before their portal opens (the owner, Nov 27): until then they reach only the academy and the onboarding pages (agreement, documents, pay details), and any other page sends them to the academy. A person''s page says how many sections are passed.
2. The whole academy is needed before held pay is paid out: commission, bonuses and referral fees for everyone, and pay for hours for Field, customer service, Fleet and Finance. Until then their payroll line is **Held** with the reason (or **Commission held**), and a commission payout is refused with it. The first pay run after the pass pays it in full; a waiver releases it too.
3. Stuck pages: When the **Stuck?** prompt opens for a staff member on a page, or the page fails for them 3 times in 30 minutes (Program settings, Stuck? errors), that page''s section is assigned to them: that part of the portal sends them to the section until they pass it. Their page in Academy lists it, with **Clear** (give the reason; it is kept in the audit log) when they do not need it; the same section is not given again for 7 days after a pass or a clear. Nothing is assigned while their staff agreement is unsigned, and the documents to sign, Welcome, the profile and the guide always open.
4. The audit of the quizzes removed the questions the lessons never taught and the ones repeated in a later section of the same path. **The renter''s side** is on the customer service path only.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Training for every staff function: paths of sections, lessons played and narrated in the browser (no video files are stored), and a quiz per section.</p><section class="gd-task" id="academy-progress-by-staff-member" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Progress by staff member</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Academy</b>. Each staff member shows their paths, sections passed and the last quiz. Settings &gt; Staff shows the same count in its Academy column.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open a person: each section with lessons watched, best score, attempts and its state.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A section closed for them? Press <b class="gd-ui">Open early</b>, give the reason and press <b class="gd-ui">Open early</b> again. The reason is kept.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="academy-edit-lessons-and-questions" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Edit lessons and questions</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Under Paths and sections, open a section. Changes apply at once for everyone.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Edit the title</b> changes its name and what it covers.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Each lesson has <b class="gd-ui">Preview</b> (the player) and <b class="gd-ui">Edit the lesson</b>: the title and the scenes. A scene is a caption, the words the voice says, and its picture: a title, a chat between the renter and you, a list, steps, money rows or a rule; or a picture: a screen with numbered pins, a good and a bad photo side by side, a flow diagram, Do and Do not pairs or an icon list (each with its alt text). Every section ends with a lesson called <b class="gd-ui">See it</b> of these pictures.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a lesson</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Delete</b> a lesson; each question has <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> (the question, the options, the right answer counted from 0, and why) and <b class="gd-ui">Delete</b>; <b class="gd-ui">Add a question</b> at the end. Every question also carries one funny wrong option (a joke, always wrong, never the right answer): it is added by itself when a question is saved, shows in the editor as &quot;a joke, always wrong&quot;, and picking it scores nothing.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="academy-the-pass-mark-and-the-gate" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The pass mark and the gate</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Settings &gt; Program: Academy: pass mark of a quiz (80% by default).</li><li>Academy gate (on by default): a section opens only once the one before it is passed, and a staff member who has not passed what their functions need (the full academy for Field, customer service, Fleet and Finance; the basics for Sales) opens only the academy and the onboarding pages: the guide, their profile and pay details, the documents to sign and Welcome. Every staff account is held until it passes: new hires from one-step Hire from the start, and the staff already working from release 34; their progress so far is kept. Admins are never held. Off: the academy only records progress.</li><li>Release 33 added a section at the end of each path on what changed in releases 28 to 32 (bookings, handovers and returns; licences, photos and agreements; money; cars and listings), with its quiz.</li><li>Take the Admin path yourself from <b class="gd-ui">Take the Admin path</b>. As an Admin you see every path there and can open any section, its lessons and its quiz, without passing the one before.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="academy-the-gate-welcome-and-waivers-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The gate, Welcome and waivers (release 34)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A new hire signs in to <b class="gd-ui">Welcome</b>: four steps in order (welcome, their profile and phone, the academy, then their first-day tasks). While they are held, Welcome, the academy, the guide and their profile are all they open; any other page brings them back to Welcome.</li><li>Each person&#39;s progress is on their academy page (Admin &gt; Academy, their name) and on their candidate page in Hiring, on the card <b class="gd-ui">Academy gate</b>: held or open, and the sections passed.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Waive the academy</b> on that card opens their portal at once without the academy. Give the reason: it is kept in the audit log. <b class="gd-ui">Take the waiver back</b> holds them again until they pass.</li><li>Release 34 added four sections, each with its quiz: pickups and returns (check-in is the pickup, Sign and pay, Book it now, overrides), money (Charge the renter, holds, owner invoices paid outside the platform), listing photos from a shared folder, and the caller panel with renter notes. Staff who already passed see the new sections on their academy page; they are not held by them.</li><li>Each section names the guide chapters it was written from. When one of those chapters is published again, the section is listed under <b class="gd-ui">To review: the guide changed</b> on Admin &gt; Academy: check its lessons and quiz against the guide, then press <b class="gd-ui">Mark reviewed</b>.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="academy-the-quiz-rules-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The quiz rules (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A quiz passes at 90% (Program settings). The questions come in a random order and open only after the section&#39;s reading time.</li><li>Under the pass mark, the person fixes the questions marked wrong once (they see which, not the right answers); that check is the try. After a failed try they wait 2 minutes, and may take a quiz 10 times a day. Answers given too fast are flagged to the Admins.</li><li>An Admin can reset chosen sections for one person.</li><li>New sections for a role are added to its path. Staff who had already passed their path keep a week before the new sections hold them, and nothing they passed is reset.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="academy-the-renter-s-side-and-ask-the-guide-first-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The renter&#39;s side and Ask the guide first (release 48)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Every staff role, and the Admin path, has the new path <b class="gd-ui">The renter&#39;s side</b>: one section for each step of the renter guide, each scene showing the renter&#39;s screen and opening that page of the guide (staff read it at <span class="gd-url">/staff/guide/renter</span>, you at <b class="gd-ui">Guides</b> &gt; Renter).</li><li>Each role&#39;s path has a section of worked examples from its own guide chapters (customer service, Sales, Fleet, Finance, field work, Admin), with the guide&#39;s screenshots and a quiz drawn from the examples.</li><li>New hires are enrolled on The renter&#39;s side by one-step Hire like every path and pass it before their portal opens. Staff already working who had passed everything have 7 days, shown on their academy page, before the new sections hold them; nothing is reset.</li><li>A lesson scene can show a guide screenshot: in <b class="gd-ui">Edit the lesson</b>, the picture <span class="gd-url">shot</span> with the chapter (for example <span class="gd-url">renter/sign-and-pay</span>), the image file and a line.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Ask the guide first</b>: the Assistant panel in every staff portal names the guide chapter of the page. When a staff question is not answered by the guide, add the answer in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Guides</b>.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="academy-guide-me" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Guide me</h2><p class="gd-p">Every staff portal has <b class="gd-ui">Guide me</b> at the top: it walks the person through a real workflow while they do it, on the live screens (send an offer, answer a request, record a payment, a pickup, a return and deposit review, approve an owner&#39;s car, a field expense). It is off by default; each person can keep it on from its menu. You have it too.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Academy</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Guide me: walkthroughs in the live screens</b>: for the last 30 days, each staff member&#39;s walkthroughs started, completed and stopped, and for each workflow the step people stop at most.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="academy-the-basics-payouts-and-stuck-pages-release-50" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The basics, payouts and stuck pages (release 50)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The basics are the first sections of each path (Sales in person 6, Sales remote 5; marked Basics). Passed, they open a salesperson&#39;s portal, work and leads. Field, customer service, Fleet and Finance staff need the full academy before their portal opens (the owner, Nov 27): until then they reach only the academy and the onboarding pages (agreement, documents, pay details), and any other page sends them to the academy. A person&#39;s page says how many sections are passed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The whole academy is needed before held pay is paid out: commission, bonuses and referral fees for everyone, and pay for hours for Field, customer service, Fleet and Finance. Until then their payroll line is <b class="gd-ui">Held</b> with the reason (or <b class="gd-ui">Commission held</b>), and a commission payout is refused with it. The first pay run after the pass pays it in full; a waiver releases it too.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Stuck pages: When the <b class="gd-ui">Stuck?</b> prompt opens for a staff member on a page, or the page fails for them 3 times in 30 minutes (Program settings, Stuck? errors), that page&#39;s section is assigned to them: that part of the portal sends them to the section until they pass it. Their page in Academy lists it, with <b class="gd-ui">Clear</b> (give the reason; it is kept in the audit log) when they do not need it; the same section is not given again for 7 days after a pass or a clear. Nothing is assigned while their staff agreement is unsigned, and the documents to sign, Welcome, the profile and the guide always open.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The audit of the quizzes removed the questions the lessons never taught and the ones repeated in a later section of the same path. <b class="gd-ui">The renter&#39;s side</b> is on the customer service path only.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'your-workday', 'chapter', 'start-here', 'Every function works the same way: start on To do, take the oldest task, finish it, and check Today for pickups and returns. The menu keeps your own work first, then the screens of your function in a few groups.

## The menu

Every office role has the same short menu: **To do** (your home; Today at a glance is its second tab; problems in your work that the nightly Data health check found show there too), at most five links for your role, the last one **More** for the rest of your work, **Bookings** (Bookings, Calendar, Find a car, Find a renter, Card coverage) and **Me** (My numbers: Scorecard and My sales; Academy). Actions are buttons on their page: **Send an offer** and **New quote** on Requests, **Add a rental** on Bookings. Bookings opens on Now for every role (Sales without the money or the renters'' phones). Your group is always open. On a phone the whole menu sits behind one Menu button.

A **More** page and a page with several parts open with a row on top (and a second row of tabs where a page has them). You see only the pages of your function.

| Function | Your links, then More |
| --- | --- |
| Customer service | Requests, Visitors (Live now, Chat, History), Messages. More customer service: Renters (Messages, Review requests, Leads), Owners (Owner and buyer leads, Owner pipeline, Owner forms), Listings (Listings, Similar cars), Chauffeur |
| Sales | Requests and offers, Visitors (Live now, Chat, History), Marketplace, My sales. More sales: Renters (Leads), Owners (Owner and buyer leads; your owners are on My sales), Chauffeur |
| Fleet | Field jobs, Fleet map, Checks (Daily checks, Photo reviews), Maintenance. More fleet: Field jobs (Jobs, Field hours), Listings (Listings, Similar cars, Calendar sync, Add-ons; Add a car for an owner is a button) |
| Finance | Money (To handle, By day, All payments, Refunds, Deposits, Reconciliation), Owner money (Invoices, Statements), Tolls and tickets, Turo trips. More finance: Maintenance and expenses |

## To do

Tasks come to your function on their own: new requests, renter replies, failed payments, toll notices and more. To do puts the most urgent first.

1. The top shows your function, today''s date, how many things need you, your open, overdue and done-today figures, and your quickest actions.
2. **Next up** is the one task to do now. Press its button to do it, or **Take it** to make it yours.
3. Your lanes group the work, for example Booking requests, Renter messages, Texts and calls, Live chat and Offers out. Each shows how many are waiting and how long the oldest has waited. Replies are timed against the 5-minute first reply target: past it the time turns red and says late. The most urgent lane comes first; press a lane to open it.
4. Customer service and Sales: **Waiting for a reply** lists every request, renter message, missed call and chat, the longest wait first, each with its reply button. Sales also sees the commission ring and Follow-ups due, Fleet today''s handovers, returns and moves and the cars right now, Finance Money today.
5. **Every open task**: filter All, Mine, Unassigned or Waiting. Under More filters: Any time, Overdue, Due today or Escalated, and by type. Each row has a priority, the task, its record, when it is due and a live timer of how long it has waited.
6. Press **Take it** to make it yours. Pressing the task opens the screen where it is done: a chat waiting for a person opens that chat, documents to check open the review, a request opens the booking. **Sheet** opens the step-by-step procedure.
7. Tasks close by themselves when their work is done elsewhere (an invoice paid or voided, a chat answered or closed); a day''s opening and closing checks close at the end of that day.
8. On a computer, press **/** to search (Find a renter; Sales: Find a car).

![](/guides/img/va-cs-01-queue-desktop-702d7c14.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 940; address: carmacars.ca/va; pins: 1 48.6 20.2, 2 31.9 52.1, 3 41.7 72.3")

## Work a task

Open the task. The buttons along the top move it on.

| Button | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| **Open the working screen** | Jumps to the booking, car or owner the task is about. |
| **Done** | You finished it. It leaves the queue. |
| **Waiting** | You are waiting on someone (a renter, an owner). It stays yours. |
| **Escalate** | It needs an Admin. Add why. |
| **Hand over** | Give it to someone else on the team. |
| **Add a note** | Leave a note for whoever looks next. |

> Tip: Work oldest due first. A task meets its target when it is done by its due time; that is what your scorecard counts.

## Today

1. Today lists pickups and returns, and what is due, for your function.
2. Press a booking number to open it. **To do** takes you back to your tasks.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-02-today-desktop-dfd277b7.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 700; address: carmacars.ca/va/today; pins: 1 22.9 24.6")

## Documents to sign

Your staff agreement, when CarmaCars sends it.

1. The queue shows "You have a document to sign". Press **Read and sign**.
2. Check the key values at the top (your role, hours, rate and start date), then press **Read the PDF** and read it.
3. Sign in a few steps: press **Send the code** and type the 6-digit code from your phone or email, tick that you read it, draw your initials beside the key terms (confidentiality, the rules on money, keys and cars, ending the agreement), tick the two consents and draw your signature.
4. Press **Sign**. Several documents? One signature covers all of them. The signed copy, with its certificate of completion, stays on the same page.

## Several functions? Switch with Working as

If you cover more than one function, **Working as** above the menu lists them: Customer service, Finance, Fleet and Sales. Choose one; the menu, To do and Today change to that function.

## Your scorecard

1. Open **Me** (the **Scorecard** tab).
2. By week shows each measure, its target and your result for each week.
3. A task meets its target when done by its due time. Daily checks count when done by 9:00 and 18:00.
4. The first reply target is 5 minutes: a new booking request, an enquiry, a change the renter asked for or a renter message is due 5 minutes after it comes in. An Admin sets it in Program settings, and the target column shows the one in force.

![](/guides/img/va-sales-05-scorecard-desktop-78ec1b03.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 360; address: carmacars.ca/va/scorecard; pins: 1 4.2 39.7, 2 62.5 58.3")

## Clock in and out

Customer service, Fleet and Finance: press **Clock in** on your home page when you start and **Clock out** when you stop. **My hours** shows today, the week and every entry. You are reminded if you have not clocked in 15 minutes after your start time.

## Breaks and activity (release 35)

Take breaks when you need them: there is no fixed length. Press **Start break** next to the clock (a reason is optional) and **End break** when you are back. The timer shows how long the break has run; after 30 minutes you get a reminder and the Admins see it. Clocking out ends a break. Your breaks are on **My hours**; only an Admin can change one, with the reason.

While you are clocked in and not on a break, the portal notes that you are active: a click, a key, a scroll or switching to its tab. It never records what you type, which pages you open or your screen. Keep the portal open in a tab while you work; a hidden tab nobody touches counts as inactive. After a few minutes without activity it asks **Still there?**: tap anywhere to carry on. Phone calls you take or make (your Quo user, the **Call** button or a note in the caller pop-up) and the townhall count as active. Nothing is counted outside your scheduled hours.

## Your first days

Your portal opens in order: your staff agreement first (sign it on Welcome or Documents to sign), then the academy, then everything else. Welcome shows each step and asks for the name you go by. Once both are done, Welcome and your home page show your WhatsApp groups (Sales: CARMA Closers and the CarmaCars Team; everyone else the Team group). Next to each link is your member tag, written for you as "Name - Position" (for example "Darren - Sales"), with **Copy member tag** and the steps: open the group, tap its name, tap your own name (or Edit member tag), paste and save. Join each group and set the tag, then press **I joined** and tick **I set my member tag**: I joined does not go through without it.

Passed the Sales part of the academy while Sales is not your main role? Your home page shows the Sales group (CARMA Closers) too: join it and set your tag the same way.

No progress in the academy for a day? You get a reminder on day 1, 2 and 4 (an alert and an email). After 5 days without using the portal the account is suspended.

## The weekly townhall

**Me** > **Townhall**: the weekly staff call''s deck, the next call time and its link. **Add to my calendar** adds the call every week.

## The weekly townhall (release 35)

Every Wednesday at 6:30 pm Toronto time, and everyone attends. Open **Townhall**: **Join the call** there, or **Check in** from 15 minutes before, counts you as there. You get a reminder an hour before.

## KPIs on your scorecard (release 35)

**KPIs by week** sits on **My scorecard**: your role''s KPIs against their targets (Program settings). Customer service: first reply within 5 minutes, conversations, licences reviewed, requests answered. Fleet: handovers on time, photo reviews, the next-day list, field jobs dispatched, calls. Finance: deposits reviewed in time, statements and invoices on time, tolls and tickets checked 2 to 3 times a week. A figure in red missed its target.

## Your schedule, hours and pay

**Hours** > **Schedule** shows your days and hours (Toronto) and who is working today. Breaks are at your discretion.

| Role | Schedule |
| --- | --- |
| Customer service | 6 days a week, 8:00 am to 6:00 pm, Tuesday off |
| Finance | Monday, Wednesday and Friday plus the 10th and the 15th of each month, 10:00 am to 7:00 pm; one extra day a week when there is overflow work |
| Fleet | 6 days a week, 11:00 am to 9:00 pm, Sunday off |

1. Clock in when you start and out when you stop. A clock-in more than 10 minutes after your start counts as late.
2. You are paid every two weeks: your monthly salary x 12 / 26. Your pay stubs are under **Hours** > **My hours**, each with its PDF, once an Admin approves the payroll.
3. Finance prepares the payroll under **Hours** > **Payroll**: start it once the period has ended, add any bonus or deduction with its reason, then **Send for approval**. An Admin approves it and records the payments; nothing is paid by itself.

## The townhall''s 30 minutes

The call link is at the top of your menu on every page. Press **Join now** (from 15 minutes before), then **Confirm I am in the call** on the Townhall page, or press **Check in**: either counts you as there. Cameras on. Something wild happened this week? **Tell yours** under Craziest story of the week: an Admin picks one for the deck. Each week''s recording is listed on the Townhall page.

> Watch out: Two townhalls missed in a row lock your account until an Admin restores it. A townhall that did not happen (nobody attended, or an Admin cancelled it) counts nobody absent, and a cancelled one sends no reminders.

## Breaks, quiet hours and the approval gate (release 35)

- Your portal opens after four steps: your staff agreement, the academy, the WhatsApp groups, then an Admin''s or a Fleet VA''s approval.
- Log a break from your home page when you step away, and end it when you are back. While you are on a break, on a call or in the townhall, the idle alert is paused. Otherwise, a long time with no activity on your shift sends you an alert, then the Admins.
- Quiet hours: alerts held by your quiet hours arrive as one summary when they end. Renters get no automatic text at night; an answer asked for then arrives in the morning.
- Your schedule, pay stubs (every two weeks) and KPIs are on your home page and My hours. The townhall is every Wednesday at 6:30 pm Toronto time; two missed in a row lock your account.

## The weekly townhall card (release 41)

From the day before the weekly townhall until it ends, your home page shows the **Townhall** card: the day and time (Toronto), a countdown, **Join / check in** (it opens 15 minutes before; joining through it checks you in), **Add to calendar**, and a red line if you missed the last townhall: one more miss locks your account. You also get a reminder the day before at 10:00 am, the morning of at 9:00 am, an hour before, and 15 minutes before with the join link.

## The townhall call in the site (release 50)

The weekly townhall is a video call inside the portal: no outside link to open. An email brings you the calendar invite once (it repeats every week, Toronto time) and updates it by itself when the day or time changes. From 15 minutes before, press **Join the call** on **Townhall** or on the Townhall card, allow your camera and microphone, then **Join the call** again. Being in the call counts your attendance by itself: the time you joined and left is recorded.

- **Mute**, **Camera off** and **Leave** are under the video; **Share screen** on a computer.
- **Slides** beside the video follow the presenter. **Previous** and **Next** let you look on your own; **Back to the presenter** catches up.
- **Raise hand** to speak, **Chat** to write to everyone (not kept after the call).
- If the call in the site is down, an Admin switches the townhall to the outside link and **Join the call** opens that instead.', 'Your workday', 'The menu, To do, task actions, Today, switching functions and your scorecard.',
