1. On the job, press **Sign now on this device**. It shows who still has to sign and whether their licence is on file.
2. Check the person: the name matches their licence, and you saw the original licence. Tick both. No licence on file? Press **Photograph: Licence, front** (and the back and the selfie).
3. Press **Hand the device to** and their name. They read the agreements (CarmaCars'' and Blind Spot''s), tick the statements and sign with their name or their finger.
4. They hand the phone back: press **Back to the staff view**. The signature record says it was signed in person, collected by you, on your phone.

## The agreements at check-in

Both rental agreements follow the check-in.

1. Signing at pickup? Record the odometer and the fuel on the check-in first, then hand over the device: the agreement then shows the time, kilometres and fuel out, and the signed copy holds them.
2. The signer gets a code on their phone, initials the key terms, ticks the consents and draws their signature.
3. Already signed online? When you complete the check-in, the "as picked up" copy of both agreements is made with your readings and your countersignature, and emailed to the renter.
4. The check-in stops if the agreement is missing something a claim needs (a licence expiry, a VIN). Ask the office to fill it on the booking, or an Admin to override.

## The deposit on your phone

Deposit not taken yet? The ready check shows how to take it under the Deposit line. You never type a card number.

1. Press **Card hold: hand this phone to the renter**. They type their credit card in Stripe''s secure form and press the button with the amount.
2. They see "Hold placed": take the phone back and press **Back to the job**. The ready check shows the deposit taken.
3. A rental longer than the hold limit shows **Save the card on this phone (long rental)** instead: Finance charges the deposit to that card.
4. No credit card? When CarmaCars allows it, the renter pays the deposit by e-Transfer or in cash: record it under the Deposit line.

## Add-ons to put in the car

A booking may come with add-ons: a baby seat, a child or booster seat, flowers, an umbrella, a phone charger or a prepaid full tank.

1. Open the job. Under Put in the car you see each add-on, how many, and what to do (for example "Put the bouquet on the front passenger seat").
2. Put every item in the car before the handover. The screen lists them again under the readings.
3. Prepaid fuel: the renter may return the car at any fuel level. Do not charge for fuel at the return.
4. A chauffeur on the booking: Fleet tells you who drives and when.

> Tip: An item missing? Write it under **Add a note for Fleet** and call the office before the handover.

> Tip: The photo count shows "19 of 19 photos taken · all uploaded" when the set is complete. The first photo must show the plate. Open circles on the damage diagram were recorded before; add only what is new.

## On one screen (release 28)

On the booking page the check-in is one screen: the time, km, fuel, and many photos picked at once from the camera roll, with the suggested angles as a checklist. If the renter checked in themselves, add your photos to theirs. It is under **Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)**; the button above it opens the one-screen handover described here.

## When a check stops the handover (release 33)
When something stops the pickup or the return (the deposit, a signature, the licence, the car''s status) and the trip must go ahead, the job shows **What stops the pickup now** with each check. Press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin approves in one tap and the handover is recorded with the time you entered; add the photos and readings afterwards on the job, as with any handover recorded now.

## Picked up, deposit pending (release 48)
When the renter cannot place the deposit hold at the pickup (the card is declined, the bank wants a call) and the car must go, you can let it go with the deposit owed. On the job, under the deposit line, open **Let the car go with the deposit owed**, say why, and go on with the check-in. On a booking, **Record the pickup now** has the box **Deposit not taken yet: let the car go owing it, because**, and the check-in panel has **Deposit not taken: let the car go owing it**. The booking then shows **Deposit pending $X** everywhere. Each morning the renter''s saved card is tried once; if that fails, the renter gets the deposit link by text (or email). After 48 hours an Admin gets a To do. You do nothing more: once the deposit is taken the chip changes by itself.

## Add old photos (photos still on your phone)
Photos of an earlier check-in or check-out that did not upload at the time can still go on the booking, even a booking you did not handle. On **Today**, press **Add old photos** at the bottom (it is also under the missing check-ins card). Every booking picked up or returned in the last 60 days is there, newest first.

1. Search by the plate, the car, the renter or the booking number, and tap the booking.
2. Tap **Check-in** or **Check-out**.
3. Tap the dashed box (Choose check-in photos, or check-out photos) and pick every photo of it from the camera roll at once. HEIC is fine.
4. They upload in the background with a bar for all of them. You can keep working. On a bad signal a photo waits and tries again by itself; it is never added twice. A photo that is refused shows why, with **Try again**.

A pile of photos from many bookings: tap **A pile of photos**, then **Choose all the photos**. The photos are grouped by the time they were taken, the plate is read where it can be, and each group shows the check-in or check-out it most likely belongs to. Check it and tap the red Add button of that group; if it is wrong, pick another under **Not this one?**.

> Good to know: Each photo keeps the time it was taken and shows on the photo report as "added later by" you. The renter and the owner are not told. The odometer and fuel of that check-in or check-out are still added on the job, as before.',
  '<p class="gd-p">You give the renter the keys only after every check passes. The whole handover is one screen: each part has a green tick once it is done, and the button at the bottom says what is still needed.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The job&#39;s header shows how much of the rental walkthrough the renter has read, for example &quot;Renter&#39;s walkthrough: read 2 of 6 steps&quot;. Below 6, walk them through the rest at the car: what to bring, the walk-around, the road rules and the return.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Finish the handover in the app, to the last step. Until the pickup is recorded the renter&#39;s messages and the office&#39;s records are guesses: 30 minutes after the pickup time you get an alert and a text to record it, or to mark a no-show.</div></aside><section class="gd-task" id="a-handover-before-you-start-the-ready-check" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Before you start: the ready check</h2><p class="gd-p">The first part lists what must be done before the car can go: signed, paid, ID checked, deposit. When everything is ready it is one green line; open <b class="gd-ui">The six checks</b> to see them.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--side"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each line should show a green tick: agreement signed, identity verified, coverage confirmed, additional drivers accepted, the booking holds the calendar, deposit taken.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A red line shows what you can do about it right under it (see the next part). Fix it, then press <b class="gd-ui">Check again</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">All green? Go on down the screen.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Coverage or the calendar not ready? Only the office fixes those: call CarmaCars. Still not ready? Press <b class="gd-ui">Stop: do not release the car</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/410"><img src="/guides/img/field-21-handover-01-ready-phone-ecb54c56.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="410"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:91%;top:63.4%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Never hand over keys if the ready check fails, the renter does not match the photo on file, or they do not have their original licence or the card on file. Stop and call us.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="a-handover-fix-the-ready-check-on-the-spot" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fix the ready check on the spot</h2><p class="gd-p">Most red lines are fixed on your phone, without calling the office. Everything you do is recorded with your name.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Agreement not signed: press <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b> and hand the phone to the renter. A copy signed on paper is not accepted.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Identity not verified: for each driver, press <b class="gd-ui">Take</b> for the licence front, the back and the selfie. Hold the original licence: tick that the name matches, the photo is the person, it is valid past the return and it is class G2 or G. No expiry on file? Type the licence number and the expiry. Press <b class="gd-ui">The licence checks out</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Deposit not taken: press <b class="gd-ui">Card hold: hand this phone to the renter</b>. They type their card in Stripe&#39;s secure form; take the phone back and press <b class="gd-ui">Back to the job</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Paid by e-Transfer instead: open <b class="gd-ui">Paid by e-Transfer</b>, type the reference number from their confirmation and press <b class="gd-ui">Record the e-Transfer</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Paid in cash: open <b class="gd-ui">Paid in cash</b>, count the amount in front of the renter and press <b class="gd-ui">I received</b>. Keep the cash apart from your own money and hand it to CarmaCars within 1 business day, as Finance directs: Finance gets a task to collect it from you.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Additional driver not accepted: press <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device (additional driver)</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>An expired licence, a face that does not match or a renter who will not sign: do not fix it. Press Stop and call us.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="a-handover-the-handover-on-one-screen" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The handover, on one screen</h2><p class="gd-p">With the car already? On the job, <b class="gd-ui">Start the check-in now</b> acknowledges, starts and opens the screen in one tap.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Renter, licence and card</b>: three taps. This is the renter named on the booking; you checked the original licence (name, photo, not expired; a photo of a licence is not enough); you saw the physical card with the same last four digits. Under the licence tick, <b class="gd-ui">Check it is the renter</b> is an optional step: take a photo of the licence the person is holding (and the back, if you like) and press <b class="gd-ui">Check now</b>. It is compared with the licence and selfie on the booking, which you open beside it with <b class="gd-ui">View</b>, and each line (name, licence number, expiry, face) says Matches, Does not match or Could not tell. <b class="gd-ui">Show the card used to pay</b> lists the card on file and the name on the booking: look at the card and answer Yes or No for its last four digits and its name. Never photograph the card or write its number down. A mismatch tells Fleet and Admin at once (&quot;Possible wrong person at pickup&quot;). The step never stops the handover by itself: when you should not hand over the keys, use <b class="gd-ui">Something is wrong</b>. Something is wrong? Open <b class="gd-ui">Something is wrong</b> and press what it is: the handover stops and the office is told.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Odometer, fuel and keys</b>: already filled in when the car reports them (from the Tracker, else from its last report). Check each against the dash and change what differs. Fuel: tap the level on the gauge, in eighths from E to F. Keys: <b class="gd-ui">+</b> and <b class="gd-ui">−</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Photos</b>: 19 photos, one tap each. <b class="gd-ui">Take this photo</b> always shows the next angle; <b class="gd-ui">All 19 photos</b> lists them, with <b class="gd-ui">Retake</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Damage</b>: nothing new? Leave it. New damage: open it, tap the car diagram where it is, choose Where and Type, press <b class="gd-ui">Add the damage</b> and take the close-up.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Tracker</b>: one green line when it reports. If not, <b class="gd-ui">Check again</b>. The car has to go anyway? Open <b class="gd-ui">The car has to go anyway?</b>, say why and press <b class="gd-ui">Release without the tracker</b>: an Admin is told at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Review and sign</b>: the renter reads the summary and signs, then you. <b class="gd-ui">Use this signature</b> for each.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Hand over the keys</b>. You see &quot;Checked in. The rental has started.&quot; The renter gets the photo report by email and in their Documents.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Not everything in yet? The button above it says what is next (for example &quot;Next: Odometer&quot;) and takes you there. A note for Fleet (anything missing or not clean) is under <b class="gd-ui">Add a note for Fleet</b>.</p><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/350"><img src="/guides/img/field-29-handover-09-photos-phone-767ecd4f.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="350"></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>You were interrupted? Open the job again: your answers and photos are where you left them.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Photos wait on the phone without a connection and upload by themselves when it returns; the count shows what is still uploading. Each photo keeps its time, and the place when your phone allows location. No signal on a step? It says &quot;Answers kept on this phone&quot; and you can go on: press Try again, or they are sent when the signal returns.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="a-handover-sign-now-on-this-device" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sign now on this device</h2><p class="gd-p">The renter (or an additional driver) has not signed the rental agreement yet? They sign on your phone.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the job, press <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b>. It shows who still has to sign and whether their licence is on file.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Check the person: the name matches their licence, and you saw the original licence. Tick both. No licence on file? Press <b class="gd-ui">Photograph: Licence, front</b> (and the back and the selfie).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Hand the device to</b> and their name. They read the agreements (CarmaCars&#39; and Blind Spot&#39;s), tick the statements and sign with their name or their finger.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">They hand the phone back: press <b class="gd-ui">Back to the staff view</b>. The signature record says it was signed in person, collected by you, on your phone.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="a-handover-the-agreements-at-check-in" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The agreements at check-in</h2><p class="gd-p">Both rental agreements follow the check-in.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Signing at pickup? Record the odometer and the fuel on the check-in first, then hand over the device: the agreement then shows the time, kilometres and fuel out, and the signed copy holds them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The signer gets a code on their phone, initials the key terms, ticks the consents and draws their signature.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Already signed online? When you complete the check-in, the &quot;as picked up&quot; copy of both agreements is made with your readings and your countersignature, and emailed to the renter.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The check-in stops if the agreement is missing something a claim needs (a licence expiry, a VIN). Ask the office to fill it on the booking, or an Admin to override.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="a-handover-the-deposit-on-your-phone" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The deposit on your phone</h2><p class="gd-p">Deposit not taken yet? The ready check shows how to take it under the Deposit line. You never type a card number.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Card hold: hand this phone to the renter</b>. They type their credit card in Stripe&#39;s secure form and press the button with the amount.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">They see &quot;Hold placed&quot;: take the phone back and press <b class="gd-ui">Back to the job</b>. The ready check shows the deposit taken.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A rental longer than the hold limit shows <b class="gd-ui">Save the card on this phone (long rental)</b> instead: Finance charges the deposit to that card.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">No credit card? When CarmaCars allows it, the renter pays the deposit by e-Transfer or in cash: record it under the Deposit line.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="a-handover-add-ons-to-put-in-the-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add-ons to put in the car</h2><p class="gd-p">A booking may come with add-ons: a baby seat, a child or booster seat, flowers, an umbrella, a phone charger or a prepaid full tank.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the job. Under Put in the car you see each add-on, how many, and what to do (for example &quot;Put the bouquet on the front passenger seat&quot;).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t