Admin approves in one tap and the handover is recorded with the time you entered; add the photos and readings afterwards on the job, as with any handover recorded now.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="a-handover-picked-up-deposit-pending-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Picked up, deposit pending (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">When the renter cannot place the deposit hold at the pickup (the card is declined, the bank wants a call) and the car must go, you can let it go with the deposit owed. On the job, under the deposit line, open <b class="gd-ui">Let the car go with the deposit owed</b>, say why, and go on with the check-in. On a booking, <b class="gd-ui">Record the pickup now</b> has the box <b class="gd-ui">Deposit not taken yet: let the car go owing it, because</b>, and the check-in panel has <b class="gd-ui">Deposit not taken: let the car go owing it</b>. The booking then shows <b class="gd-ui">Deposit pending $X</b> everywhere. Each morning the renter&#39;s saved card is tried once; if that fails, the renter gets the deposit link by text (or email). After 48 hours an Admin gets a To do. You do nothing more: once the deposit is taken the chip changes by itself.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="a-handover-add-old-photos-photos-still-on-your-phone" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add old photos (photos still on your phone)</h2><p class="gd-p">Photos of an earlier check-in or check-out that did not upload at the time can still go on the booking, even a booking you did not handle. On <b class="gd-ui">Today</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">Add old photos</b> at the bottom (it is also under the missing check-ins card). Every booking picked up or returned in the last 60 days is there, newest first.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Search by the plate, the car, the renter or the booking number, and tap the booking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Tap <b class="gd-ui">Check-in</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Check-out</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Tap the dashed box (Choose check-in photos, or check-out photos) and pick every photo of it from the camera roll at once. HEIC is fine.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">They upload in the background with a bar for all of them. You can keep working. On a bad signal a photo waits and tries again by itself; it is never added twice. A photo that is refused shows why, with <b class="gd-ui">Try again</b>.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">A pile of photos from many bookings: tap <b class="gd-ui">A pile of photos</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Choose all the photos</b>. The photos are grouped by the time they were taken, the plate is read where it can be, and each group shows the check-in or check-out it most likely belongs to. Check it and tap the red Add button of that group; if it is wrong, pick another under <b class="gd-ui">Not this one?</b>.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Each photo keeps the time it was taken and shows on the photo report as &quot;added later by&quot; you. The renter and the owner are not told. The odometer and fuel of that check-in or check-out are still added on the job, as before.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('field', 'my-hours-and-pay', 'chapter', 'photo-shoots', 'Jobs are put on shifts: claim a shift and its jobs are yours. Your hours are paid every two weeks at your hourly rate (CA$18.00 an hour unless your agreement says another rate), with the commissions an Admin has approved.

## My shifts

Shifts are published by themselves, up to 14 days ahead: one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 every second day, and a shift of its own for a handover or return no shift covers. Fleet may add or cancel shifts too.

1. **Free to claim**: shifts someone gave up (first to claim takes it) and open shifts. Each shows the jobs already on it, for example "On it: 3 pickups, 1 return, 2 cleans". Press **Claim this shift**: its jobs are yours on **Today** and here. You can claim once you passed the academy.
2. **Coming up**: your shifts, each with the shift''s jobs and the work planned for you. It updates as bookings come in. Sharing a shift? Its jobs are split between you, least busy first; the others'' show on **Today** under **Also on your shift**, and **Take it** takes one.
3. Cannot work one? Press **Give this shift up** and say why. It is offered at once to everyone free then, and its jobs go with it to whoever claims it. Under 24 hours before the start it is marked late on your record.
4. **Swap with someone**: choose their shift and press **Ask for the swap**. They press **Accept the swap** or **Decline**. Each of you takes the other shift''s jobs.
5. **Past shifts**: each day with your hours, the jobs, the photos and the money you spent.
6. **Money you spent**: each one with where it stands. No receipt yet? Take the photo and press **Add the receipt**.


### Your shifts in Google Calendar

On **My shifts** (and on **Profile**), **Add my shifts and townhalls to Google Calendar** gives you a private link with the shifts you claimed, the tasks given to you and the weekly townhall. Press **Make my calendar link**, then **Add to Google Calendar** and **Add** in Google. New and changed shifts show by themselves; Google refreshes every few hours. Keep the link to yourself: **Regenerate link** stops the old one.

## Clock in and out

Clock in and out on **Today**, with your shift. Forgot to clock out, or a time is wrong? Tell Fleet: they fix it, say why, and the change is written in a log.

## Pay details

Before your first pay, **My pay** asks for your pay details: your full legal name, email, phone, SIN and a photo of a void cheque. Press **Save my pay details**. Your SIN is kept encrypted: only Finance and Admin can see it, every look is recorded, and you see only its last 3 digits. How you are paid (bank, e-Transfer) is just below.

## Your pay and your pay statements

A pay period is two weeks, Sunday to Saturday. An Admin runs the pay after it ends.

1. The pay is your hours times your hourly rate, plus the commissions and referral fees an Admin approved by the end of the period (see Commissions). Overtime and vacation pay are added only if CarmaCars has switched them on.
2. An Admin approves the pay run, pays you (by e-Transfer, bank transfer or cash) and records it. You get an email with the amount and how you were paid.
3. Under Pay statements on **My pay**, press **PDF** for the statement of a period: your hours day by day, the amounts, the commissions in it and how it was paid.

> Tip: A pay statement shows no income tax, CPP or EI. They are not worked out in the portal: for your tax slips, ask CarmaCars or your accountant.

## Where you clock in and out

The phone asks for your location once when you clock in and once when you clock out, and never in between. Allow it. If it is off, or you are more than 500 m from the lot, you can still clock in or out: write why in the box that appears, and Fleet sees it.

## Availability, standing shifts and the minimum (release 35)

1. Set when you can work (mornings, afternoons and evenings for each weekday, plus a note) on Welcome; change it later on My shifts or Profile.
2. My shifts opens as a week calendar: tap a shift to claim it. The cards are on the List tab.
3. A standing weekly shift, such as every Saturday 10 to 6, claims each matching published shift by itself up to two weeks ahead. Drop one date (the give-up rules apply) or end it.
4. Hold at least the minimum (2 shifts in 7 days by default). Under it, you get a daily reminder and a To do.
5. Pay stubs come every two weeks under My pay, with a PDF and an email once paid.

## Your tips

**My pay** shows **My tips**: your half of each tip on a car you handed over (all of it when you also sold the rental). A tip given to you in cash: tell the office, they record it on the booking''s Money tab.

## Shift claims when you also do Sales (release 50)

When you also work in Sales, a shift you claim waits for an Admin: My shifts lists it under **Shift claims** as waiting. It is yours once approved; if it is denied, you see why. You get an alert either way.
', 'My shifts and My pay', 'Claim, give up and swap shifts, what you did on each, your hours, pay statements and pay details.',
  'Jobs are put on shifts: claim a shift and its jobs are yours. Your hours are paid every two weeks at your hourly rate (CA$18.00 an hour unless your agreement says another rate), with the commissions an Admin has approved.

## My shifts

Shifts are published by themselves, up to 14 days ahead: one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 every second day, and a shift of its own for a handover or return no shift covers. Fleet may add or cancel shifts too.

1. **Free to claim**: shifts someone gave up (first to claim takes it) and open shifts. Each shows the jobs already on it, for example "On it: 3 pickups, 1 return, 2 cleans". Press **Claim this shift**: its jobs are yours on **Today** and here. You can claim once you passed the academy.
2. **Coming up**: your shifts, each with the shift''s jobs and the work planned for you. It updates as bookings come in. Sharing a shift? Its jobs are split between you, least busy first; the others'' show on **Today** under **Also today**, and **Take it** takes one.
3. Cannot work one? Press **Give this shift up** and say why. It is offered at once to everyone free then, and its jobs go with it to whoever claims it. Under 24 hours before the start it is marked late on your record.
4. **Swap with someone**: choose their shift and press **Ask for the swap**. They press **Accept the swap** or **Decline**. Each of you takes the other shift''s jobs.
5. **Past shifts**: each day with your hours, the jobs, the photos and the money you spent.
6. **Money you spent**: each one with where it stands. No receipt yet? Take the photo and press **Add the receipt**.


### Your shifts in Google Calendar

On **My shifts** (and on **Profile**), **Add my shifts and townhalls to Google Calendar** gives you a private link with the shifts you claimed, the tasks given to you and the weekly townhall. Press **Make my calendar link**, then **Add to Google Calendar** and **Add** in Google. New and changed shifts show by themselves; Google refreshes every few hours. Keep the link to yourself: **Regenerate link** stops the old one.

## Clock in and out

Clock in and out on **Today**, with your shift. Forgot to clock out, or a time is wrong? Tell Fleet: they fix it, say why, and the change is written in a log.

## Pay details

Before your first pay, **My pay** asks for your pay details: your full legal name, email, phone, SIN and a photo of a void cheque. Press **Save my pay details**. Your SIN is kept encrypted: only Finance and Admin can see it, every look is recorded, and you see only its last 3 digits. How you are paid (bank, e-Transfer) is just below.

## Your pay and your pay statements

A pay period is two weeks, Sunday to Saturday. An Admin runs the pay after it ends.

1. The pay is your hours times your hourly rate, plus the commissions and referral fees an Admin approved by the end of the period (see Commissions). Overtime and vacation pay are added only if CarmaCars has switched them on.
2. An Admin approves the pay run, pays you (by e-Transfer, bank transfer or cash) and records it. You get an email with the amount and how you were paid.
3. A stub marked **Held** waits for the academy: your pay for hours and any commission are paid once you finish every section of your path (not only the basics). Nothing is lost: the first pay run after you pass pays it in full. The line says how many sections are passed.
4. Under Pay statements on **My pay**, press **PDF** for the statement of a period: your hours day by day, the amounts, the commissions in it and how it was paid.

> Tip: A pay statement shows no income tax, CPP or EI. They are not worked out in the portal: for your tax slips, ask CarmaCars or your accountant.

## Where you clock in and out

The phone asks for your location once when you clock in and once when you clock out, and never in between. Allow it. If it is off, or you are more than 500 m from the lot, you can still clock in or out: write why in the box that appears, and Fleet sees it.

## Availability, standing shifts and the minimum (release 35)

1. Set when you can work (mornings, afternoons and evenings for each weekday, plus a note) on Welcome; change it later on My shifts or Profile.
2. My shifts opens as a week calendar: tap a shift to claim it. The cards are on the List tab.
3. A standing weekly shift, such as every Saturday 10 to 6, claims each matching published shift by itself up to two weeks ahead. Drop one date (the give-up rules apply) or end it.
4. Hold at least the minimum (2 shifts in 7 days by default). Under it, you get a daily reminder and a To do.
5. Pay stubs come every two weeks under My pay, with a PDF and an email once paid.

## Your tips

**My pay** shows **My tips**: your half of each tip on a car you handed over (all of it when you also sold the rental). A tip given to you in cash: tell the office, they record it on the booking''s Money tab.

## Shift claims when you also do Sales (release 50)

When you also work in Sales, a shift you claim waits for an Admin: My shifts lists it under **Shift claims** as waiting. It is yours once approved; if it is denied, you see why. You get an alert either way.

## Shifts paused: the work still comes to you (release 50)

New shifts are not published by themselves for now. The shifts already claimed stay, with their jobs.

1. On a shift day, **Today** lists your work, then **Also today**: every other pickup and return of the day, whoever has it (or nobody yet). **Take it** takes one onto your shift.
2. **Before the next shift** lists the pickups and returns until the next shift''s day: prep those cars now (clean, fuel, photos).
3. A day with pickups or returns and no shift: a pickup goes on the shift before it, a return on the shift after it.
4. Work not done when your shift ends moves to the next shift by itself.
',
